VALUES
	(1,1,'Expected number of attendees','fire','gathering','Fires',NULL,0,'fires-gift-image-v3-(2).jpg','https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/3tew72r/','A Wild at Heart Fire is an authentic, monthly gathering where men experience God through the stories of other men.  \r\n\r\nAll around a fire.','easy, no requisite',1,'men','fires','Wild at Heart Fires: A Sanctuary of Brotherhood and Sharing\r\n\r\n## Connect Deeply in a Trusted Circle\r\n\r\nJoin Fireside Gatherings of Trust and Friendship.\r\n\r\nExperience the unique Wild at Heart Fires, where a small group of men unite monthly to share stories and insights within a safe and confidential space.\r\n\r\n## Share and Listen in Confidence\r\n\r\nAround the fire, discover a sanctuary for men to openly share deeper parts of their stories, knowing their experiences are met with understanding and respect.\r\n\r\n## Foster Genuine Bonds and Support\r\n\r\nBe part of a community that values honesty, support, and the power of shared experiences in a confidential setting.\r\n\r\n## Ignite Personal Growth and Connection\r\n\r\nWild at Heart Fires offer a chance to explore life\'s deeper questions and build authentic friendships and a deeper spiritual connection.',NULL,'[]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'https://vimeo.com/505766418','reg text','reg before','[]','[]','event_types/481aa244-1ba4-4522-8ac6-093a927b3526.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-fires.jpg',NULL,NULL,'[\"event_types/fires/image.jpg\", \"event_types/fires/image1.jpg\", \"event_types/fires/image2.jpg\", \"event_types/fires/image3.jpg\", \"event_types/fires/image4.jpg\"]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-11 02:39:46','At Wild at Heart Fires, men gather around a fire to talk about the real stuff—the challenges, the wins, the questions that don’t always have easy answers.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"k1hgZc7f\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M18 3a1 1 0 00-1.447-.894L8.763 6H5a3 3 0 000 6h.28l1.771 5.316A1 1 0 008 18h1a1 1 0 001-1v-4.382l6.553 3.276A1 1 0 0018 15V3z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M18 3a1 1 0 00-1.447-.894L8.763 6H5a3 3 0 000 6h.28l1.771 5.316A1 1 0 008 18h1a1 1 0 001-1v-4.382l6.553 3.276A1 1 0 0018 15V3z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Fires aren\'t religious\", \"description\": \"Leave your religious and professional credentials behind.\"}, \"headline\": \"Fires aren\'t religious\", \"description\": \"Leave your religious and professional credentials behind.\"}, {\"id\": \"P1dowUK4\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Your story matters\", \"description\": \"Fires are not a place for teaching or a podium for experts.\"}, \"headline\": \"Your story matters\", \"description\": \"Fires are not a place for teaching or a podium for experts.\"}, {\"id\": \"2LdWweMu\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M13.477 14.89A6 6 0 015.11 6.524l8.367 8.368zm1.414-1.414L6.524 5.11a6 6 0 018.367 8.367zM18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M13.477 14.89A6 6 0 015.11 6.524l8.367 8.368zm1.414-1.414L6.524 5.11a6 6 0 018.367 8.367zM18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"No bullshit allowed\", \"description\": \"Fires are a place for authentic masculinity. No posing.\"}, \"headline\": \"No bullshit allowed\", \"description\": \"Fires are a place for authentic masculinity. No posing.\"}, {\"id\": \"2rHQ4lHp\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Confidentiality is essential\", \"description\": \"What is shared at a Fire stays at the Fire.\"}, \"headline\": \"Confidentiality is essential\", \"description\": \"What is shared at a Fire stays at the Fire.\"}]','[{\"id\": \"m0zah0ef\", \"button_url\": \"https://b-cdn.wildatheart.org/wp-app/uploads/2023/06/05095547/WaH-Fires_Firestarter-Manual_v1.0-060623.pdf\", \"button_label\": \"Firestarter Manual\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0zae6ni\", \"button_url\": \"https://shop.wildatheart.org/discount/RCFH23RNRE8J\", \"button_label\": \"Order Books\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m220q346\", \"button_url\": \"https://join.slack.com/t/wildatheartcommunity/shared_invite/zt-2l65yzopd-RKRyTo4ROQ6VShTI0RpUzg\", \"button_label\": \"Fires Slack Community\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'be30fea0-e984-4b88-a433-a4e7ec911284'),
	(2,1,'Expected number of attendees','retreat','retreat','Wild at Heart Retreat',NULL,2,NULL,'https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/2m39hrq/','A Wild at Heart retreat is Wild at Heart Boot Camp led by John Eldredge and his team through video session in your local area.',NULL,1,'men','wild-at-heart-retreat','A Wild At Heart retreat (formerly BASIC) isn\'t just another men\'s retreat. That\'s the last thing anybody needs. The reason most messages for men ultimately fail is simple: they ignore what is deep and true to a man\'s heart and try to shape him up through various forms of pressure.\n\nNot this. This event is an honest, no-BS trek into the deep passions and desires of a man\'s heart, the healing of the wounds he\'s taken in this battle, the realm of fatherhood and sex and God and calling—life as it was meant to be lived.\n\nFor over two decades, Wild At Heart retreats, featuring John and his team in-person, have taken place in remote locations around the world. Previously, only individuals who could afford and manage the travel had access to these impactful gatherings. Today, this transformative event is accessible to men everywhere by empowering local hosts in facilitating this life-changing journey for the men in their communities. Wild At Heart retreats package all video sessions from the live events, along with resources designed to support local hosts.\n\nThrough the sessions, times of quiet reflection, movies, adventures and downtime, you will discover something profound about the heart of God and the heart he gave you as a man. Those who come say it is one of the greatest weekends of their entire life. Now It’s your turn.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0vmoyox\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmp4ax\", \"body\": \"Start by watching this message from John and the Wild at Heart Team.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmpgck\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/769577075\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmq0ci\", \"body\": \"Written on every man’s heart is a yearning for adventure, battle, and a beauty. A man needs a deeper understanding of why these longings govern him—and why God made him just like that. And he needs a deeper understanding of why women long to be fought for, to be swept up into adventure, and to be the beauty.\\n\\nWhat if? What if those deep desires in our hearts are telling us the truth, revealing to us the lives we were meant to live? God gave us eyes so that we might see; he gave us ears that we might hear; he gave us wills that we might choose; and he gave us hearts that we might live. The way we handle the heart is everything. A man must know he is powerful; he must know he has what it takes.\\n\\nThe story of Wild at Heart Boot Camp is one of men encountering God and experiencing healing, breakthrough, freedom, and strength restored. It is not a retreat about the “seven things a man ought to do to be a nicer guy.” It is a four-day quest into the recovery of a man’s masculine soul, the release of a man’s heart—his passions and his true nature—all given him by God. It’s an invitation to rush the fields at Bannockburn, to go West, to leap from the falls and save the beauty. For if a man is going to know who he truly is as a man, if he is going to find a life worth living, love a woman deeply, and not pass on his confusion to his children, he simply must get his heart back.\\n\\nFor over a decade, John Eldredge and his team have led more than 20,000 men through Wild at Heart Boot Camps, all around the globe, against a backdrop of beauty and adventure. They are expeditions of the heart, and the men who’ve attended will never be the same.\\n\\nGod is up to something epic, and it’s much larger than John and his team.\\n\\nThat’s why we’ve created the Wild at Heart retreat.\\n\\nSimply put, Wild at Heart retreat is Wild at Heart Boot Camp led by John and his team through video session and facilitated by courageous men like you all over the globe.\\n\\nYou invite a handful of interested men in your world to experience the transformational Wild at Heart message, and we will give you all the tools you need to successfully facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat.\\n\\nAll the sessions are by video—you serve as host and facilitator. Just hit play and watch each session along with the other men.\\n\\nWe will provide you with a detailed schedule to lead you through each day of this four-day expedition of the masculine heart.\\n\\nIt was William Wallace who once said,\\n\\n“Every man dies. Not every man really lives.”\\n\\nAnd here’s where you come in.\\n\\nWould you be willing to take the risk and join us in this mission to fight for the recovery of life as it was intended for the hearts of men in your world?\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmqba4\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmqcuk\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Welcome to the Fellowship\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmqns0\", \"body\": \"Congratulations. We are thrilled.\\n\\nYou are now a part of a fellowship of like-hearted allies, armed with a message and mission that will forever transform the lives of men.\\n\\nBy choosing to facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat, you have just joined a rare and courageous company of men all around the globe who are united in fighting for the hearts of others.\\n\\nYour part is simple—but it will require courage and perseverance.\\n\\nThis event is for your heart as well as the participants. Together, we can partner with God to bring his Kingdom here on earth, one man’s heart at a time.\\n\\nIf you’re interested in bringing this message to men, let’s dive into more about Wild at Heart retreat.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmrl5f\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Before Your Retreat\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vms5fk\", \"body\": \"Anyone can facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat if they have a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with us in following the guidelines we’ve laid out for you. As a facilitator, you agree to offer the full four-day Wild at Heart retreat experience, adhering to the details, not adding to or subtracting from any of the content. You also agree to provide us with feedback so we can continue to improve Wild at Heart retreat for future events.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vms9q6\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmsb7s\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Choose your date\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmsjow\", \"body\": \"Important: Wild at Heart retreat requires four days (usually Thursday afternoon through Sunday at noon).\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmsnkp\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Choose your men\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmssjx\", \"body\": \"This guide is designed for a group of four to eight men, but it will work for any size.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmswsj\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Choose your location\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmt144\", \"body\": \"This is a full-immersion experience. It’s your responsibility to create a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility that is removed from everyday life.\\n\\nThis event is an invitation for your heart, and the hearts of attendees, to have permission to be the priority. God has been waiting to meet you in this place. And this retreat is the next great chance to receive, distraction-free.\\n\\nIn order to create the best possible environment for this event, we have set Wild at Heart retreat as an official Technology-Free Zone.\\n\\nAlong with location, you should begin planning to have an emergency phone number to provide to men attending. They will have time to call or text anyone who needs the emergency number on the opening day of the retreat. Invite your attendees to turn off all phones, smart-watches, laptops etc for the duration of the event. \\n\\nIn the event of an emergency, you as the Wild at Heart retreat facilitator, can be reached at the emergency number provided to the men.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmtbbr\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Invite your guys\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmtfcm\", \"body\": \"The following materials can be found in the marketing folder of the downloads section:\\n\\n- PDF poster \\n- PDF flyer\\n- Video trailer \\n- Email invite templates\\n- Wild at Heart retreat logo and graphics\\n\\nWhen you agree to facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat, you\'re agreeing to maintain the look and feel of a Boot Camp event—including the integrity and use of the Wild at Heart retreat logo. \\n\\nlf you plan to create materials beyond what Wild at Heart provides, it\'s important you:\\n\\n1. only use the Wild at Heart retreat logo provided—without adding or taking away any design elements\\n2. not create your own Wild at Heart retreat logo or hybrid design\\n3. remember, although this is a local gathering, it is part of a larger movement that already has an established look and feel.\\n\\nThanks for helping us stay true to every aspect of Wild at Heart retreat at your facilitated event - including the use of the Wild at Heart name and logo.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmuoa7\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Get yourself ready\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmuuj7\", \"body\": \"Read the book [Wild at Heart](https://churchsource.com/products/wild-at-heart-expanded-ed-discovering-the-secret-of-a-mans-soul?variant=32679916142689) before the event. Watch all the downloadable Wild at Heart retreat video sessions ahead of time so you’re familiar with the content. We want to make sure you have the most up-to-date version of each session. These are available for free download in Section.  You might also consider purchasing the book and Field Guide for all of your attendees by [clicking here](https://churchsource.com/pages/wild-at-heart-captivating)—it would be so good for them to have copies of their own through the weekend. At that link, you can save 50% on orders of 20+ Items when you use the promo code WAH20\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmwtjm\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"The Retreat Schedule\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmx3ox\", \"body\": \"**IMPORTANT NOTES:**\\n\\n- All sessions will be taught by the Wild at Heart team via video. You will not add to or take away from the content / schedule.\\n- Men need to fully unplug. Provide an emergency contact number (that goes to you) and tell your participants to make one last call or e-mail to give that number to those who may need it. Then have them turn off all devices. The outside world will try to distract people. This will be one of the best decisions you make.\\n- Built into the Wild at Heart retreat schedule are “covenants of silence” so the men have dedicated time to hear from God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the sessions. These times of silence are the centerpiece of Wild at Heart retreat, and you will need to help preserve and protect them.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmxkti\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmxlvz\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Sessions Overview\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmy0cg\", \"body\": \"Here’s an overview of the sessions:\\n\\nSession One – The Heart of a Man\\n\\nSession Two – Epic: The Larger Story\\n\\nSession Three – The Poser\\n\\nSession Four – Healing the Wound\\n\\nSession Five – New Name\\n\\nSession Six – Warfare\\n\\nSession Seven – Adventure\\n\\nSession Eight – Beauty\\n\\nSession Nine – Sonship\\n\\nSession Ten – Where We Go From Here\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vmy3gv\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Retreat Day 1\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vmyddb\", \"body\": \"1:00 p.m.\\nFacilitators: Watch Day 1 Facilitator Briefing Video\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmyfxe\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/215538850\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmz64m\", \"body\": \"1:30 - 3:00 p.m.\\nFacilitators: Watch Consecration Briefing & Consecrate your Wild at Heart retreat\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmz95p\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/309925460\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmznvt\", \"body\": \"4:00 - 5:00 p.m.\\nAttendees arrive \\n\\n6:00 - 7:00 p.m.\\nDinner \\n\\n7:00 - 8:25 p.m.\\nSession 1 – The Heart of a Man\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vmzur0\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214711903\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vn07eo\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Retreat Day 2\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vn0ij5\", \"body\": \"7:00 a.m.\\nFacilitators: Watch the Day 2 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team Facilitators: Pray the Daily Prayer\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn0lbh\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/215539946\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn0ycw\", \"body\": \"8:00 - 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast\\n\\n8:45 - 9:50 a.m.\\nSession 2 – Epic: The Larger Story\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn146d\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712179\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn1j9z\", \"body\": \"10:00 - 10:15 a.m.\\nBreak\\n\\n10:15 - 11:15 a.m.\\nSession 3 – The Poser\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn1pzo\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712542\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn276s\", \"body\": \"11:15 - 12:00 p.m.\\nReflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point (a time for facilitators to check in with the other each other and to pray as a group for the guys, the coming sessios and whatever else God has in store for you)\\n\\n12:00 - 12:45 p.m.\\nLunch\\n\\n12:45 - 4:30 p.m.\\nFree Time – Ask God what your heart needs (sleep, adventure, solitude, etc.)\\n\\n4:30 - 6:00 p.m.\\nSession 4 – The Wound\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn2hbk\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712603\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn2z7y\", \"body\": \"6:00 - 6:30 p.m.\\nReflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n6:30 - 7:30 p.m.\\nDinner\\n\\n7:30 - 8:35 p.m.\\nSession 5 – The New Name\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn326i\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712644\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn3f7z\", \"body\": \"8:35 - 9:00 p.m.\\nReflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n9:00 p.m. \\nBurning of the Yellow Passports\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vn3hh4\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Retreat Day 3\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vn3nt6\", \"body\": \"7:00 a.m.\\nFacilitators: Watch the Day 3 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team Facilitators: Pray the Daily Prayer\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn3uvc\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/215541921\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn4s7g\", \"body\": \"8:00 - 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast\\n\\n8:45 - 9:45 a.m.\\nSession 6 – Warfare (opens with a Message to the Attendees)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn4xn7\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712686\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn5w7k\", \"body\": \"9:45 - 10:15 a.m.\\nReflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n10:15 - 11:20 a.m.\\nSession 7 – Adventure\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn63ik\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712754\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn6ecr\", \"body\": \"11:20 a.m.- 12 p.m.\\nReflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n12:00 - 12:45 p.m. Lunch\\n\\n12:45 - 5:00 p.m. Free Time\\n(Note: Originally when Wild at Heart retreat launched we had a Saturday afternoon session. But due to a changing world, both at the Wild at Heart Boot Camp and here in Wild at Heart retreat we have pulled a session in order to provide more breathing room for the souls of the men attending. Please protect the free time and allow men to get outside, to breathe, to rest, and get what they need)\\n\\n5:00 - 6 :00 p.m.\\nDinner\\n\\n6:00 - 7:25 p.m.\\nSession 8 – Beauty\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn6nkp\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712793\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn6wfo\", \"body\": \"8:25 p.m.\\nOptional Movie\\n\\nAt this point in Wild at Heart retreat, men need to pray and ask God what they need. Maybe it’s some extra rest. Maybe it’s some down time by a campfire with a cigar. Maybe it’d be good for the masculine soul to watch a film that features the narrative of Wild at Heart retreat. If you choose to offer an optional film, we suggest one of these:\\n\\n- Braveheart\\n- Gladiator\\n- The Legend of Bagger Vance\\n- The Kingdom of Heaven\\n- The Kid\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vn7ai7\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Retreat Day 4\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vn7hao\", \"body\": \"7:00 a.m.\\nFacilitators: Watch the Day 4 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team Facilitators: Pray the Daily Prayer\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn7o4v\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/215543249\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn80p6\", \"body\": \"8:00 - 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast\\n\\n8:45 - 10:05 a.m.\\nSession 9 – Sonship\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn861u\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712886\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn8jef\", \"body\": \"10:05 - 11:00 a.m.\\nFinal Time with God\\n\\n11:00 a.m. - 12:00 p.m.\\nSession 10 – Where We Go From Here\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn8poa\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/214712925\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vn92gz\", \"body\": \"12:00 p.m.\\nOptional Lunch\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vn96rk\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Attendee Feedback\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vn9eej\", \"body\": \"We need your feedback. It helps us to offer ongoing strength, support, and development to you and your men. We ask that you and your men follow through with that feedback upon completion of Wild at Heart retreat. [https://my.wildatheart.org/wah/form/wild-at-heart-retreat-feedback] (https://my.wildatheart.org/wah/form/wild-at-heart-retreat-feedback)\\n\\n\\nFacilitators: We also want to hear your thoughts about facilitating a Wild at Heart retreat. We want to know how it went. Leave your feedback at [https://my.wildatheart.org/wah/form/wild-at-heart-retreat-feedback](https://my.wildatheart.org/wah/form/wild-at-heart-retreat-feedback).\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnaz7w\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"FAQ\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnb4mt\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnb8aq\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Why doesn’t the schedule include typical retreat elements like worship music or communion?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnbbkb\", \"body\": \"Because this isn’t a typical men’s retreat. Trust us on this one. You’ll see why later.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnbgpx\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Do I need to follow the 4-day schedule?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnbmud\", \"body\": \"If you would like to publicly list your Wild at Heart retreat on our website for anyone to find and attend then yes, we require you to follow the schedule exactly. The reason we require you to follow the schedule is because we’re promoting the Wild at Heart retreat listings on our website to thousands of people each month and guaranteeing they’re all lead the exact same way. Also, through more than a decade we’ve learned this schedule works.\\n\\nThat being said, we’re certainly behind you if God is leading you to host on a different schedule. We will happily bless any schedule you choose including weekly for 11 weeks. If you’d like to host a Wild at Heart retreat and deviate from the Wild at Heart retreat schedule laid out in this Facilitator’s guide, make sure you register your Wild at Heart retreat and then choose the option to remove it from the website listings. This way you’ll still receive your note taking guides and all of the Wild at Heart retreat benefits.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnbxi7\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What about meals?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnc19w\", \"body\": \"Choose simple, ready-made meals. Don’t require prep of the attendees. If prep and cleanup take more than 10 minutes, we recommend having a dedicated person not involved in the event to do it. Meal time—not the sessions—is also the chance to make any “housekeeping announcements.”\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnc8hz\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Can you facilitate this alone?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vncda5\", \"body\": \"You can, but we encourage you to find a partner or a small team to help. It’s always better not to fly solo when possible.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vncjuq\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Should you charge men to attend a Wild at Heart retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vncow7\", \"body\": \"We don’t recommend doing so. We provide our content and notebooks to you at no charge. Our assumption is the only additional costs would be meals and perhaps a facility charge. Some facilitators choose to absorb these costs. Others charge a minimal fee to each attendee.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vncu1d\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Why can’t I use the DVDs?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnczv2\", \"body\": \"We want to make sure you have the most up-to-date version of each session. Free downloads of these are available in the downloads section.\\n\\nYou’ll want to use a laptop that has an HDMI output to connect to your TV or projector.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vndob5\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What is the Facilitator Touch Point referenced in the schedule?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vndso6\", \"body\": \"A Facilitator Touch Point is a time for your group of facilitator’s to gather together and check in with each other and with God. You may use this time to pray for each other and for your attendees and to ask God for direction into your Wild at Heart retreat.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vndxzs\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What are the ground rules for Wild at Heart retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vne3vs\", \"body\": \"Great question. It starts with pledging absolute confidentiality. Nothing shared in Wild at Heart retreat gets repeated outside the group, unless specific permission is given. This is vital, as the mission is to create the most safe and sacred environment for a man to encounter God in the depths of his masculine soul.\\n\\nNext, commit to the technology-free dimension of this event. Again, this is a full-immersion experience. It’s your responsibility to create a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. Wild at Heart retreat is a beautiful and rare chance to receive from God, distraction-free. Be strategic and proactive in securing, and providing an emergency contact number.\\n\\nFacilitators, be slow to offer advice. Let God lead this. Less is more. Give room for God, and he will show up.\\n\\nPrayer is the backbone. It’s not a religious act—it’s the lifeblood of God’s supernatural work in and through Wild at Heart retreat. Pray before, consecrating the men, the space, and every aspect of the mission. Pray during, and ask a few you trust to serve as intercessory prayer warriors for these four days. Pray after—against retaliation, and for the full enforcement of Heaven for what God is doing. It will be the difference between inspiration and transformation.\\n\\nSee it through to the end. You’ll face opposition. It’s all part of his training for your role in the Kingdom. Don’t lose heart. You’re not alone. And you’re dangerous, in a really good way. See it through, and he’ll give you every resource you need for it to be realized.\\n\\nFinally, give us feedback. We want to invest in you. We want to invest in your men so that your communities will be strengthened and become a center for God’s Kingdom advancement. Every bit of feedback helps us offer more.\\n\\nLastly, we’re proud of you and admire your courage to give it a try.\\n\\nYou’ll never regret it.\\n\\nYou are rare.\\n\\nThe lives of many rest in the courage of a few.\\n\\nStrength and Honor,\\nThe Wild at Heart Team\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## WELCOME \n\nWritten on every man’s heart is a yearning for adventure, battle, and a beauty. A man needs a deeper understanding of why these longings govern him—and why God made him just like that. And he needs a deeper understanding of why women long to be fought for, to be swept up into adventure, and to be the beauty.\n\nWhat if? What if those deep desires in our hearts are telling us the truth, revealing to us the lives we were meant to live? God gave us eyes so that we might see; he gave us ears that we might hear; he gave us wills that we might choose; and he gave us hearts that we might live. The way we handle the heart is everything. A man must know he is powerful; he must know he has what it takes.\n\nThe story of Wild at Heart retreats is one of men encountering God and experiencing healing, breakthrough, freedom, and strength restored. It is not a retreat about the “seven things a man ought to do to be a nicer guy.” It is a four-day quest into the recovery of a man’s masculine soul, the release of a man’s heart—his passions and his true nature—all given him by God. It’s an invitation to rush the fields at Bannockburn, to go West, to leap from the falls and save the beauty. For if a man is going to know who he truly is as a man, if he is going to find a life worth living, love a woman deeply, and not pass on his confusion to his children, he simply must get his heart back.\n\nFor over a decade, John Eldredge and his team have led more than 20,000 men through Wild at Heart retreats, all around the globe, against a backdrop of beauty and adventure. They are expeditions of the heart, and the men who’ve attended will never be the same.\n\nGod is up to something epic, and it’s much larger than John and his team.\n\nThat’s why we’ve created Wild at Heart retreats.\n\nSimply put, Wild at Heart retreat led by John and his team through video session and facilitated by courageous men like you all over the globe.\n\nYou invite a handful of interested men in your world to experience the transformational Wild at Heart message, and we will give you all the tools you need to successfully facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat.\n\nAll the sessions are by video—you serve as host and facilitator. Just hit play and watch each session along with the other men.\n\nWe will provide you with a detailed schedule to lead you through each day of this four-day expedition of the masculine heart.\n\nIt was William Wallace who once said,\n“Every man dies. Not every man really lives.”\n\nAnd here’s where you come in.\n\nWould you be willing to take the risk and join us in this mission to fight for the recovery of life as it was intended for the hearts of men in your world?\n\nOnce you complete registration, we’ll unlock all of the content, videos, and provide an agenda for your event.','## BEFORE YOUR RETREAT \n\nAnyone can facilitate a Wild at Heart retreat if they have a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with us in following the guidelines we’ve laid out for you. As a facilitator, you agree to offer the full four-day Wild at Heart retreat experience, adhering to the details, not adding to or subtracting from any of the content. You also agree to provide us with feedback so we can continue to improve Wild at Heart retreats for future events.\n\nAs part of registration, you will:\n1. Choose your date - Wild at Heart retreats require four days (usually Thursday afternoon through Sunday at noon).\n2. Choose your men - Wild at Heart retreats are designed for a group of four to eight men, but it will work for any size.\n3. Choose your location - This is a full-immersion experience. It’s your responsibility to create a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility that is removed from everyday life. More details in this same section after registration.\n4. Invite your guys - We’ll provide full marketing content in the resources section after registration that include posters, flyers, video trailers, and email invite templates.\n5. Get yourself ready - We recommend you read the Wild at Heart book before the event and watch all of the downloadable content from the resources section so you’re familiar with the content.','[{\"id\": \"176ce20a\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## RETREAT SCHEDULE\\n\\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\\n\\n1. All sessions will be taught by the Wild at Heart team via video. You will not add to or take away from the content / schedule.\\n2. Men need to fully unplug. Provide an emergency contact number (that goes to you) and tell your participants to make one last call or email to give that number to those who may need it. Then have them turn off all devices. The outside world will try to distract people. This will be one of the best decisions you make.\\n3. Built into the Wild at Heart Retreat schedule are “covenants of silence” so the men have dedicated time to hear from God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the sessions. These times of silence are the centerpiece of the Wild at Heart retreat, and you will need to help preserve and protect them\\n\\nOverview of retreat sessions:\\n1. Session One - The Heart of a Man\\n2. Session Two - Epic: The Larger Story\\n3. Session Three - The Poser\\n4. Session Four - Healing the Wound\\n5. Session Five - New Name\\n6. Session Six - Warfare\\n7. Session Seven - Adventure\\n8. Session Eight - Beauty\\n9. Session Nine - Sonship\\n10. Session Ten - Where We Go From Here\\n\\nAfter registration, the resources section will provide a detailed agenda for each day, facilitator briefings, and video sessions for each day.\"}]','[{\"id\": \"lzihv7dd\", \"answer\": \"Because this isn’t a typical men’s retreat. Trust us on this one. You’ll see why later.\", \"question\": \"Why doesn’t the schedule include typical retreat elements?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzihvf0c\", \"answer\": \"If you would like to publicly list your Wild at Heart Retreat on our website for anyone to find and attend then yes, we require you to follow the schedule exactly. The reason we require you to follow the schedule is because we’re promoting the Wild at Heart Retreat listings on our website to thousands of people each month and guaranteeing they’re all lead the exact same way. Also, through more than a decade we’ve learned this schedule works.\\n\\nThat being said, we’re certainly behind you if God is leading you to host on a different schedule. We will happily bless any schedule you choose including weekly for 11 weeks. If you’d like to host a Wild at Heart Retreat and deviate from the Wild at Heart Retreat schedule laid out in this Facilitator’s guide, make sure you register your Wild at Heart Retreat and then choose the option to remove it from the website listings. This way you’ll still receive your note taking guides and all of the Wild at Heart Retreat benefits.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to follow the 4-day schedule?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzihvvyk\", \"answer\": \"Choose simple, ready-made meals. Don’t require prep of the attendees. If prep and cleanup take more than 10 minutes, we recommend having a dedicated person not involved in the event to do it. Meal time—not the sessions—is also the chance to make any “housekeeping announcements.”\", \"question\": \"What about meals?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzihw98c\", \"answer\": \"You can, but we encourage you to find a partner or a small team to help. It’s always better not to fly solo when possible.\", \"question\": \"Can you facilitate this alone?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzihwj58\", \"answer\": \"We don’t recommend doing so. We provide our content and notebooks to you at no charge. Our assumption is the only additional costs would be meals and perhaps a facility charge. Some facilitators choose to absorb these costs. Others charge a minimal fee to each attendee.\", \"question\": \"Should I charge men to attend?\"}]','event_types/bee345c6-206e-4642-a010-7e7f917b0e3b.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-wahretreat.jpg',NULL,'https://vimeo.com/1012088094','[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-18 02:57:08','The Wild At Heart Retreat is a multi-day experience designed to help men recover their strength, reconnect with God, and step more fully into the life they were created to live.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vnf8uu\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/uhyvzi9gzrysga40t7coq/AFq-B54xAn8yAQZtNLdoYp8/current%20wah%20retreat%20downloads?dl=0&rlkey=0v9tkexmrugnsdtjandgz1wa1&subfolder_nav_tracking=1\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnfo14\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/g7ays52c6inmgj3yaailv/ACgRKSt0s75ZZNaUvoDW6IA?rlkey=j5dq4st4xgyas3mht80w6xziq&e=1&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Event Guide PDF\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'2a481ed1-bf59-41c0-95d4-70e228c94a14'),
	(3,1,'Expected number of attendees','retreat','retreat','4-Day Captivating Retreat',NULL,3,NULL,'https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/2m31jy1/','The Captivating retreat is a retreat led by Stasi Eldredge and her team through video session in your local area.',NULL,1,'women','captivating-retreat','Rooted in the message of _Captivating_ by Stasi and John Eldredge, this video-led experience is hosted by women around the world who are saying yes to offering beauty, rest, and healing to the women in their communities.\n\nFor over two decades, women have gathered in the Colorado mountains for the Captivating Retreat, hosted by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team, to meet with God and recover what has been lost. Now this life-changing retreat is available through local hosts to women everywhere. Whether you host or attend, you\'re invited to walk with God through a deeper journey of restoration, identity, and joy.\n\nGod sees your longing for more life, more hope, and more healing, and he is inviting you to go on a treasure hunt for his heart—and your own. “Come away with me, my beloved,” he says (Song of Songs 2:10). Through the powerful video sessions, music, intentional times with God, and beauty, you won’t just gain more information—you’ll encounter Jesus. \n\nThis is for you: an invitation to risk, awaken, and recover your heart. Come and experience the beauty, strength, and presence of God in a setting crafted just for you.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0umzjpy\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0umzn09\", \"body\": \"Dear one, welcome to the 4-Day Captivating Retreat. Thank you for saying yes!\\n\\nYou’ve stepped into something beautiful and brave. It matters. Generations will be healed and changed for the good. Remember, this is God’s invitation. He is inviting you to walk with him and do it out of his strength. He will give you everything you need to create space for women to encounter his love and recover the beauty and strength of their hearts. \\n\\nYou’re not doing this alone. We’ll walk you through every step and give you all you need to create a sacred experience for the women you invite, so that they can encounter God and move towards the more that he has for them.\\n\\nTo begin, watch this personal message from Stasi and the Captivating team:\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vofq5v\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/358885691\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vog4s9\", \"body\": \"## What’s at the Heart of the Captivating Retreat?\\n\\nWritten on the heart of every woman are three core desires:\\n- to be romanced\\n- to play an irreplaceable role in a grand adventure\\n- to unveil a beauty all her own\\n\\nThese longings aren’t shallow or unrealistic dreams. They are echoes of who God created us to be and the life we were meant to live. This is the heartbeat of the Captivating message.\\n\\nWe as women are longing to come alive again, and Jesus is inviting us into more—into a sacred space to encounter God and reclaim the truth of who we are as his beloved daughters.\\n\\nWhether you’re hosting a few close friends or a larger group, we thank you for joining this global movement of women creating space for healing, restoration, and deeper connection with God. You are stepping into the beautiful mission of his Isaiah 61 ministry; this is what Jesus came to do: heal the brokenhearted and restore what has been lost. And now he is inviting you to join him.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What Comes with Your Registration\\n\\nAs a registered Captivating Retreat facilitator, you now have free access to\\n\\n- all video sessions led by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team\\n- a detailed retreat schedule\\n- note-taking guides mailed to the address you provided at registration\\n- behind-the-scenes guidance videos from our Wild at Heart women’s team\\n- access to an online community of facilitators where you can ask and answer questions, encourage one another, and offer support \\n\\nWhether you’re hosting a public or private retreat, you’ll have everything you need to facilitate your retreat. You’ll find all the resources and next steps in this guide.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vogx97\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": false, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vogxxu\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Welcome\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0voh5yb\", \"body\": \"Congratulations. We are so happy you said yes!\\n\\nBy choosing to facilitate a Captivating Retreat, you have just joined a courageous community of women all around the globe united in fighting for the hearts of others. This message and mission will forever transform the lives of women. \\n \\nYour part is simple—but it will require courage and perseverance.\\n\\nThis event is for your heart as well as the participants. Together, we can partner with God to bring his Kingdom here on earth, one woman’s heart at a time.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": false}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzwywmc\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Preparing the Way\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzwz447\", \"body\": \"**This is about your presence, not performance.**\\n\\nYou don’t need to be a teacher, counselor, or expert host—just have a willing heart. God has invited you into something sacred: creating a space for women to encounter him. That’s no small thing.\\n\\nAs a facilitator, you’re committing to lead with integrity, which means honoring the way this retreat has been prayerfully shaped over decades:\\n\\n- hosting the full 4-day experience as designed\\n- creating a distraction-free, sacred space\\n- letting the sessions unfold without adding or removing content\\n\\nYou’re part of something beautiful: God’s invitation to restore hearts and change lives.\\n\\nLet’s begin preparing the way.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Choose Your Dates \\n\\nThe Captivating Retreat is a 4-day experience, most commonly held from Thursday afternoon through Sunday at noon. Please plan for the full time. This message builds session by session and isn’t to be rushed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Choose Your Location\\n\\nThis is a full-immersion experience. Wherever you host, your goal is to provide an unplugged, peaceful, distraction-free setting. It doesn’t have to be fancy, just set apart.\\n\\nSome options:\\n\\n- Borrow or rent a cabin, VRBO, or retreat center. Make sure you have strong Wi-Fi, and download the sessions in advance just in case.\\n- Use your home. Do what you can to minimize noise, interruptions, pets, kids, and daily demands.\\n- Find a venue that provides meals or allows catering. Costs can be shared among attendees.\\n\\nNote: If overnight accommodations are not possible, as a last resort, women can go home to sleep and return the next day. However, we encourage you to allow time for worship before the first session to help everyone settle back in.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Invite Your Participants  \\n\\nThis retreat was created for both small and large groups. What matters most is a safe, sacred space where hearts can open and God can move.\\n\\nWe’ve provided a Captivating Retreat logo for you in the download section. Because this retreat is a local expression of a global movement with an established identity, we ask that the logo be used as-is, without edits. You’re welcome to use it across any promotional materials you need as long as you honor its original design. Thank you for helping us steward the heart and visual integrity of Captivating.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Prepare Your Heart\\n\\nThis retreat is for you too. Before the logistics take over, pause to tend your own heart and invite God to speak about what he has in this. Here are a few ways to prepare:\\n\\n- **Use the Pause App daily**, or whenever needed, to center your heart and realign with God’s presence.  [(Download the Pause App here.)](https://www.pauseapp.com/)\\n- **Read the book _Captivating_ again.**\\n- **Consider purchasing the _Captivating_ book and _Guided Journal_** for your attendees. [(Get 50% off orders of 20 or more using the code WAH20.)](https://churchsource.com/collections/wild-at-heart-captivating)\\n- **Watch all the video sessions ahead of time** so you’re familiar with the content. [(Make sure you download the most updated versions from the resources section.)](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/34pk1488c9tiu5b04xavi/APk6u4TRuP6AxHZ6gzqHrsM?rlkey=ho68r8p4l349oqry3ji7oezbu&st=vojvadkg&dl=0)\\n\\n**Tech note:** We recommend having 200 GB of free space to download and run all video files smoothly.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThank you, beloved. You are offering something sacred. Something bold.\\n\\nGod is with you; you are not in this alone.\\n\\nWe are covering you in prayer and cheering you on as you step into this holy mission.\\n\\nLet the preparation begin.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzwzfs5\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Guiding the Experience\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzwznsl\", \"body\": \"Every session of the Captivating Retreat is delivered by video from Stasi and the Captivating team. Your role is to host, keeping the space sacred, staying on schedule, and guiding the flow of the experience.\\n\\n---\\n**Protect an unplugged environment**\\n\\nInvite women to fully unplug. Share an emergency contact number (yours or a co-host’s) so family can reach them if needed. This gift of disconnection is rare and deeply powerful and important for this sacred time.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Guard the covenants of silence**\\n\\nBuilt into the schedule is dedicated time alone with God—quiet, personal space we call “covenants of silence.” This gives women time to be alone with God, journal, and go deeper with what the sessions have stirred. These times are often the most impactful part of the retreat. As the facilitator, your role is to encourage and protect this sacred space.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Worship is simple but sacred**\\n\\nYou can download session videos with or without built-in worship. If you choose the version without, links to Spotify playlists will be provided in the schedule. \\n\\nEach session begins with one or two worship songs. This is an essential part of the flow that helps center the women’s hearts. Some evenings include extended worship times. (A Spotify Premium account will help avoid ads.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Worship Room Setup**\\n\\nIf your venue allows, consider creating a dedicated worship room—a sanctuary for women to meet with God beyond the sessions for personal worship, prayer, or reflection.\\n\\n**Setup Ideas (Keep It Simple):**\\n\\n- soft lighting (lamps, fairy lights, or flameless candles)\\n- cozy seating (pillows, blankets, or chairs)\\n- gentle instrumental worship or a soaking worship playlist on loop\\n- simple supplies (paper, pens, tissues, and Scripture cards)\\n- prayer board or basket for women to leave written prayers\\n- optional sign on the door: “Worship Room – Sacred Space for Silence and Prayer”\\n\\n**Optional Touches:**\\n\\n- table with art supplies for expressive worship (watercolors, pastels, etc.)\\n- printed Scripture displayed around the room\\n- cross or focal point to draw hearts toward Jesus\\n- designated intercessor available to pray quietly if someone desires\\n\\nEncourage women to use the space as they feel led—to kneel, weep, journal, dance, or simply rest. There’s no right way; this is just an invitation to come close to the One who loves them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Free Time: An Intentional and Sacred Pause**\\n\\nTwo afternoons include generous space for rest. This isn’t just a break but an essential part of the retreat. Encourage women to ask God what their hearts need and give themselves permission to receive it without guilt or obligation.\\n\\nSome low-key options:\\n- coffee and tea — It\'s helpful to have these available throughout the retreat. Consider asking someone to quietly keep these stocked.\\n- reading\\n- hot tub — Remind the ladies in your preliminary emails to bring their swimsuits if this will be an option.\\n- board games and puzzles\\n- creativity with simple supplies like coloring books, paints, or beads \\n- outdoor games\\n- hiking\\n\\nYou don’t need to entertain during this time; rather, create space for restoration. The most important thing isn’t what’s offered but that the time is protected, peaceful, and unhurried. Encourage women not to fill the time but to choose what will restore their souls.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5j1us9\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Retreat Schedule\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j1ysd\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j1zff\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Overview\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j23ef\", \"body\": \"Day One:\\n- Session 1 – Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart\\n\\nDay Two:\\n- Session 2 – The Larger Story\\n- Session 3 – Fallen Eve\\n- Session 4 – Healing the Wound\\n- Session 5 – Your New Name\\n\\nDay Three:\\n- Session 6 – The Enemy of Your Heart\\n- Session 7 – The Great Romance\\n- Session 8 – Loving Men\\n- Session 9 – Come Closer\\n\\nDay Four:\\n- Session 10 – Your Irreplaceable Role\\n- Session 11 – Where Do We Go from Here?\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5j2a7s\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"The Captivating Retreat – Day 1\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j2gly\", \"body\": \"**1:00 p.m. - Facilitator Prep Time**\\n\\nWatch the **Day 1 Briefing Video** from the Captivating team.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j2mn0\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/358885650\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j2roj\", \"body\": \"**1:30 – 3:00 p.m.\\nConsecration Time for Facilitators:** Set aside time for prayer and consecration of your heart, the space, and the women coming.\\n\\n- Watch the **Consecration Briefing** video. \\n- Use the provided [**worship playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/4JXFLIv57zxB3HmDRmVgbm?si=1798f2a058494a9b) to prepare the atmosphere and invite Jesus into the space for consecration.\\n- Pray over the retreat, your team, the women, and all that God wants to do.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j34ao\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/366859423\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j38xd\", \"body\": \"**4:00 – 5:00 p.m. — Check-In and Settling In**\\n\\n- Welcome the women as they arrive.\\n- Keep the atmosphere peaceful and light, helping the attendees feel safe and welcomed from the moment they walk in.\\n\\n**6:00 – 7:00 p.m.\\nDinner**\\n\\n- Use this meal as a chance to make gentle announcements (where bathrooms are, how mealtimes will work, etc.).\\n\\n**7:00 – 8:35 p.m.\\nSession 1: Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart** \\n\\n- Begin with an opening worship song. If you are not using videos with worship included, you can use this [**Session 1 playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0PkD12hdNUGfTiJYixYhfM?si=da11008cd5584c36).\\n- Play the video session.\\n- Close by releasing the women with a few announcements: \\n\\t- Encourage everyone to fully unplug to lean into the sacredness of the weekend.\\n\\t- Let the women know the time for breakfast and when the first session will begin in the morning.\\n\\t- Let them know they’re free to unwind however they need: enjoy the hot tub, grab a snack, take a walk, or head to bed (likely the best option for most).\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j3hsc\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/354949818\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j3q7k\", \"body\": \"**Facilitator Evening Note:**\\n\\n- Take a moment to check in with your heart and connect as a team (if applicable).\\n- This [**Bedtime Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/bedtime-prayer/) will be a helpful way to end your evening, releasing everything and everyone to God. \\n\\nYou’ve set the table. You’ve opened the door. God is already moving. Rest well, beloved.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5j3tjy\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"The Captivating Retreat – Day 2\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j3yfv\", \"body\": \"**7:00 a.m.\\nFor the Facilitators** \\n\\n- Pray the [**Daily Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/stasidailyprayer/).\\n- Watch the Day 2 Briefing Video from the Captivating team.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j477m\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/358885662\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j4d6f\", \"body\": \"**8:00 - 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast**\\n\\n**8:45 - 9:45 a.m.\\nSession 2 – The Larger Story** \\n\\n- Begin with a worship song from the **[Session 2 playlist](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/16I5J7sCNs0zsEafuhospe?si=2919b45b81264192)**.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j4h5i\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/354950355\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j4qa7\", \"body\": \"**9:45 – 10:00 a.m.\\nBreak**\\n\\n- Allow the women to stretch, hydrate, use the bathroom, and maybe have a small snack.\\n- You can find a between-session playlist [**here**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3nyLZLK34K52W4sCywygQp?si=c4ea8a61e5d145d8).\\n\\n**10:00 – 11:00 a.m.\\nSession 3: Fallen Eve**\\n\\n- Open with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3sP1yiH3lX4KjL2IbVweoT?si=6cca8c852edf442f) to bring the women back in from the break. \\n- At the end of the session and video, a still image of a whale appears. At this point, begin playing [**“I Am Set Free\\\"**](https://open.spotify.com/track/3rcSNbBgCBqY0pdvzfEfSn) to start the first mandatory covenant of silence.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j4v3b\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364471\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j51f5\", \"body\": \"**11:00 – 11:45 a.m.\\nCovenant of Silence (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God.\\n- **Facilitator Touchpoint:** This is a time for you and any co-facilitators to check in in a private space, pray together, intercede for the women, or whatever God has for you.\\n\\n**12:00 – 1:00 p.m.\\nLunch**\\n\\n- This is a good time to announce the afternoon free time and any optional opportunities.\\n- Invite the women to ask God what their hearts need most this afternoon.\\n\\n**1:00 – 4:30 p.m.\\nFree Time**\\n\\n- Rest, play, wander, nap, create—make room for joy and restoration.\\n\\n**4:30 – 5:45 p.m.\\nSession 4: Healing the Wound**\\n\\n- Open with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/32ExGBtQVhAmTrVrAUXLGF?si=905bb47be9064534) to bring the women back in from the break.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j56gk\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364483\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j5cyc\", \"body\": \"**5:45 – 6:30 p.m.\\nCovenant of Silence (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God. \\n- **Facilitator Touchpoint:** Take time to connect, reflect, and pray together before dinner.\\n\\n**6:30 – 7:30 p.m.\\nDinner**\\n\\n**7:30 – 8:45 p.m.\\nSession 5: Your New Name**\\n\\n**Open with a few quick announcements:**\\n\\n- Let the women know the evening ends with extended worship. They’re welcome to stay as long as it\'s good for them—but remind everyone to keep the space quiet for those lingering with God.\\n- After worship, they’re free for the evening, to unwind as they need.\\n- Let them know the time for breakfast and when the first session begins in the morning.\\n- Begin with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/2bVAwlbyF8rtU8iFRZwOTc?si=6335cc62af784565) to bring the women back in.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j5m94\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364489\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j5tx0\", \"body\": \"**8:45 – 9:15 p.m.\\nExtended Worship (Covenant of Silence)**\\n\\nYou can find the playlist [**here**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/2gh8JIQfD7Nu2E3RlSHXW9?si=5fa4581b8048447a).\\n\\nAt Wild at Heart Captivating Retreats, we give each woman a white stone on which to write her “new name”—a keepsake to remember who she is to God. This is optional for your retreat, but if you’d like to include the white stones, here’s how:\\n\\n- Bring enough smooth stones for each attendee (plus a few extras) and Sharpies to share.\\n- After the session video ends—but before soaking worship begins—gently let the women know there’s a gift for them: stones to write their new name on, as God leads.\\n- Remind them that this is a sacred time of silence. Place the stones at the front of the room and invite the women to come forward as they feel led. Let them know that if they don’t hear a name yet, it’s okay. They can take one for later.\\n\\n**Facilitator Evening Note:**\\n\\n- Before bed, take a few quiet minutes to pray the [**Bedtime Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/bedtime-prayer/).\\n\\nGod is moving—personally, tenderly, powerfully—in each woman’s heart. You can trust him with them and with this holy time together. Remain close to his heart, beloved.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5j5x3v\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"The Captivating Retreat – Day 3\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j64g7\", \"body\": \"**7:00 a.m.\\nFor the Facilitators**\\n\\n- Pray the [**Daily Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/stasidailyprayer/).\\n- Watch the **Day 3 Briefing Video** from the Captivating Team.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j697g\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/358885671\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j6fs3\", \"body\": \"**8:00 - 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast**\\n\\n**8:45 - 10:00 a.m.\\nSession 6 – The Enemy of Your Heart**\\n\\n- Begin with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/2zxgHSmPVksDHEknd2ZRYB?si=d448c87ae4ce4d60) from the Session 6 playlist.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j6ibp\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364497\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j6n7o\", \"body\": \"**10:00 – 10:15 a.m.\\nCovenant of Silence / Burning of Agreements (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- At the close of this session, Stasi will guide the women through a Prayer for Breaking Agreements. She’ll encourage them to write their agreements down.\\n- **Before the session begins**, place index cards or small pieces of paper under each attendee\'s seat. After the session, provide a safe place to burn the agreements—this could be a fire pit, fireplace, or even a sink with matches, depending on what’s available and safe.\\n- Tears may flow. This is a sacred and personal moment between each woman and God. Allow space for God, but also be quietly present for anyone who may need gentle support in stepping forward to let go.\\n- [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the holy space during the time of breaking agreements.\\n\\n**10:15 – 11:15 a.m.\\nSession 7: The Great Romance**\\n\\n- Open with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0t6Z1e4yvx5P6EsXCpVHhX?si=f80a796b68a84098) to bring the women back in from the break.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j6t8r\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364504\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j6yft\", \"body\": \"**11:15 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.\\nCovenant of Silence (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God. \\n- **Facilitator Touchpoint:** Take time to connect, reflect, and pray together before the afternoon.\\n\\n**12:00 – 12:45 p.m.\\nLunch**\\n\\n- Announce any afternoon free-time activities.\\n- Encourage each woman to follow God’s leading for what her heart needs most.\\n\\n**12:45 – 4:00 p.m.\\nFree Time**\\n\\n- Rest, play, wander, nap, create—make room for joy and restoration.\\n\\n**4:00 – 5:45 p.m.\\nSession 8: Loving Men** \\n\\n- Welcome the women back from break, and let them know that this session is taught by Stasi’s husband, John Eldredge. Afterward, they’ll have a short time with God before dinner.\\n- You can then open with a worship song to bring the women back in.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j76b4\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364519\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j7fn8\", \"body\": \"**5:45 – 6:00 p.m.\\nCovenant of Silence (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- Short but significant. [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God. \\n\\n**6:00 – 7:00 p.m.\\nDinner**\\n\\n- This is a great time to share any logistical reminders for packing up or cleaning in the morning before they come to breakfast.\\n\\n**7:00 – 8:30 p.m.\\nSession 9: Come Closer**\\n\\n- As you welcome the women back and before you begin, share a few announcements:\\n\\t- This session ends with communion and extended worship. The women may stay as long as they’d like, but remind everyone to keep the space quiet. \\n\\t- Let them know communion is open to any woman who wants to meet Jesus in this personal way. There’s no rush—worship will be about an hour, so each woman can come forward when she feels ready.\\n\\t- If you\'re planning to show a movie tonight, let them know the start time, allowing enough time for them to grab a snack and get comfy.\\n\\t- If there are other optional evening activities, share those now.\\n\\t- If there’s nothing planned afterward, let the women know the evening ends with extended worship. \\n\\t- Finally, let them know the time for breakfast and when the first session will begin in the morning.\\n- Open with a [**worship song**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/6B0FsshdtO3siTzzDItjRT?si=558f47cfc14b45c9) to bring the women back in from the break.\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j7jo6\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364529\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j7qwt\", \"body\": \"**Communion / Extended Worship**\\n\\nYou can find the playlist [**here**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/6fFzqn5byuzJLsJW2YM3fn?si=1ff2193e2f214fec).\\n\\n**Communion Guidance**\\n\\nCommunion is a sacred and optional part of Session 9 (Come Closer) and is meant to be a personal, holy encounter between each woman and Jesus. Keep the atmosphere quiet and reverent. Here are a few tips to help you create a meaningful communion experience:\\n\\n**Supplies to Prepare:**\\n\\n- grape juice and/or wine\\n- communion bread, wafers, and/or gluten-free options\\n- small cups or glasses for serving\\n- a simple table or tray with a cloth for presentation \\n\\n**Optional: Movie Night**\\n\\n- After worship, you may consider offering the choice to watch a film that aligns with the weekend\'s themes. Let the women know in advance so they can get cozy or opt out. (Optional: Provide popcorn or movie snacks.) Here are some movie suggestions:\\n\\t- Pride and Prejudice\\n\\t- Cinderella (2015)\\n\\t- The Help\\n\\t- Shall We Dance?\\n\\t- Anna and the King\\n\\t- The Greatest Showman\\n\\n**Facilitator Evening Note:**\\n\\n- Before bed, take a few quiet minutes to pray the [**Bedtime Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/bedtime-prayer/).\\n\\nHe is with each of these dear hearts. Stay with him. His victory is already won.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5j7ycu\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"The Captivating Retreat – Day 4\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5j8130\", \"body\": \"**7:00 a.m.\\nFor the Facilitators**\\n\\n- Pray the [**Daily Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/prayer/stasidailyprayer).\\n- Watch the Day 4 Briefing Video from the Captivating Team\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j86tz\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/358885682\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j8cfb\", \"body\": \"**8:00 – 8:45 a.m.\\nBreakfast**\\n\\n**8:45 – 10:15 a.m.\\nSession 10: Your Irreplaceable Role**\\n\\n- Begin with a worship song from the [**Session 10 playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/7t0ZZwZtw31yYFVT241k2B?si=9cc60554a9714030).\\n- Play the video session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j8hsu\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364541\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j8o39\", \"body\": \"**10:15 – 11:00 a.m.\\nFinal Covenant of Silence (Mandatory Silence)**\\n\\n- [**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God.\\n\\n**11:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.\\nSession 11: Where Do We Go from Here?**\\n\\n- No opening worship—this session will close with extended worship instead.\\n- Play the video session.\\n\\n**At 21:15 (timestamp in video): Pause for Final Worship** \\n\\n- Invite the women to enter into this final time of worship with hearts full and open.\\n- You can find the playlist [**here**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/1OiteGpRA2gb915v5WHVYW?si=89836249ab994e63).\\n- After worship ends, return to the video and play the closing words from Stasi and the team.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j8t1y\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/355364548\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml5j91il\", \"body\": \"**After the Video** \\n\\n- We encourage you as the facilitator to offer a final prayer or personal words of blessing, or conclude the retreat however the Holy Spirit leads you.\\n\\n**12:00 p.m. – Optional Lunch**\\n\\n- You may offer a final meal together if it fits your space and schedule. Or you can invite the women to head out and carry the beauty into their world, holding fast to every way God showed up for them over the past few days.\\n\\n---\\n\\nYou did it.\\n\\nYou offered your yes, and heaven touched earth.  \\n\\nWell done, beloved. May his favor rest on you, and may the ripples of this retreat extend far beyond what you can see this side of heaven.\\n\\nWe encourage you to stay in the Daily and Bedtime prayers, especially over the next week. Consecrate your mind daily, so that it is only the voice of God that lets you know the glory of this retreat. \\n\\nBless you, dear one. May God now fill you to overflowing, restoring everything you just poured out for others to know him more deeply and have their hearts and stories healed and restored. \\n\\nWith joy and gratitude,\\n**The Captivating Team**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx7gtq\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"FAQ\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx7msy\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx7ozo\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Can I facilitate this alone?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx7sfb\", \"body\": \"You can. But if you\'re inviting more than a few women, we encourage you to find a co-facilitator or small team. It’s a significant commitment, and it’s wonderful to share the experience, carry the load, and cover each other in prayer. If you invite someone to join you, ask God who that should be, and ensure you’re aligned in heart and vision.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx7x2x\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Do I need to follow the provided schedule?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx81xf\", \"body\": \"Yes. For the 4-day retreat, please follow the schedule and use the videos exactly as provided. This ensures that every woman attending a Captivating Retreat—no matter where she is in the world—receives the same transformative message, session by session.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx85q1\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How soon should I start planning?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx89wh\", \"body\": \"Ideally, begin 90-days before your retreat to allow time for invitations, lodging, and preparation. Trust God with the timing—he will make a way.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx8e8h\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What about meals?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx8mpn\", \"body\": \"The key is to keep it simple. Meals and snacks shouldn’t pull the women—or you—away from the retreat experience. If prep or cleanup takes more than 10 minutes, invite someone not attending to help behind the scenes.\\n\\nHere are a few easy options:\\n- catering (some venues offer this)\\n- takeout or delivery\\n- prepped sandwich or salad bars\\n- grocery platters or grab-and-go items\\n- potluck-style (ask each attendee to bring something)\\n\\nThe goal is simplicity and ease, not perfection.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx8qqx\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Should I charge women to attend?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx8sov\", \"body\": \"The content and materials are provided at no cost, so the only expenses would be food or a rented venue. You may choose to cover those costs yourself or split them among attendees with a small fee. Either is fine—just be transparent up front so women know what to expect.\\n\\nWild at Heart Ministries is not able to provide scholarships for independently hosted retreats. If a woman expresses financial need and that is not something your event can support, you might encourage her to explore support through her local church, such as women’s ministry or benevolence funds, as a possible avenue for help.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx8wvr\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How do I access the video sessions?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx91b0\", \"body\": \"Go to the [**Dropbox folder**](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/v9a0ugwqz1m9hprfkwrqm/AD-rxlpAMWOB18eYshzPWrU?rlkey=utcgn163skz4uo0o1go6ob3he&e=1&dl=0) with all the video sessions. (You don’t need a Dropbox account to access them). We suggest you download videos ahead of time, because Wi-Fi at retreat sites can be unreliable.\\n\\nYou\'ll need\\n- a computer with adequate storage (We recommend 200 GB of free space to download and run all video files smoothly.)\\n- a TV or projector (connected via HDMI or compatible cable) that allows everyone to see and hear the sessions clearly\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx98bc\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How do I create a safe space when facilitating a Captivating Retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx9b7i\", \"body\": \"Sacred space isn’t built through logistics alone—it’s created by the posture of our hearts. These are the things that matter most:\\n\\n- **Confidentiality is everything.** What’s shared at the retreat stays there. No exceptions unless someone gives express permission. This protects every heart.\\n- **Don’t offer advice, offer an ear.** Resist the urge to give counsel. This is a place for the women to hear from God, so leave room for him to speak and move.\\n- **Cover it all in prayer** before, during, and after the retreat. We also encourage you to invite intercessors to come alongside you, people you trust to pray for you and your group throughout the retreat.\\n- **Persevere.** You are doing Kingdom work, and hearts will be set free. There will be opposition, but don’t lose heart. Stay in prayer and allow God to lead. He will give you everything you need.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx9g3f\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What if someone needs emotional support during the retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx9jo5\", \"body\": \"Sometimes the content stirs deep emotion. Be prepared with tissues and a kind presence. You’re not expected to counsel—simply listen and guide each woman back to Jesus, our Healer. \\n\\nRemember, your role isn’t to be responsible for another’s healing—Jesus will come for her. Still, if you’d like to learn more about walking with others, this [**Four Streams Clinic**](https://wildatheart.org/media/four-streams-clinic/01-the-four-streams) from John Eldredge offers a thoughtful perspective and helpful tools.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx9r0j\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What if something goes wrong—technical issues, illness, weather?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzx9v3a\", \"body\": \"Don’t panic. Pray, walk with God, and adapt as needed. Trust that God is still leading, and he is in this. Every Captivating Retreat unfolds uniquely, and he’ll meet you right where you are, just as you need him to.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzx9yeq\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Can teenagers attend?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzxa3bk\", \"body\": \"The content is designed for adult women, but mature older teens (17+) may attend at your discretion. Just consider whether the content is appropriate for where they are emotionally.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"mkzxa7tm\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What if someone needs to leave early?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"mkzxabvx\", \"body\": \"Encourage women to commit to the four days upon registration. However, we understand that life happens, so if someone must leave early, bless her and release her without worry.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"mkzxak8c\", \"body\": \"Dear one, thank you for saying yes. Thank you for fighting for the hearts of women in your world.\\n\\nYou are rare. You are radiant. And your obedience is opening doors for the Spirit of God to move.\\n\\nWith love, blessing, and gratitude,\\n**Stasi and the Captivating team**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": false}]}]}, {\"id\": \"mnqc7kv4\", \"body\": \"---\\n\\nDear one, thank you for saying yes. Thank you for fighting for the hearts of women in your world.\\n\\nYou are rare. You are radiant. And your obedience is opening doors for the Spirit of God to move.\\n\\nWith love, blessing, and gratitude,\\n**Stasi and the Captivating team**\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]',NULL,'Invitation','About','Schedule','FAQs',NULL,'## INVITATION\n\n\nThe invitation of the Gospel is to live fully alive and in union with God. To come home to who you truly are—restored by his love, alive in his presence, walking in joy and courage, and offering the strength and beauty that flow from your radiant heart as a woman.\n\nThis goes far beyond duty or pressure. It’s the epic story of God pursuing you, awakening something deep and eternal, because there is something fierce and life-giving inside you. Something essential to God’s heart and to his mission to come and rescue what has been lost.\n\nSo…what if this is God’s invitation to you?\n\nWhat if God is stirring something in your heart and asking you to explore this with him—to pray, to listen, and to follow his lead as you consider creating a space for women to encounter his love and remember who they truly are?\n\nYou don’t have to have all the answers or any special experience.\n\nBut if your heart is stirring, if something inside you whispers _maybe_, then we invite you to walk with God and explore what it might look like to host a Captivating Retreat.\n\n- It will be holy.\n- It will be tender.\n- It will be beautiful.\n- It will require something of you.\n\nAnd Jesus will meet you every step of the way.\n\n---\n\n**A Woman’s Deepest Longings**\n\nWritten on the heart of every woman are these longings:\n\n- to unveil a beauty all her own\n- to play an irreplaceable role in a grand adventure\n- to be romanced\n\nThese longings aren’t shallow or unrealistic dreams. They are echoes of who God created you to be. \n\nA woman must know she is seen. That she is delighted in. That she is chosen, cherished, and called into a story far bigger than herself.\n\nAnd as her heart awakens, she begins to see, honor, and want to call up the beauty in others. Our journey is not just about discovering who we are; it’s about learning to love and stand with one another with grace, strength, and compassion.\n\nThis is why we offer the Captivating Retreat—a journey into the welcoming heart of God to uncover the deep, restored places of our feminine souls.','## ABOUT THE RETREAT\n\n### What Is the Captivating Retreat?\n\nThe **Captivating Retreat** is a **video-led experience** hosted by women like you around the world—in homes, cabins, or retreat centers—in partnership with Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team.\n\nYou offer the invitation, and we’ll provide the resources designed to carry the weight for you:\n\n- video sessions led by Stasi and the Captivating team\n- the full 4-day retreat schedule (a step-by-step guide)\n- guidance videos from our Wild at Heart women’s team\n- access to a private online facilitator community of women hosting worldwide\n\n\nWhen you register your retreat, you’ll gain full access to these resources. You’ll also choose whether your retreat is\n\n- private (by invitation only), or\n- public (listed on our site so others may register to join)\n\n---\n\n### A Note on Expectations (at a Glance)\n\nIf you feel God stirring your heart to host a retreat, we’ll walk you through all the details once you register. For now, here’s a brief summary of what’s involved:\n\n**Commit to the full experience** \n\n- The full 4-day retreat typically runs Thursday evening through Sunday noon.\n- Please plan for the full time. This message unfolds intentionally, each session building upon the last.\n\n**Lead by hosting**\n\n- The content is fully provided to you, for free, through video sessions. \n- You don’t need to teach, just provide a space, follow the guide, and allow God to move.\n\n**Create a distraction-free environment**\n\n- Whether you’re at a cabin, VRBO, or your living room, the space should invite peace so women can step away for this set-apart time and meet with God uninterrupted.\n\n**Invite women into this sacred experience**\n\n- Groups can be large or small. What matters most is a safe, sacred space where hearts can open and God can move.\n\n**Let God meet you too**\n\n- Let your heart be open to what God has for you in this. Remember, this is an invitation to do this with him. \n\n---\n\n### The Larger Story—and Your Beautiful Role\n\nOver the past two decades, Captivating Retreats led by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team have guided more than **20,000 women** from around the world. These are not events. They are sacred encounters with God, and women leave forever changed, because something deep within is awakened and restored.\n\nEvery woman carries wounds as well as lies that say she’s too much, not enough, or somehow not quite right. But that is not the story God is telling. He is rewriting our stories with truth and inviting us to partner with him in that—not as an afterthought, but as a vital ally in his mission to heal and restore the hearts of others.\n\nAs Catherine of Siena wrote, “Become who you are meant to be, and you will set the world on fire.”\n\nDo you feel God asking you to take a chance on him? To bring this message to your community, to create space for women to encounter God, receive his love, and recover their true hearts?\n\nIf so…let’s begin.','[{\"id\": \"22186d0d\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## SCHEDULE OVERVIEW \\n\\nA detailed schedule will be provided upon your registration.\\n\\nDay One\\n\\n- Session 1 – Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart\\n\\nDay Two\\n\\n- Session 2 – The Larger Story\\n- Session 3 – Fallen Eve\\n- Session 4 – Healing the Wound\\n- Session 5 – Your New Name\\n\\nDay Three\\n\\n- Session 6 – The Enemy of Your Heart\\n- Session 7 – The Great Romance\\n- Session 8 – Loving Men\\n- Session 9 – Come Closer\\n\\nDay Four\\n\\n- Session 10 – Your Irreplaceable Role\\n- Session 11 – Where Do We Go from Here?\"}]','[{\"id\": \"lzjwybsy\", \"answer\": \"Not at all. You don’t need to be a speaker, teacher, or counselor. You just need to love Jesus, have a desire to encourage women, and say yes to creating a space for God to move. If he’s inviting you, trust that he will equip you.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to be “qualified” to lead?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjwysjq\", \"answer\": \"You can, but if you plan to invite more than a few women, we encourage you to find a co-facilitator or team. It is a big commitment, and it’s wonderful to be able to share the experience, carry the load, and cover each other in prayer. Should you choose a co-leader or team, we encourage you to prayerfully consider who and make sure you\'re aligned in heart and vision.\", \"question\": \"Can I facilitate this alone?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjwzmx6\", \"answer\": \"Both formats offer powerful teaching, worship, and space to meet with God. Both invite women to step away from their worlds so they can receive his love and walk with him into the \\\"more\\\" he has for them, in order to recapture their whole hearts.\\n\\n- The 4-day retreat is the full 4-Day Captivating Retreat filmed in the mountains in Colorado. It is the retreat that Wild at Heart has been offering for over two decades.\\n- The 1-day retreat is a condensed, beautifully crafted introduction to the message of _Captivating_—perfect for women who are new to the message or whose season of life doesn’t allow for a multi-day retreat.\\n\\nYou’ll be able to choose which retreat when you resgister. We’ll then give you access to the sessions, worship lists, schedules, and other detailed information for whichever you choose, all for free.\", \"question\": \"What’s the difference between the 1-day and 4-day retreat?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx1ejj\", \"answer\": \"If your retreat will be listed publicly on our website, yes. We ask that you follow the schedule exactly as laid out, including using the provided videos for the session teaching (you’ll receive the detailed schedule upon registration). This ensures that every woman attending a Captivating Retreat—wherever she is in the world—receives the same powerful experience, session by session.\\n\\nThat said, if God is leading you to host the retreat on a different schedule, we honor that. You are welcome to adapt the format to fit a weekend, multiple evenings, or even weekly gatherings. If so, just be sure to select “private listing” when registering. This way, you’ll still get all the facilitator resources without being listed on the public map.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to follow the provided schedule?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx23fo\", \"answer\": \"The key is to keep it simple. Mealtime shouldn’t pull women—or you—away from the retreat experience. If prep or cleanup takes more than 10 minutes, ask someone not attending to help.\\n\\nHere are a few easy options:\\n\\n- catering (some venues offer this)\\n- takeout or delivery\\n- prepped sandwich or salad bars\\n- grocery platters or grab-and-go items\\n- potluck-style (ask each attendee to bring something)\\n\\nThe goal is simplicity and ease, not perfection.\", \"question\": \"What about meals?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx34hy\", \"answer\": \"We are so happy to provide the video content and downloadable materials at no cost to you, so the only expenses should be meals and your venue (if you’re renting a space). Some hosts choose to absorb these costs. Others split them among attendees with a small registration fee.\\n\\nEither way is fine. Just be transparent upfront so your attendees know what to expect.\", \"question\": \"Should I charge women to attend?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx3j3u\", \"answer\": \"After you register, you’ll receive access to a Dropbox folder with all the video sessions. (You don’t need a Dropbox account.) We suggest you download videos ahead of time, because Wi-Fi at retreat sites can be unreliable.\\n\\nYou\'ll need\\n\\n- a computer with adequate storage (We recommend having 200 GB of free space available to download and run all video files smoothly.)\\n- a TV or projector (connected via HDMI or compatible cable) that allows everyone to see and hear the sessions clearly\", \"question\": \"How do I access the video sessions?\"}, {\"id\": \"mkzwws9o\", \"answer\": \"Sacred space isn’t built through logistics alone—it’s created by the posture of our hearts. These are the things that matter most:\\n\\n- Confidentiality is everything. What’s shared at the retreat stays there—no exceptions unless someone gives express permission. This protects every heart.\\n- Don’t offer advice, offer an ear. Resist the urge to offer advice or counseling. This is a place for the women to hear from God, so leave room for him to speak and move.\\n- Cover it all in prayer before, during, and after the retreat. We also encourage you to invite intercessors to come alongside you, people you trust to pray for you and your group throughout the retreat.\\n- Persevere. You are doing Kingdom work, and hearts will be set free. There will be opposition. Don’t lose heart. Stay in prayer and allow God to lead, and he will give you everything you need.\", \"question\": \"How do I create a safe space when facilitating a Captivating Retreat?\"}]','square-logo-4d-cap-rt-(2).png','4k-horiz-logo-capretreat.jpg',NULL,'https://vimeo.com/1012088113/dd6e0407ea','[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-04-09 10:38:29','Sint ullam ut dignissimos quos suscipit.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vpfy8n\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/dryb91eoax3x2bn/AABPMgA-drvN4G6M4uBQ5Kyfa?dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'f42e74d0-d4d4-44d9-a6d3-a8cd9b9208b0'),
	(4,0,'Expected number of attendees','retreat','retreat','Becoming A King Retreat',NULL,8,NULL,NULL,'The Becoming a King retreat is a transformational men’s event curated and distilled over decades by Morgan Snyder and the Wild at Heart team.',NULL,1,'men','becoming-a-king-retreat','## What is a Becoming a King Retreat?\n\nThe Becoming a King retreat is a transformational men’s event curated and distilled over decades by Morgan Snyder and the Wild at Heart team. Through powerful video sessions, interactive story groups, and a guided rhythm of engagement, reflection, and relationship, the BAK retreat immerses you and the men in your community in this transforming message.\n\n\n## What can I receive through a Becoming a King retreat?\n\nEvery boy knows he was made to be powerful. Yet the headlines often confirm what we know too well from our own stories: the anguished consequences of masculine power gone awry.\n\nMasculinity is in need of restoration. But what is the way, and how can we find it?\n\nThe Becoming a King retreat provides a sacred context to explore the path and process of becoming transformed men God can gladly entrust with power and the care of his Kingdom. During this experience, you will have the opportunity to pull back 50 yards from the pressures of the front lines, explore and share your story, carefully identify and tend to your wounds, recover what makes you come alive, rekindle curiosity, joy, and hope, and strengthen your soul for the seasons ahead within a multi-generational masculine environment that connects older, wiser guides with men who thirst for pervasive transformation. \n\nThe Father Heart of God is pursuing you, inviting you to become the man you were created to be. \n\nReceive the good news: you are not alone, and it’s not up to you. All you have to do is say yes and dive in.\n\nJoin us as we engage the path and process of masculine initiation and restoration together.\n\nAs thousands of the brave like-hearted men who have gone before us can attest, engaging the Becoming a King retreat will be one of the most rewarding risks you have ever taken.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0vqohqg\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vqok9a\", \"body\": \"Start by watching this short message from Morgan Snyder.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0wtiiiz\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/672548799\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqr2k8\", \"body\": \"**Welcome to a fellowship of kings.** \\n\\nWell done. You’ve found yourself on the narrow path, my brother. You are among the few of a growing tribe of like-hearted and maturing kings. Together, let’s dive in.\\n\\nBy choosing to lead a Becoming a King retreat (BAKR), you are joining a global fellowship of men choosing masculine initiation as the interpretive grid and narrative arc for every moment of their lives. \\n\\nYour role is both simple and profound, requiring vulnerability, humility, and deep strength.\\n\\nThis event is for your heart as well as the participants. \\n\\nRest assured that it is not up to you: your mission is to carry the message but not the man. God will come through—it\'s what he loves to do.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vqrw1l\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Before Your Retreat\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vqs3bp\", \"body\": \"Anyone can facilitate a BAKR if he has a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with our team to follow the time-tested guidelines we have laid out for you. There are no prerequisites for leading or participating. However, reading [Wild at Heart](https://www.amazon.com/dp/1400225264/ref=cm_sw_r_as_gl_api_gl_i_B97R8SZXB4DK0YGQ82GG) and [Becoming a King](https://www.amazon.com/dp/0785232117/ref=cm_sw_r_as_gl_api_gl_i_NRNY6QV3XFSZ0TT6DKVJ) will benefit you immensely as you prepare your own heart. As a leader, you agree to offer the full four-day BAKR experience, adhere to the detailed guidelines, and neither add to nor subtract from the retreat content. You also agree to provide feedback so we can continue to improve BAKR for future events.\\n\\n**Choose Your Date**\\nImportant: BAKR requires four days. (Day 1 begins in the afternoon and Day 4 concludes around noon.)\\n\\n**Choose Your Men**\\nThis content works for as few as four men and as many as 400. It’ll work for men from 18 to 80. The most important thing is that the men are thirsty for God and are going to risk true authenticity.\\n\\n**Choose Your Location**\\nThe BAKR is an immersive experience. It’s your responsibility to choose and curate a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility that is removed from the pulls and pressures of everyday life. As you consider your location, it is important to bear in mind the “no digital technology” boundary of the retreat. \\n\\n**Invite Your Guys**\\nThe following materials can be found in the [marketing folder of the downloads section:](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/m0xj4zpy52f3v4zp06n52/ADv1PH-dYpsWTF5zQGEQqC0?rlkey=0ao9dbajb8olmt0wvn2dn7ty2&e=1&dl=0)\\n\\n- PDF poster \\n- PDF flier\\n- Video trailer \\n- NOTE: If you register your BAKR as a public event, we will promote it through our websites as a “featured event” in related searches people make in our Allies Network.\\n\\nWhen you agree to facilitate a BAKR, you\'re agreeing to maintain the look and feel of Wild at Heart/Become Good Soil events—including the integrity and use of the BAKR logo. lf you plan to create promotional materials beyond what Wild at Heart provides, it\'s important that you…\\n\\n1. only use the BAKR logo provided, without adding to or taking away any design elements\\n2. not create your own BAKR logo or hybrid design\\n3. remember that, although this is a local gathering, your event is part of a larger movement that has an established look and feel.\\n\\nThanks for helping us stay true to every aspect of the BAKR at your facilitated event, including the use of the Becoming a King name and logo.\\n\\n**Get Yourself Ready**\\nJesus reminds us, when going into a mission, to “travel light. You are the equipment.” Your masculine soul matters. Read [Becoming a King](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king) on your own before the event. Spend time immersing yourself not only in the book but also in the [BAKR notetaking guide.](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/idehdtq8wdy9e3clgsqie/BAK-Retreat-Notetaking-Guide-2nd-Edition-MASTER-Updated-2025.03.pdf?rlkey=hcgra1h850h55s3ri1qenkwt2&e=1&dl=0) (You can choose to print the notetaking guide in color or in black and white.) Open your heart to what God is up to in you. The power isn’t in the book—it’s in the hearts of men consented to the Father and his initiation of their masculine soul. Also watch all the video sessions of the BAKR so you are familiar with what the men attending will experience during your event. You can find those [here](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/hakqv8u9mku12zg95svvz/ABPBTxcwnsnrbWhdC9hQkv8?rlkey=d1ting3pqjrsdj8lwvoltfc4m&st=mvi8uod3&dl=0). Finally, you’ll want to begin praying through and sitting in the BAKR Daybreak Prayer, which is also found in the back of the [notetaking guide](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/idehdtq8wdy9e3clgsqie/BAK-Retreat-Notetaking-Guide-2nd-Edition-MASTER-Updated-2025.03.pdf?rlkey=hcgra1h850h55s3ri1qenkwt2&e=1&dl=0). This will be immensely helpful as you root your soul in God and his Kingdom in preparation for the retreat. \\n\\n**A few more items to consider before your Becoming a King retreat:**\\n\\nYou’ll Need to Provide a Pocket Knife for Each Participant\\nThe retreat culminates in bestowing a pocket knife on each participant. We’ve worked out a pro-deal with DLT Trading to source our custom engraved knives at a great value. You can find those bulk-discount knives as you scroll down [this page.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/knife/)\\n\\n**A Note About Participants**\\nThis retreat is not targeted for a particular age of men but rather for a pivotal stage of masculine development through which every man must pass. In the earlier years, this retreat targeted men 25 to 45. But we have learned that Becoming a King has much more to do with the parts of each man in need of masculine initiation. Regardless of an attendee’s biological age, look for how God is surfacing parts within his soul in fresh need of fathering, initiation, and care at a variety of stages of development.\\n\\n**Chimney Sweep**\\nDallas Willard once said, “The most important thing about a man is not what he does. It is who he becomes.” As men, we have so few opportunities to talk about who we are apart from what we do. At the Becoming a King retreat, we are committed to flipping this script and centering the entire experience around who we are. To that end, we agree to withhold what we “do” for a living. Instead, for the duration of the retreat, we stack hands on one answer to the question of “What do you do?” Our shared answer is simply, “I’m a chimney sweep.” Advise your attendees that anytime they need to talk about their work as a context for their masculine initiation, be sure to refer to it as a chimney sweep (Ex.: “So there I am, at my chimney sweep job, when my boss comes to me and tells me I am failing miserably….”). The same goes for you and all your facilitators. Focusing on who we are apart from the specifics of our livelihood is foundational to digging deep into our masculine hearts; committing to the “chimney sweep” guideline is vital to this end. It is your responsibility as the leader to communicate the heart of this guideline at the beginning of your event and reinforce it throughout.\\n\\n**A Note About Language**\\nSome of the film clips and stories during the BAKR contain strong or explicit language. Including this language is not gratuitous but motivated by our commitment to honesty, authenticity, and vulnerability. The mission of Becoming a King is to connect the heart of every man with the heart of God, and our hope is that occasionally including strong language helps to this end. We ask for your grace in this category, and if a man finds this choice offensive, this retreat is probably not for him at this time.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vqwej9\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Retreat Schedule\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vqwkl8\", \"body\": \"All sessions will be taught by Morgan Snyder via video. (Remember your commitment to neither add nor take away from the content/schedule.)\\n\\n**Technology-Free Zone** – In order to create the best possible environment for mens’ hearts to show up, make your retreat a digital technology-free zone. First, establish an emergency contact number for your BAKR. Please provide that number to all attendees before the retreat and again when they arrive. Then cast the vision of this tech-free zone for your attendees. Remind them that this event is an invitation to let their masculine hearts take center stage, shut out the sea of distractions, and allow their souls to surface and be cared for. Assure them that their Father is present and eager to connect personally with them, and this retreat is the next great chance to receive, distraction-free. Then, invite your attendees to prepare to secure all phones, smartwatches, etc., for all four days in the safekeeping of a designated leader (we find it helpful to assign someone on your leadership team to keep all devices in a secure location). Set the men at ease; assure them they can be reached as needed. Encourage your attendees to call or text anyone who needs the emergency number so that they can confidently surrender their technology. Compassionately normalize that this might feel really tough or uncomfortable. Make sure the emergency contact number for your retreat is manned 24 hours a day. Finally, remember to prioritize the spirit of the law over the letter of the law when enforcing the tech-free zone. It’s not worth kicking a man out if he won’t comply. It’s his heart we are after. Do everything in your power to stay winsome and kind around the challenge of surrendering digital devices, remembering we all are addicted to our technology, and detox is never pretty.\\n \\n**BAKR Session Overview**\\n\\n1. Becoming Powerful\\n2. Becoming the Man You Were Born to Be\\n3. Becoming a Son \\n4. Becoming a Generalist\\n5. Becoming Deep Roots\\n6. Becoming Like-Hearted\\n7. Becoming a King\\n8. Closing Counsel and Where We Go from Here\\n\\n**Eight Video Sessions are provided.** Please do not add to or subtract from these video sessions. They have been prayerfully choreographed to shepherd the hearts of the participants through the retreat. Note that Sessions 3 and 4 are designed to be paused during the content for a 10-minute break to use the restroom, get a drink, or catch your breath. \\n\\n**Becoming a King Retreat Master Schedule** – This is included in the front of the notetaking guide.\\n\\n**Using Facilitators to Host Story Groups** – This is optional. If you are hosting your first Becoming a King retreat and do not have seasoned leaders, the story groups work fine without facilitators. If, however, you have more mature men among your leadership circle who have been through the material and experience themselves, we recommend you add a facilitator role to your story groups. If you are using facilitators, see below:\\n\\n- **Facilitator’s Training** – This is an optional training video to be played in a Facilitator Training session on Day 1 of your retreat BEFORE the participants arrive. This is not to be shared with participants. This is only for leaders and facilitators. If you have facilitators, watch and process the Facilitator Training session together before your participants arrive at the retreat.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqyg6n\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/672503880\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqyi9n\", \"body\": \"- **Consecrating a Men’s Event** – Whether you are leading the BAKR with a team, with facilitators, or on your own, we strongly encourage you to consecrate the event in prayer. Watch this short video from the Wild at Heart team for some simple training on Consecrating a Men’s Event.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqyrws\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1008207504\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqyv2q\", \"body\": \"- **Facilitator Touch Points** – During each of the “Time with God” opportunities on the schedule for the duration of the retreat, facilitators and the leader(s) of the event will circle up. This is a confidential time to share what is surfacing among attendees and within the story groups. It’s a chance to offer encouragement, ask for prayer, and be strengthened as a community of guides throughout the retreat. \\n- **Facilitator Closing** – Once all participants have left the retreat on the last day, we strongly encourage facilitators and leaders to circle up one last time. It’s a chance to share stories of what God did during the event. Use the time to pray, releasing all the men and all the unfinished work in their lives to God as you make the transition from the mission to home.\\n\\n**Story Groups** – (These are explained in more detail in the Facilitator Training session. Leaders should all watch this video.) \\n\\nEvery participant will have the privilege of being part of a Becoming a King retreat story group. Facilitators for these groups are optional. If you have mature leaders, assigning facilitators to each story group is recommended. Story groups should have no more than four participants and no fewer than three (not including facilitators). In addition to a check-in each morning, there are three story group gatherings scheduled during the retreat. Each man gets one full hour to share his story and receive prayer in response. These story groups are explained to the participants at the end of Session 2. Facilitators do not share their stories in the story groups. If attendees are interested in hearing a facilitator’s story, that sharing can take place over meals or during free time.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqzojf\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/672503880/\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqzqhl\", \"body\": \"**Morning Story Group Prayer** – Days 2, 3, and 4 all begin with a chance for the men of each story group to connect and pray together. The goal is to both consecrate the day and also to have a check-in to ensure that no guy is struggling on his own or stays isolated. The retreat leader will announce the story groups over breakfast on Day 2, and the first story-group gathering for prayer and check-in will follow immediately after that breakfast. Days 3 and 4 will begin with story-group prayer and check-in, then move straight into breakfast.\\n\\n**Time with God** – Every session for Day 1, Day 2, and Day 3 concludes with a 30-minute time with God. These times with God are explained at the conclusion of Session 1. Reflection questions are presented via the video at the end of each session and included in the note-taking guide as well. These dedicated windows of silence provide each man with an opportunity to share conversation with God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the sessions. They are the centerpiece of the retreat, and you will need to help preserve and protect them.\\n\\n**Story Group One** – This will take place the morning of Day 2 after Session 2. Story-group training for ALL participants is included at the end of the Session 2 video.\\n\\n**Free Time** – You’ll notice consistent blocks of free time built into the retreat. This is not space to add more content or a formal activity. Instead, it is an intentional space for each man to discern what would be best for his soul. Maybe he needs rest. Maybe he needs solitude. Maybe he needs to process what is surfacing in his heart with other men. Invite the men to follow God’s invitation to personally and courageously choose what they need most during these times.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr0r6w\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr0s8w\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Becoming a King retreat Sessions\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr0zf8\", \"body\": \"Here’s an overview of the sessions:\\n\\n- Session 1 – Becoming Powerful\\n- Session 2 – Becoming the Man You Were Born to Be\\n- Session 3 – Becoming a Son\\n- Session 4 – Becoming a Generalist\\n- Session 5 – Becoming Deep Roots \\n- Session 6 – Becoming Like-Hearted\\n- Session 7 – Becoming a King\\n- Session 8 – Closing Counsel and Where We Go from Here\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vr1jtx\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"BAKR - Day 1\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr1ot6\", \"body\": \"5:00 pm — 6:00 pm     \\nDinner\\n\\n6:00 pm — 7:00 pm     \\nSession 1 – Becoming Powerful - Part 1\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr211t\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1035956506\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr23au\", \"body\": \"7:00 pm — 7:15 pm     \\nBreak \\n\\n7:15 pm - 8:15 pm             \\nSession 1 - Becoming Powerful - Part 2\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69tpgbr\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1035965491\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69tpn63\", \"body\": \"8:15 pm - 8:45 pm\\nTime With God (Covenant of Silence) \\n\\n8:45 pm \\nFree Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vr28r4\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"BAKR - Day 2\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr2d3q\", \"body\": \"7:00 am — 7:30 am     \\nLeadership Only Touchpoint/Prayer\\n\\n8:00 am - 8:30 am\\nBreakfast - Story Group Assignments Announced\\n\\n8:30 am - 9:30 am\\nSession 2 - Becoming True - Part 1\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr2ryr\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1035967088\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr2tr9\", \"body\": \"9:30 am - 9:45 am \\nBreak\\n\\n9:45 am - 10:30 am \\nSession 2 - Becoming True - Part 2\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr312k\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1035968476\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr34bd\", \"body\": \"10:30 am - 11:00 am \\nTime With God (Covenant of Silence) \\n\\n11:00 am - 12:30 pm\\nStory Group One\\n\\n12:30 pm - 1:00 pm \\nLunch\\n\\n1:00 pm - 2:30 pm \\nFree Time\\n\\n2:30 pm - 3:45 pm \\nSession 3 - Becoming a Son\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr3eak\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1039786177\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr3ic0\", \"body\": \"3:45 pm - 4:15 pm \\nTime with God (covenant of Silence)\\n\\n4:15 pm - 5:45 pm \\nStory Group 2\\n\\n5:45 pm - 6:45 pm \\nDinner\\n\\n6:45 pm - 8:15 pm \\nSession 4 - Becoming a Generalist\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69tykt2\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1038429177\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69tymtl\", \"body\": \"8:15 pm - 8:45 pm \\nTime with God (Covenant of Silence) \\n\\n8:45 pm \\nFree Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vr3pus\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"BAKR - Day 3\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr3umw\", \"body\": \"7:00 am \\nLeadership Only Touchpoint/Prayer\\n\\n8:00 am - 8:30 am \\nBreakfast with Story Groups\\n\\n8:30 am - 10:00 am\\nSession 5 - Becoming Good Soil\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr43dx\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1038429951\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr44wf\", \"body\": \"10:00 am - 10:30 am \\nTime With God (Covenant of Silence) \\n\\n10:30 am - 12:00 pm \\nStory Group 3\\n\\n12:00 pm - 12:30 pm \\nLunch\\n\\n12:30 pm - 4:00 pm \\nFree Time\\n\\n4:00 pm - 5:00 pm \\nSession 6 - Becoming Deep Roots\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr4bir\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1035974382\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr4ebq\", \"body\": \"5:00 pm - 5:30 pm \\nTime With God (Covenant of Silence)\\n(Note: Leader distributes knives to facilitators to have for bestowing tomorrow) \\n\\n5:30 pm - 6:30 pm \\nDinner\\n\\n6:30 pm - 8:00 pm \\nSession 7 - The Company Men\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr4jy3\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1039689195\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr4p9e\", \"body\": \"8:00 pm \\nFree Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vr4znc\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"BAKR - Day 4\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr540f\", \"body\": \"7:00 am \\nLeadership Only Touchpoint/Prayer\\n\\n8:00 am - 8:30 am \\nBreakfast with Story Groups\\n\\n8:30 am - 9:45 am\\nSession 8 - Becoming a King\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr5cib\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1039693155\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr5inc\", \"body\": \"9:45 am - 10:15 am\\nBestowing Ceremony in Story Groups\\n\\n10:15 am - 11:15 am\\nSession 9 - Closing Counsel\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vr5wqv\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1039831701\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69ua26i\", \"body\": \"11:20 am - 11:30 am \\nBreak\\n\\n11:30 am - 11:45 am \\nSession 10 - Where We Go From Here\\n\\nFacilitator Schedule Note: IF Facilitators are being utilized (this is optional), they will gather as a team privately for a touch point each time participants head out for a “Time with God.” They will also conclude the event with a final touch point after participants have left the retreat. See retreat leader(s) for more details.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vr88gc\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"FAQ\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vr8l5y\", \"body\": \"**What\'s the best way to print out the notetaking guides?**\\nYou can print them out in color, as it is a color document. However, a lot of our allies choose to save money and simply print them out in black and white. \\n\\n**Do you have to attend Wild at Heart BASIC or Boot Camp before attending BAKR?** \\nNo. It helps, but it is not a prerequisite. BAKR is designed as a deep dive into discipleship in the Wild at Heart message, but is also an awesome event for a first-timer who is willing to take the risk and authentically engage with an open heart.\\n\\n**Do you have to attend a Become Good Soil event before attending BAKR?**\\nNo. It helps, but it is not a prerequisite. BAKR is designed as a deep dive into discipleship in the Wild at Heart message, but is also an awesome event for a first-timer who is willing to take the risk and authentically engage with an open heart.\\n\\n**Why doesn’t the schedule include traditional retreat elements like worship or communion?**\\nWe do have worship built in to a few of the morning sessions. Additionally, this is not a typical men\'s event. Trust us on the schedule and format—you’ll understand why later. \\n\\n**Do I need to follow the four-day schedule?**\\nIf you would like to publicly list your BAKR on our website for anyone to find and attend, then yes, we require you to follow the schedule exactly. The reason is that we\'re promoting the BAKR listings on our website to thousands of people each month and guaranteeing that these promoted events will all be led in the same manner. Also, through more than a decade of experience, we’ve learned that this schedule works.\\n\\n**What about meals?** \\nChoose simple, ready-made meals. Don’t require prep of the attendees. If prep and cleanup take more than 10 minutes, we recommend having a dedicated person taking care of meals who is not  involved in the event. Meal time—not the sessions—is also the chance to make any “housekeeping announcements.”\\n\\n**Can you facilitate this alone?**\\nYou can, but we encourage you to find a partner or a small team to help. It’s always better to engage this mission with a team if possible.\\n\\n**Should we charge men to attend BAKR?**\\nThis is your choice. However, this event is not intended to be a “for-profit” venture. We provide all the material to you at no charge. Our assumption is that the only additional costs would be meals, knives, and perhaps a facility charge. Some facilitators choose to absorb these costs. Others charge a minimal fee to cover costs. Walk with God.\\n\\n**What’s the best way to show the videos clearly?**\\nFirst, download the videos for free in the downloads section.\\nYou’ll want to use a laptop that has an HDMI output to connect to your TV or projector. \\n\\n**Does attending BAKR count as the BASIC/Boot Camp pre-requisite for the live BGS Intensive?** \\nYes, when you attend BAKR it’s just like attending a Boot Camp or a BASIC. Your attendance at BAKR meets the requirement to attend the live Become Good Soil Intensive.\\n\\n**What\'s a story group?** \\nGreat question. (These are explained in more detail in the Facilitator Training session. Leaders should all watch this video.) Every participant will have the privilege of being a part of a BAKR story group. Facilitators for these groups are optional. If you have mature leaders, assigning facilitators to each story group is recommended. Story groups should have no more than four participants and no fewer than three (not including facilitators). In addition to a check in each morning, there are three story-group gatherings scheduled during the retreat. Each man gets one full hour to share his story and receive prayer in response. These story groups are explained to the participants at the end of Session 2. Facilitators do not share their stories in the story groups. If attendees are interested in hearing a facilitator’s story, that sharing can take place over meals or during free time.\\n\\n**Do the story groups have to have a formal leader or facilitator?** \\nFacilitators for these groups are optional. If you have mature leaders, assigning facilitators to each story group is recommended. It is not essential.\\n\\n**Is there an age requirement for participating in a BAKR?** \\nNo. It is recommended that no man under 18 years of age participate. This retreat is not targeted for a particular age of man but rather for a stage of masculine development through which every man must pass. In the earlier years, this retreat targeted men 25 to 45. But we have learned this deep dive into Becoming a King has much more to do with the parts of each man in need of masculine initiation. Regardless of an attendee’s biological age, look for how God is surfacing parts within his soul in need of Fathering, initiation, and care at different stages of development.\\n\\n**I see that this is the Becoming a King retreat Second Edition.**\\nIs there access to the First Edition?\\nYes. The first edition was recorded in 2014. The Second edition was released in spring of 2025. You can access the video sessions and the note taking guide here for the first edition.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## WELCOME TO THE FELLOWSHIP OF KINGS\n\nWell done. You’ve found yourself on the narrow path, my brother. You are among the few of a growing tribe of like-hearted and maturing kings. Together, let’s dive in.\n\nBy choosing to lead a Becoming a King retreat (BAKR), you are joining a global fellowship of men choosing masculine initiation as the interpretive grid and narrative arc for every moment of their lives. \n\nYour role is both simple and profound, requiring vulnerability, humility, and deep strength.\n\nThis event is for your heart as well as the participants. \n\nRest assured that it is not up to you: your mission is to carry the message but not the man. God will come through—it\'s what he loves to do. \n\n**How it works**\n\nA detailed schedule and all of the materials necessary will be available in the resources section after completing registration. In the registration process, you can choose whether your event is public (open to anyone interested in attending) or private (a private event you’re hosting by invitation only). While some BAK retreats are most effective as a private event (therefore unsearchable) to serve a select fellowship of men who are already doing life together, we strongly recommend making your event searchable so we can promote your event at WildAtHeart.org and BecomingAKing.com and help local men find you.\n\nBy registering your event, you not only access all the material and resources you need to make your event successful, you also connect with our team so we can offer you more unique support, partnership, and exclusive opportunities along the way.','## Before your Becoming a King retreat\n\nAnyone can facilitate a BAKR if he has a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with our team to follow the time-tested guidelines we have laid out for you. There are no prerequisites for leading or participating. However, reading [Wild at Heart](https://www.amazon.com/dp/1400225264/ref=cm_sw_r_as_gl_api_gl_i_B97R8SZXB4DK0YGQ82GG) and Becoming a King [Becoming a King](https://www.amazon.com/dp/0785232117/ref=cm_sw_r_as_gl_api_gl_i_NRNY6QV3XFSZ0TT6DKVJ) will benefit you immensely as you prepare your own heart. As a leader, you agree to offer the full four-day BAKR experience, adhere to the detailed guidelines, and neither add to nor subtract from the retreat content. You also agree to provide feedback so we can continue to improve BAKR for future events.\n\n\n## Choose Your Date\nImportant: BAKR requires four days. (Day 1 begins in the afternoon and Day 4 concludes around noon.)\n\n## Choose Your Men\nThis content works for as few as four men and as many as 400. It’ll work for men from 18 to 80. The most important thing is that the men are thirsty for God and are going to risk true authenticity.\n\n## Choose Your Location\nThe BAKR is an immersive experience. It’s your responsibility to choose and curate a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility that is removed from the pulls and pressures of everyday life. As you consider your location, it is important to bear in mind the “no digital technology” boundary of the retreat. \n\n## Invite Your Guys\nThe following materials can be found in the resources section after registration:\n\n- PDF poster \n- PDF flier\n- Video trailer \n- Email invitation templates\n- BAKR logo and graphics\n- NOTE: If you register your BAKR as a public event, we will promote it through our websites as a “featured event” in related searches people make in our Allies Network.\n\nWhen you agree to facilitate a BAKR, you\'re agreeing to maintain the look and feel of Wild at Heart/Become Good Soil events—including the integrity and use of the BAKR logo. If you plan to create promotional materials beyond what Wild at Heart provides, it\'s important that you…\n\n1. only use the BAKR logo provided, without adding to or taking away any design elements\n2. not create your own BAKR logo or hybrid design\n3. remember that, although this is a local gathering, your event is part of a larger movement that has an established look and feel.\n\nThanks for helping us stay true to every aspect of the BAKR at your facilitated event, including the use of the Becoming a King name and logo.\n\n## Get Yourself Ready\nJesus reminds us, when going into a mission, to “travel light. You are the equipment.” Your masculine soul matters. Read [Becoming a King](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king) on your own before the event. Spend time immersing yourself not only in the book but also in the [BAKR notetaking guide](https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/idehdtq8wdy9e3clgsqie/BAK-Retreat-Notetaking-Guide-2nd-Edition-MASTER-Updated-2025.03.pdf?rlkey=hcgra1h850h55s3ri1qenkwt2&e=2&st=8nhrl4rk&dl=0). (You can choose to print the notetaking guide in color or in black and white.) Open your heart to what God is up to in you. The power isn’t in the book—it’s in the hearts of men consented to the Father and his initiation of their masculine soul. Also watch all the video sessions of the BAKR so you are familiar with what the men attending will experience during your event. You can find those in the resources section after registering. Finally, you’ll want to begin praying through and sitting in the BAKR Daybreak Prayer, which is also found in the back of the notetaking guide. This will be immensely helpful as you root your soul in God and his Kingdom in preparation for the retreat. \n\n## A few more items to consider before your Becoming a King retreat:\n\n## You’ll Need to Provide a Pocket Knife for Each Participant\nThe retreat culminates in bestowing a pocket knife on each participant. We’ve worked out a pro-deal with DLT Trading to source our custom engraved knives at a great value. You can find those bulk-discount knives as you scroll down this [page](https://becomegoodsoil.com/knife/).\n\n## A Note About Participants\nThis retreat is not targeted for a particular age of men but rather for a pivotal stage of masculine development through which every man must pass. In the earlier years, this retreat targeted men 25 to 45. But we have learned that Becoming a King has much more to do with the parts of each man in need of masculine initiation. Regardless of an attendee’s biological age, look for how God is surfacing parts within his soul in fresh need of fathering, initiation, and care at a variety of stages of development.\n\n## Chimney Sweep\nDallas Willard once said, “The most important thing about a man is not what he does. It is who he becomes.” As men, we have so few opportunities to talk about who we are apart from what we do. At the Becoming a King retreat, we are committed to flipping this script and centering the entire experience around who we are. To that end, we agree to withhold what we “do” for a living. Instead, for the duration of the retreat, we stack hands on one answer to the question of “What do you do?” Our shared answer is simply, “I’m a chimney sweep.” Advise your attendees that anytime they need to talk about their work as a context for their masculine initiation, be sure to refer to it as a chimney sweep (Ex.: “So there I am, at my chimney sweep job, when my boss comes to me and tells me I am failing miserably….”). The same goes for you and all your facilitators. Focusing on who we are apart from the specifics of our livelihood is foundational to digging deep into our masculine hearts; committing to the “chimney sweep” guideline is vital to this end. It is your responsibility as the leader to communicate the heart of this guideline at the beginning of your event and reinforce it throughout.\n\n## A Note About Language\nSome of the film clips and stories during the BAKR contain strong or explicit language. Including this language is not gratuitous but motivated by our commitment to honesty, authenticity, and vulnerability. The mission of Becoming a King is to connect the heart of every man with the heart of God, and our hope is that occasionally including strong language helps to this end. We ask for your grace in this category, and if a man finds this choice offensive, this retreat is probably not for him at this time.','[{\"id\": \"00e96c55\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## EVENT SCHEDULE \\n\\nAll sessions will be taught by Morgan Snyder via video. (Remember your commitment to neither add nor take away from the content/schedule.)\\n\\nTechnology-Free Zone – In order to create the best possible environment for mens’ hearts to show up, make your retreat a digital technology-free zone. First, establish an emergency contact number for your BAKR. Please provide that number to all attendees before the retreat and again when they arrive. Then cast the vision of this tech-free zone for your attendees. Remind them that this event is an invitation to let their masculine hearts take center stage, shut out the sea of distractions, and allow their souls to surface and be cared for. Assure them that their Father is present and eager to connect personally with them, and this retreat is the next great chance to receive, distraction-free. Then, invite your attendees to prepare to secure all phones, smartwatches, etc., for all four days in the safekeeping of a designated leader (we find it helpful to assign someone on your leadership team to keep all devices in a secure location). Set the men at ease; assure them they can be reached as needed. Encourage your attendees to call or text anyone who needs the emergency number so that they can confidently surrender their technology. Compassionately normalize that this might feel really tough or uncomfortable. Make sure the emergency contact number for your retreat is manned 24 hours a day. Finally, remember to prioritize the spirit of the law over the letter of the law when enforcing the tech-free zone. It’s not worth kicking a man out if he won’t comply. It’s his heart we are after. Do everything in your power to stay winsome and kind around the challenge of surrendering digital devices, remembering we all are addicted to our technology, and detox is never pretty.\\n \\nBAKR Session Overview\\n\\n1. Becoming Powerful\\n2. Becoming the Man You Were Born to Be\\n4. Becoming a Son \\n5. Becoming Good Soil\\n6. Becoming Deep Roots\\n7. Becoming Like-Hearted\\n8. Becoming a King\\n9. Closing Counsel and Where We Go from Here\\n\\nA more in depth schedule, facilitator training, and downloads will be available after registration.\"}]','[{\"id\": \"lzjxp7zp\", \"answer\": \"You can print them out in color, as it is a color document. However, a lot of our allies choose to save money and simply print them out in black and white.\", \"question\": \"What\'s the best way to print out the notetaking guides?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxpc7y\", \"answer\": \"No. It helps, but it is not a prerequisite. BAKR is designed as a deep dive into discipleship in the Wild at Heart message, but is also an awesome event for a first-timer who is willing to take the risk and authentically engage with an open heart.\", \"question\": \"Do you have to attend Wild at Heart BASIC or Boot Camp before attending BAKR?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxploq\", \"answer\": \"No. It helps, but it is not a prerequisite. BAKR is designed as a deep dive into discipleship in the Wild at Heart message, but is also an awesome event for a first-timer who is willing to take the risk and authentically engage with an open heart.\", \"question\": \"Do you have to attend a Become Good Soil event before attending BAKR?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxpxwj\", \"answer\": \"We do have worship built in to a few of the morning sessions. Additionally, this is not a typical men\'s event. Trust us on the schedule and format—you’ll understand why later.\", \"question\": \"Why doesn’t the schedule include traditional retreat elements like worship or communion?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxq8uz\", \"answer\": \"If you would like to publicly list your BAKR on our website for anyone to find and attend, then yes, we require you to follow the schedule exactly. The reason is that we\'re promoting the BAKR listings on our website to thousands of people each month and guaranteeing that these promoted events will all be led in the same manner. Also, through more than a decade of experience, we’ve learned that this schedule works.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to follow the four-day schedule?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxqo0b\", \"answer\": \"Choose simple, ready-made meals. Don’t require prep of the attendees. If prep and cleanup take more than 10 minutes, we recommend having a dedicated person taking care of meals who is not  involved in the event. Meal time—not the sessions—is also the chance to make any “housekeeping announcements.”\", \"question\": \"What about meals?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxqxt4\", \"answer\": \"You can, but we encourage you to find a partner or a small team to help. It’s always better to engage this mission with a team if possible.\", \"question\": \"Can you facilitate this alone?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxrcej\", \"answer\": \"This is your choice. However, this event is not intended to be a “for-profit” venture. We provide all the material to you at no charge. Our assumption is that the only additional costs would be meals, knives, and perhaps a facility charge. Some facilitators choose to absorb these costs. Others charge a minimal fee to cover costs. Walk with God.\", \"question\": \"Should we charge men to attend BAKR?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxrhvc\", \"answer\": \"You’ll want to use a laptop that has an HDMI output to connect to your TV or projector.\", \"question\": \"What’s the best way to show the videos clearly?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxrx2z\", \"answer\": \"Yes, when you attend BAKR it’s just like attending a Boot Camp or a BASIC. Your attendance at BAKR meets the requirement to attend the live Become Good Soil Intensive.\", \"question\": \"Does attending BAKR count as the BASIC/Boot Camp pre-requisite for the live BGS Intensive?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxs7gm\", \"answer\": \"Great question. (These are explained in more detail in the Facilitator Training session. Leaders should all watch this video.) Every participant will have the privilege of being a part of a BAKR story group. Facilitators for these groups are optional. If you have mature leaders, assigning facilitators to each story group is recommended. Story groups should have no more than four participants and no fewer than three (not including facilitators). In addition to a check in each morning, there are four story-group gatherings scheduled during the retreat. Each man gets one full hour to share his story and receive prayer in response. These story groups are explained to the participants at the end of Session 2. Facilitators do not share their stories in the story groups. If attendees are interested in hearing a facilitator’s story, that sharing can take place over meals or during free time.\", \"question\": \"What\'s a story group?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxsgi3\", \"answer\": \"Facilitators for these groups are optional. If you have mature leaders, assigning facilitators to each story group is recommended. It is not essential.\", \"question\": \"Do the story groups have to have a formal leader or facilitator?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjxssm6\", \"answer\": \"No. It is recommended that no man under 18 years of age participate. This retreat is not targeted for a particular age of man but rather for a stage of masculine development through which every man must pass. In the earlier years, this retreat targeted men 25 to 45. But we have learned this deep dive into Becoming a King has much more to do with the parts of each man in need of masculine initiation. Regardless of an attendee’s biological age, look for how God is surfacing parts within his soul in need of Fathering, initiation, and care at different stages of development.\", \"question\": \"Is there an age requirement for participating in a BAKR?\"}]','event_types/c8468f97-8e87-4e39-9b52-26b088415bdb.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-bakr.jpg',NULL,'https://vimeo.com/672457665/d11cf5ea57','[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-11 02:41:19','The Becoming A King Retreat helps men explore their personal story, confront the wounds that shape them, and grow into the kind of man others can rely on for strength and guidance.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vqodc4\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/34qkbabzy505jlsx7lbrb/AB6oDt9uqGbKA5oBNIRxRkg?rlkey=ff0z4ijoj6qivc70zrxwyqi5a&e=1&st=x1reqj1v&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m69ueya9\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/idehdtq8wdy9e3clgsqie/BAK-Retreat-Notetaking-Guide-2nd-Edition-MASTER-Updated-2025.03.pdf?rlkey=hcgra1h850h55s3ri1qenkwt2&e=1&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Download Guide\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'77e67b23-27de-45ba-ad96-99f804465bf2'),
	(5,1,'Expected number of attendees','experience','course','Wild at Heart Experience',NULL,4,NULL,NULL,'The Wild at Heart Experience is a 6-week film series featuring the teaching of John Eldredge and the stories of men pursuing their warrior hearts through God’s invitation of battle, adventure, and beauty.',NULL,1,'men','wild-at-heart-experience','The Wild at Heart Experience is a 6-week film series featuring the teaching of John Eldredge and the stories of men pursuing their warrior hearts through God’s invitation of battle, adventure, and beauty.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0v22oub\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0v23vot\", \"body\": \"Thank you for your willingness to lead your group through Wild at Heart. This film series features the teaching of John Eldredge and the stories of men pursuing their warrior hearts through God\'s invitation of battle, adventure, and beauty. We\'re excited for you to take the men in your community on this journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader’s guide will give you tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\\n\\n**WHAT DOES IT TAKE TO LEAD THIS STUDY?**\\n\\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that’s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several people together who have a hunger for God, want to learn how to get their lives back, and are willing to be open and honest with God and themselves. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don’t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart, a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\\n\\n**HOW THIS STUDY WORKS**\\n\\nAs the group leader, you will want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of the Wild at Heart Study Guide. (The group members will also want to have a copy of the Wild at Heart book if they are doing the recommended readings for each session.) It works best if you can get the guides (and books) to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the material in the book ahead of time and be prepared to watch the first video session together.\\n\\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session being approximately fifteen to twenty minutes in length. Each week, you will meet together to watch the video and discuss the session. This series can also be used in classroom settings, such as Sunday school classes, though you may need to modify the discussion time depending on the size of the class. You could even use the video as sessions for a special prayer retreat. Basically, each week you will:\\n\\n1) Watch the video session, \\n2) Talk about it, and\\n3) Reflect on what you have learned by completing the between-sessions activities.\\n\\nThat’s it!\\n\\n**A FEW TIPS FOR LEADING A GROUP**\\n\\n\\n**The setting really matters.**\\n\\nIf you can choose to meet in a living room over a conference room in a church, do it. Pick an environment that’s conducive to people relaxing and getting real. Remember the enemy likes to distract us when it comes to seeking God, so do what you can to remove these obstacles from your group (silence cell phones, limit background noise, no texting). Set the chairs or couches in a circle to prevent having a “classroom” feel.\\n\\n**Consider having some refreshments!** \\n\\nCoffee and water will do; cookies and snacks are even better. People tend to be nervous when they join a new group, so if you can give them something to hold onto (like a warm mug of coffee), they will relax a lot more. It’s human nature.\\n\\n**Good equipment is important.** \\n\\nMeet where you can watch the video sessions on a screen big enough for everyone to see and enjoy. Get or borrow the best gear you can. Also, be sure to test your media equipment ahead of time to make sure everything is in working condition. This way, if something isn’t working, you can fix it or make other arrangements before the meeting begins. (You’ll be amazed at how the enemy will try to mess things up for you!)\\n\\n**Be honest.** \\n\\nRemember that your honesty will set the tone for your time together. Be willing to answer questions personally, as this will set the pace for the length of your group members’ responses and will make others more comfortable in sharing.\\n\\n**Stick to the schedule.** \\n\\nStrive to begin and end your meetings at the same time each week. The people in your group are busy, and if they can trust you to be a good steward of their time, they will be more willing to come back each week. Of course, you want to be open to the work God is doing, and at times you may want to linger in prayer or discussion. Remember the clock serves you; your group doesn’t serve the clock. But work to respect the group’s time, especially when it comes to limiting the discussion times.\\n\\n**Don’t be afraid of silence or emotion.** \\n\\nWelcome awkward moments. The material presented during this study will challenge the group members to reconsider some of their beliefs and compel them to make the necessary changes in their lives. Don’t be afraid to ease into the material with the group.\\n\\n**Don’t dominate the conversation.** \\n\\nEven though you are the leader, you are also a member of this small group. So don’t steamroll over others in an attempt to lead—and don’t let anyone else in the group do so either.\\n\\n**Prepare for your meeting.** \\n\\nWatch the video for the meeting ahead of time. Although it may feel a bit like cheating because you’ll know what’s coming, you will be better prepared for what the session might stir in the hearts of your group members. Also, be sure to review the material in this guide and spend some time in prayer. In fact, the most important thing you can do is simply pray ahead of time each week:\\n\\n> _Lord Jesus, come and rule this time. Let your Spirit fill this place. Bring your kingdom here. Take us right to the things we really need to talk about and rescue us from every distraction. Show us the heart of the Father. Meet each person here. Give us your grace and love for one another. In your name I pray._\\n\\nWe understand people are busy, but we encourage your group members to also prepare. Before the first meeting, secure enough copies of the study guide for each member. Have these ready and on hand for the first meeting, or make sure the participants have purchased them. Send out a reminder email or a text a couple of days before the meeting to make sure folks don’t forget about it.  \\n\\n**AS YOU GATHER**\\n\\nYou will find the following counsel to be especially helpful when you meet for the first time as a group. These comments are offered in the spirit of “here is what I would do if I were leading a group through this study”:\\n\\nFirst, as the group gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself and share your name, how long you’ve been a follower of Christ, if you have a spouse and/or children, and what you want to learn most from this study. Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right into watching the video teaching, as this will help get things started on a strong note. In the following weeks, you may want to start by allowing folks to catch up a little with some “how are you?” kind of banter. Too much of this burns up your meeting time, but you have to allow some room for it because it helps build relationships among the group members.\\n\\nNote that each group will have its own personality and dynamics. Typically, people will hold back the first week or two until they feel the group is “safe.” Then they will begin to share. Again, don’t let it throw you if your group seems a bit awkward at first. Of course, some people never want to talk, so you’ll need to coax them out as time goes on. But let it go the first week.\\n\\n**INSIGHT FOR DISCUSSION**\\n\\nIf the group members are in any way open to talking about their lives as it relates to this material, you will likely not have enough time for every question suggested in this study guide. That’s okay! Pick the questions ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them.\\n\\nYou set the tone for the group. Your honesty and vulnerability during discussion times will tell them what they can share. How long you talk will give them an example of how long they should respond. So give some thought to what stories or insights from your own work in the study guide you want to highlight.\\n\\nWARNING: The greatest temptation for most small group leaders is to add to the video teaching with a little “teaching session” of their own. This is unhelpful for three reasons:\\n\\n1) The discussion time will be the richest time during your meeting. The video sessions have been intentionally kept short so you can have plenty of time for discussion. If you add to the teaching, you sacrifice this precious time.\\n\\n2) You don’t want your group members teaching, lecturing, or correcting one another. The group members are all at a different place in their spiritual journey. If you set a tone by teaching, the group will feel like they have the freedom to teach one another. That can be disastrous for group dynamics.\\n\\n3) The participants will be watching the video teachings during your group time and exploring the topics in more detail by completing the between-sessions exercises in the study guide. They don’t need more content! What they want is a chance to talk and process their own lives in light of all they have taken in.\\n\\n**A STRONG CLOSE**\\n\\nSome of the best learning times will take place after the group time as God brings new insights to the participants during the week. Encourage group members to write down any questions they have as they work through the between-sessions exercises in the study guide. Make sure they know you are available for them as they explore the material. Finally, make sure you close your time by praying together—either by following the suggested prompts or coming up with your own closing prayers. Ask two or three people to pray, inviting God to fill your group and lead each person during this study.\\n\\nThanks again for taking the time to lead your group. May God reward your efforts to help men recover their masculine hearts!\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0v2ni1m\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Leader\'s Guide\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0v2nuki\", \"body\": \"There\'s great power in diving into this journey with like-minded men, with each session taking them deeper into the restoration of their masculine heart. As you begin this study, we recommend that each man have a copy of:\\n\\n[Wild at Heart (book)](https://churchsource.com/products/wild-at-heart-expanded-ed-discovering-the-secret-of-a-mans-soul?variant=32679916142689)\\n\\n[Wild at Heart Study Guide](https://churchsource.com/products/wild-at-heart-study-guide-discovering-the-secret-of-a-man-s-soul-1?variant=33930869244001)\\n\\n[The Field Guide](https://churchsource.com/products/wild-at-heart-field-guide-revised-edition-discovering-the-secret-of-a-man-s-soul?variant=32868969742433) is also available, designed more for personal use or deeper, further study than most groups have time for. It is an option for the men to have a copy, but it\'s not needed for this study.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0v2oz5k\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0v2p091\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 1: The Heart of a Man\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0v2pboz\", \"body\": \"**Chapters to have read for this week:** _Wild at Heart_ chapters 1 & 2\\n\\n**About This Session:** Masculinity isn\'t something that is socially created. Gender is from God. He made the masculine heart and set it into every man. From it flows all the things that make your life worth living—friendships, love, adventure, career, dreams, and your relationship with God. It\'s time to recover your masculine heart.\\n\\n**Initial Welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions (if people don’t know each other). Begin with yourself (you can share your name, how long you’ve been a follower of Christ, if you have a spouse and/or children, and what you want to learn most from this study.) Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right into watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0v2psu2\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127340\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0v2rduc\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 4) for Session 1 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. However, it can be difficult at this first meeting for the men to want to open up. That\'s ok. If your group is very large, it may be helpful to break up into smaller groups for the discussion.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- Remember to end on time, especially this first week. You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 1 (found on page 2 of the Study Guide)\\n- Encourage the men to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 1. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the men know it will be helpful to read Chapter 3 in Wild at Heart to prepare for Session 2\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0v2rjeg\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 2: The Poser\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0v2rqhi\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** _Wild at Heart_ chapter 3\\n\\n**About This Session:** Every boy has two questions in life: Do I have what it takes? Am I powerful? As men, we stay where we feel powerful—and run from anything that makes us feel weak. We try to become what the world wants. We need to be honest about the Poser we\'ve constructed, name it, face it and lay it down in our search for a deep and genuine strength.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If there are new members in your group, take a moment to introduce yourselves to one another before watching the video. We suggest simply sharing your name, some brief details about your life, and why you decided to join this study. If you feel there is time, you can also take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack jumping into today\'s session. Then, watch the Session 2 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0v2rz51\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127353\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0v2s5tt\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 26) for Session 2 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you discuss only allows for a few of them. You can also share the most significant point you took away from this session to start everyone out.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 2 found on page 24 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Wrap up your time with prayer, simply talking to God. A few ideas based on the topics of Session 2 can be found on page 28 of the Study Guide.\\n- Encourage the men to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 2, and the primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the men know it will be helpful to read Chapters 4 & 7 in Wild at Heart to prepare for Session 3\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vlp3g3\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 3: The Wound\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vlpd22\", \"body\": \"**Chapters to have read for this week:** _Wild at Heart_ chapters 4 & 7\\n\\n**About This Session:** In our journey to become a man, we\'ve all taken arrows to the heart. This shapes us into the men we are—and are not. The wounds play out in a variety of ways, from anger and perfectionism to hiding and addictions. Yet the mission of Jesus is all about restoration (Isaiah 61). He came to heal your broken heart and restore you as a son…and as a man.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments for men to briefly share any insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—be careful this doesn\'t hijack jumping into today\'s session. Then, watch the Session 3 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlpzyk\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127375\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlq1tj\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide for Session 3 (found on page 46) ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you discuss only allows for a few of them. You can also share the most significant point you took away from this session to start everyone out.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 3, found on page 44 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Wrap up your time with prayer, simply talking to God. A few ideas based on the topics of Session 3 can be found on page 48 of the Study Guide.\\n- Encourage the men to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 3, and the primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the men know it will be helpful to read Chapters 8 & 9 in Wild at Heart to prepare for Session 4\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vlqvcj\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 4: The Battle\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vlr39q\", \"body\": \"**Chapters to have read for this week:** _Wild at Heart_ chapters 8 & 9\\n\\n**About This Session:** You have been born into a world at war—and have a role to play in this unfolding story. God, who is a great warrior, created man in his image. He set within each of us a warrior heart so we can join him in his war against evil. Discover how to reawaken this fierce quality hardwired into every man…and recover your warrior heart.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments for men to briefly share any insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—be careful this doesn\'t hijack jumping into today\'s session. Then, watch the Session 4 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlrpee\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127390\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlrv53\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide for Session 4 (found on page 70) ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you discuss only allows for a few of them. You can also share the most significant point you took away from this session to start everyone out.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 4, found on page 68 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Wrap up your time with prayer, simply talking to God. A few ideas based on the topics of Session 4 can be found on page 72 of the Study Guide.\\n- Encourage the men to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 4, and the primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the men know it will be helpful to read Chapter 10 in Wild at Heart to prepare for Session 5\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vlsmh5\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 5: The Beauty\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vlsy8e\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Wild at Heart chapter 10\\n\\n**About This Session:** Nothing captures the attention of a man like a woman. She is wonderful. She is a mystery. Beauty, Love, Sex—these things run deep in men. Yet Eve also can feel like such a challenge to our masculinity. That\'s why learning to fight for the heart of a woman and love her courageously are absolutely core to what it means to be a man.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments for men to briefly share any insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—be careful this doesn\'t hijack jumping into today\'s session. Then, watch the Session 5 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vltmtw\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127411\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vltoqv\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide for Session 5 (found on page 92) ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you discuss only allows for a few of them. You can also share the most significant point you took away from this session to start everyone out.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 5, found on page 90 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Wrap up your time with prayer, simply talking to God. A few ideas based on the topics of Session 5 can be found on page 94 of the Study Guide.\\n- Encourage the men to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 5, and the primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the men know it will be helpful to read Chapter 11 in Wild at Heart to prepare for Session 6\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vlu9fc\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 6: The Adventure\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vlug8n\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Wild at Heart chapter 11\\n\\n**About This Session:** Men are wired for adventure. They come in three different forms—Casual, Crucial and Critical. And the amount of risk you\'re willing to live with in these categories is a direct correlation to what you believe about God. Find out how to pursue God in the particular adventures that feed and nourish your masculine soul.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments for men to briefly share any insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—be careful this doesn\'t hijack jumping into today\'s session. Then, watch the Session 6 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlv08l\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127419\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vlv21t\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide for Session 6 (found on page 114) ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you discuss only allows for a few of them. You can also share the most significant point you took away from this session to start everyone out.\\n\\n**A Strong Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 6, found on page 112 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Wrap up this time together with prayer, simply talking to God. A few ideas based on the topics of Session 6 can be found on page 116 of the Study Guide.\\n- Even though this is the last week of your group meeting together for this particular study, encourage the men to finish strong by working through the questions for Session 6 in their Study Guide in the coming week. \\n- Encourage the men to stay in this message. You may recommend the Field Guide at this point, for continued personal growth, and as a helpful tool to stay in the themes of Wild at Heart with God.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m1z95ja4\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 7: What\'s Next?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m1z96220\", \"body\": \"Congratulations! you\'ve made it to the final session. We encourage you to watch Session 7 and we invite you to encourage others to lead a an experience like you have.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m1z9csnd\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/539660791\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m1z9dqgx\", \"body\": \"**Steps to consider:**\\n\\n1. Read [Wild at Heart](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08BYZBC8C?ref=exp_ransomedheart_dp_vv_d) or [Captivating](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08BZ1BQ5T?ref=exp_ransomedheart_dp_vv_d) and share it with someone you know.\\n2. Dive deeper into this message with the [Wild at Heart Podcast](https://wildatheart.org/podcasts/wild-at-heart) and [Wild at Heart App](https://wildatheart.org/app/?sapurl=LytmODNjL2FwcD9lbWJlZD10cnVlJnJlY2VudFJvdXRlPWFwcC53ZWItYXBwLnJlZGlyZWN0b3ImcmVjZW50Um91dGVTbHVnPWFw).\\n3. Lead others in a group through the [Wild At Heart Experience](https://wildatheart.org/experiences/wildatheart).\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## WILD AT HEART EXPERIENCE \n\nThank you for your willingness to lead your group through Wild at Heart. This film series features the teaching of John Eldredge and the stories of men pursuing their warrior hearts through God\'s invitation of battle, adventure, and beauty. We\'re excited for you to take the men in your community on this journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader’s guide will give you tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\n\n## What does it take to lead this study?\n\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that’s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several people together who have a hunger for God, want to learn how to get their lives back, and are willing to be open and honest with God and themselves. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don’t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart, a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\n\n## How this study works\n\nAs the group leader, you will want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of the Wild at Heart Study Guide. (The group members will also want to have a copy of the Wild at Heart book if they are doing the recommended readings for each session.) It works best if you can get the guides (and books) to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the material in the book ahead of time and be prepared to watch the first video session together.\n\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session being approximately fifteen to twenty minutes in length. Each week, you will meet together to watch the video and discuss the session. This series can also be used in classroom settings, such as Sunday school classes, though you may need to modify the discussion time depending on the size of the class. You could even use the video as sessions for a special prayer retreat. Basically, each week you will:\n\n1. Watch the video session, \n2. Talk about it, and\n3. Reflect on what you have learned by completing the between-sessions activities.\n\nThat’s it!','## A FEW TIPS FOR LEADING A GROUP\n\nThe setting really matters. If you can choose to meet in a living room over a conference room in a church, do it. Pick an environment that’s conducive to people relaxing and getting real. Remember the enemy likes to distract us when it comes to seeking God, so do what you can to remove these obstacles from your group (silence cell phones, limit background noise, no texting). Set the chairs or couches in a circle to prevent having a “classroom” feel.\n\nConsider having some refreshments! Coffee and water will do; cookies and snacks are even better. People tend to be nervous when they join a new group, so if you can give them something to hold onto (like a warm mug of coffee), they will relax a lot more. It’s human nature.\n\nGood equipment is important. Meet where you can watch the video sessions on a screen big enough for everyone to see and enjoy. Get or borrow the best gear you can. Also, be sure to test your media equipment ahead of time to make sure everything is in working condition. This way, if something isn’t working, you can fix it or make other arrangements before the meeting begins. (You’ll be amazed at how the enemy will try to mess things up for you!)\n\nBe honest. Remember that your honesty will set the tone for your time together. Be willing to answer questions personally, as this will set the pace for the length of your group members’ responses and will make others more comfortable in sharing.\n\nStick to the schedule. Strive to begin and end your meetings at the same time each week. The people in your group are busy, and if they can trust you to be a good steward of their time, they will be more willing to come back each week. Of course, you want to be open to the work God is doing, and at times you may want to linger in prayer or discussion. Remember the clock serves you; your group doesn’t serve the clock. But work to respect the group’s time, especially when it comes to limiting the discussion times.\n\nDon’t be afraid of silence or emotion. Welcome awkward moments. The material presented during this study will challenge the group members to reconsider some of their beliefs and compel them to make the necessary changes in their lives. Don’t be afraid to ease into the material with the group.\n\nDon’t dominate the conversation. Even though you are the leader, you are also a member of this small group. So don’t steamroll over others in an attempt to lead—and don’t let anyone else in the group do so either.\n\nPrepare for your meeting. Watch the video for the meeting ahead of time. Although it may feel a bit like cheating because you’ll know what’s coming, you will be better prepared for what the session might stir in the hearts of your group members. Also, be sure to review the material in this guide and spend some time in prayer. In fact, the most important thing you can do is simply pray ahead of time each week:\n\n_Lord Jesus, come and rule this time. Let your Spirit fill this place. Bring your kingdom here. Take us right to the things we really need to talk about and rescue us from every distraction. Show us the heart of the Father. Meet each person here. Give us your grace and love for one another. In your name I pray._\n\nWe understand people are busy, but we encourage your group members to also prepare. Before the first meeting, secure enough copies of the study guide for each member. Have these ready and on hand for the first meeting, or make sure the participants have purchased them. Send out a reminder email or a text a couple of days before the meeting to make sure folks don’t forget about it.\n\nAdditional details will be available in the resources section after registration.','[{\"id\": \"lziiixho\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## SCHEDULE\\n\\n- Session 1 - The Heart of a Man\\n- Session 2 - The Poser\\n- Session 3 - The Wound\\n- Session 4 - The Battle\\n- Session 5 - The Beauty\\n- Session 6 - The Adventure\\n\\nAdditional details, downloads and the leader guide will be available in the resources section after registration.\"}]','[]','square-logo-wahexp-1725636439.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-wahexp.jpg',NULL,NULL,'[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-11 02:41:35','The Wild At Heart Experience is a guided video series for men that explores the core message of Wild at Heart and invites men to recover their strength, purpose, and connection with God.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vmg7k3\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/qpa0cczoijhb5kbd9rgyt/AAAVheMt-EEjapd2Aygp7xQ?rlkey=o4xfvqlg08fim1qweo7irq8hj&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'c765f4b7-4948-43f6-9b80-18730a871995'),
	(6,0,'Expected number of attendees','experience','course','Captivating Experience',NULL,5,NULL,NULL,'Through women’s personal stories and Stasi’s teachings, this new film series reveals every woman’s longing to be loved, play an irreplaceable role in a great adventure, and bring life and beauty to the world.',NULL,1,'women','captivating-experience','## Restore Your Feminine Heart\r\n\r\nThrough women’s personal stories and Stasi’s teachings, this new film series reveals every woman’s longing to be loved, play an irreplaceable role in a great adventure, and bring life and beauty to the world.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0vnpowy\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnpznn\", \"body\": \"Thank you for your willingness to lead your group through Captivating. This film series, featuring the teaching of Stasi Eldredge, reveals every woman\'s longing to be loved, play an irreplaceable role in a great adventure, and bring life and beauty to the world. We\'re excited for you to take the women in your community through this life-changing journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader\'s guide will give you some tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\\n\\n### What Does It Take to Lead This Study?\\n\\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that\'s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several people together who have a hunger for God, want to learn more about what is available for them in the here and now, and are willing to be open and honest with God and themselves. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don\'t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart, a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\\n\\n### How This Study Works\\n\\nAs the group leader, you’ll want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of the Captivating Study Guide, and the book Captivating: Unveiling the Mystery of a Woman’s Soul if they are doing the recommended readings for each session. It works best if you can get books and guides to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the first chapter ahead of time, which will prepare them for your first video session together. The Study Guide is written in such a way that participants do not have to read the book to participate; however, their experience will be much richer if they do. In the Study Guide, there is a section for the group to do together and there is a section to help participants go deeper into the material on their own, during the following week. To do that, it is helpful that they read the corresponding chapters in the book as well.\\n\\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session approximately fifteen to twenty minutes in length. Each week, you\'ll meet together to watch the video and discuss the session. This series can also be used in classroom settings, such as Sunday school classes, though you may need to modify the discussion time depending on the size of the class. You could even use the video as sessions for a special retreat. Basically, each week you and your group will:\\n\\n1) Watch the video session together\\n2) Talk about it with provided discussion questions\\n3) Reflect on what you have learned, and go deeper, by completing the between-session activities and reading the corresponding chapter(s) in Captivating.\\n\\nThat\'s it!\\n\\n### A Few Tips for Leading a Group\\n\\n### The setting really matters.\\n\\nIf you can choose to meet in a living room over a conference room in a church, do it. Pick an environment that\'s conducive to people relaxing and getting real. Remember, the enemy likes to distract us when it comes to prayer and seeking God, so do what you can to remove these obstacles from your group (silence cell phones, limit background noise, no texting). Set the chairs or couches in a circle to prevent having a \\\"classroom\\\" feel.\\n\\n**Consider having some refreshments!** \\nCoffee and water will do; cookies and snacks are even better. People tend to be nervous when they join a new group, so if you can give them something to hold onto (like a warm mug of coffee), they will relax a lot more. It\'s human nature.\\n\\n**Good equipment is important.** \\nMeet where you can watch the video sessions on a screen big enough for everyone to see and enjoy. Get or borrow the best gear you can. Also, be sure to test your media equipment ahead of time to make sure everything is in working condition. This way, if something isn\'t working, you can fix it or make other arrangements before the meeting begins. (You\'ll be amazed at how the enemy will try to mess things up for you!)\\n\\n**Be honest.** \\nRemember that your honesty will set the tone for your time together. Be willing to answer questions personally, as this will set the pace for the length of your group members\' responses and will make others more comfortable in sharing.\\n\\n**Stick to the schedule.**\\nStrive to begin and end at the same time each week. The people in your group are busy, and if they can trust you to be a good steward of their time, they will be more willing to come back each week. Of course, you want to be open to the work God is doing in the group members as they are challenged to reconsider some of their preconceived ideas about the availability of the kingdom of God to bring them joy in their everyday lives, and at times you may want to linger in prayer or discussion. Remember the clock serves you; your group doesn\'t serve the clock. But work to respect the group\'s time, especially when it comes to limiting the discussion times.\\n\\n**Don\'t be afraid of silence or emotion.**\\nWelcome awkward moments. The material presented during this study will likely bring to the surface areas of pain and suffering. Don\'t be afraid to ease into the material with the group to allow space for honoring one another\'s stories and personal questions.\\n\\n**Don\'t dominate the conversation.**\\nEven though you are the leader, you are also a member of this small group. So don\'t steamroll over others in an attempt to lead-and don\'t let anyone else in the group do so either.\\n\\n**Prepare for your meeting.**\\nWatch the video for the meeting ahead of time. Though it may feel a bit like cheating because you\'ll know what\'s coming, you\'ll be better prepared for what the session might stir in the hearts of your group members. Also, review the material in this guide and be sure to spend time in prayer. In fact, the most important thing you can do is simply pray ahead of time each week:\\n\\n> Lord Jesus, come and rule this time. Let Your Spirit fill this place. Bring Your kingdom here. Take us right to the things we really need to talk about and rescue us from every distraction. Show us the heart of the Father. Meet each person here. Give us Your grace and love for one another. In Your Name I pray.\\n\\nWe understand people are busy, but we encourage your group members to also prepare. Before the first meeting, secure enough copies of the study guide and the Captivating book for each member. Have these ready and on hand for the first meeting, or make sure the participants have purchased these resources for themselves. Send out a reminder email or a text a couple of days before the meeting to make sure folks don\'t forget about it.\\n\\n**As You Gather**\\nYou will find the following counsel to be especially helpful when you meet for the first time as a group. I offer these comments in the spirit of \\\"here is what I would do if I were leading a group through this study.\\\"\\n\\nFirst, as the group gathers, start your time with introductions if people don\'t know each other. Begin with yourself and share your name, how long you\'ve been a follower of Christ, if you have a spouse and/or children, and what you hope for during this time together. Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter each person has introduced herself, share-in no more than five minutes-what your hopes are for the group. Then jump right into watching the video session, as this will help get things started on a strong note. In the following weeks you will then want to start by allowing folks to catch up a little-say, fifteen minutes or so-with some \\\"hey, so how are you?\\\" kind of banter. Too much of this burns up your meeting time, but you have to allow some room for it because it helps build relationships among the group members.\\n\\nNote that each group will have its own personality and dynamics. Typically, people will hold back the first week or two until they feel the group is \\\"safe.\\\" Then they will begin to share. Again, don\'t let it throw you if your group seems a bit awkward at first. Of course, some people never want to talk, so you\'ll need to coax them out as time goes on. But let it go the first week.\\n\\n**Insight for Discussion**\\nIf the group members are in any way open to talking about their lives as it relates to this material, you will not have enough time for every question suggested in this study guide. That\'s okay! Pick the questions ahead of time that you know you want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them.\\n\\nYou set the tone for the group. Your honesty and vulnerability during discussion times will tell them what they can share. How long you talk will give them an example of how long they should. So give some thought to what stories or insights from your own work in the study guide you want to highlight.\\n\\nWARNING: The greatest temptation for most small group leaders is to add to the video teaching with a little \\\"teaching session\\\" of their own. This is unhelpful for three reasons:\\n\\n1) The discussion time will be the richest time during your meeting. The video sessions have been intentionally kept short so you can have plenty of time for discussion. If you add to the teaching, you sacrifice this precious time.\\n2) You don\'t want your group members teaching, lecturing, or correcting one another. Every person is at a different place in her spiritual journey—and that\'s good. But if you set a tone by teaching, the group will feel like they have the freedom to teach one another. That can be disastrous for group dynamics.\\n3) The participants will have watched the video teaching and possibly read the corresponding chapters in Captivating. They don\'t need more content! They want a chance to talk and process their own lives in light of all they have taken in.\\n\\n**A Strong Close**\\nSome of the best learning times will take place after the group time as God brings new insights to the participants during the week. Encourage group members to write down any questions they have as they read through Captivating and do the preparation work. Make sure they know you are available for them as they explore what God has to say about any of the concepts that might be new or challenging to them. Finally, make sure you close your time by praying together. Perhaps ask two or three people to pray, inviting God to fill your group and lead each person during this study. (A closing prayer is included in the Study Guide, should you want to use it instead of or in addition to extemporaneous prayer.)\\n\\nThank you again for taking the time to lead your group. May God reward your efforts and dedication and make your time together in Captivating fruitful for His kingdom.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnstfc\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Leader\'s Guide\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnt5eb\", \"body\": \"There\'s great power walking through this journey with like-minded women, as each session takes them deeper with God into the restoration of their feminine heart. As you begin this study, we recommend that each participant have a copy of:\\n\\n[Captivating (book)](https://churchsource.com/products/captivating-unveiling-the-mystery-of-a-womans-soul-1?variant=34095828861025)\\n[Captivating Study Guide](https://churchsource.com/products/captivating-study-guide-unveiling-the-mystery-of-a-woman-s-soul-1?variant=33930863378529)\\n\\nThe [Captivating Guided Journal](https://churchsource.com/products/captivating-guided-journal-revised-edition-unveiling-the-mystery-of-a-womans-soul?variant=34091521114209) is also available, designed more for personal use and deeper, further study than most groups have time for. It is an option for the women to have a copy, but it is not needed for this study.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnu8h7\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnu9be\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 1: The Heart of a Woman\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnuieb\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Captivating chapter 1\\n\\n**About This Session:** What did God mean when he meant you? Your feminine heart has been created as a reflection of God\'s own heart. And though we are all unique, we also each share the same core desires. Discover how every woman longs to be romanced, to play an irreplaceable role in a heroic adventure, and to unveil beauty.\\n\\n**Initial Welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions (if the ladies don’t know each other). Begin with yourself (you can share your name, how long you’ve been a follower of Christ, if you have a spouse and/or children, and what you hope to learn most from this study.) Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\n**Core Scripture:** Proverbs 4:23; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 1 Video:** After introductions and sharing of Proverbs 4:23, jump right into watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnvdin\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127959\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnvup4\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 4) for Session 1 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. However, it may be difficult at this first meeting for the women to want to open up. That\'s ok. If your group is very large, it may be helpful to break up into smaller groups for the discussion.\\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- Remember to end on time, especially this first week. You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 1 (found on page 2 of the Study Guide)\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 5, which is based on the topics of Session 1, if helpful.\\n- Encourage the women to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 1. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the women know it will be helpful to read Chapters 2 & 3 in Captivating to prepare for Session 2\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnwl0a\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 2: Fallen Eve\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnwqr6\", \"body\": \"**Chapters to have read for this week:** Captivating chapters 2 & 3\\n\\n**About This Session:** Eve fell to the lies of the enemy because she was convinced that God was holding out on her. We make that same choice today. Having forfeited our confidence in God, we believe that in order to have the life we want, we must take matters into our own hands. So we do…only to then ache with an emptiness nothing seems able to fill.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If there are new members in your group, take a moment to introduce yourselves to one another. We suggest simply sharing your name, some brief details about your life, and why you decided to join this study. If you feel there is time, you can also take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack the time for today\'s session. \\n\\n**Core Scripture:** Genesis 2:18; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 2 Video:** After the welcome and sharing of Genesis 2:18, jump right into watching the Session 2 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnxi5d\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127969\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnxv6r\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 20) for Session 2 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. \\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 2, found on page 18 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 21, which is based on the topics of Session 2, if helpful.\\n- Encourage the women to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 2. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the women know it will be helpful to read Chapters 4 & 6 in Captivating to prepare for Session 3.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vnykk7\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 3: The Wound and the Healer\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vnyrqe\", \"body\": \"**Chapters to have read for this week:** Captivating chapters 4 & 6\\n\\n**About This Session:** Some women\'s lives look perfect from a distance. But only from a distance. We all have sorrows and pains. The offer from God is to heal our broken hearts and set free the places that are held captive within us (Isaiah 61). But to be healed, we must let God tenderly open our wounds and expose them to his light, to his love, and to his truth.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack the time for today\'s session. \\n\\n**Core Scripture:** Psalm 56:8; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 3 Video:** After the welcome and sharing of Psalm 56:8, jump right into watching the Session 3 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnzi22\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127976\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vnzwiz\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 42) for Session 3 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. \\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 3, found on page 40 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 43, which is based on the topics of Session 3, if helpful.\\n- Encourage the women to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 3. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the women know it will be helpful to read Chapter 5 in Captivating to prepare for Session 4.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vo16t3\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 4: A Special Hatred\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vo1g1m\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Captivating chapter 5\\n\\n**About This Session:** The story of every woman\'s life is the story of the long and sustained assault upon her heart by the one who knows who she could be and fears her. You are under regular spiritual assault. In order to have the life God wants for you, you must rise up and take your stand in him. Resist the enemy…and he will flee (James 4:7).\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack the time for today\'s session. \\n\\n**Core Scripture:** Ephesians 6:12; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 4 Video:** After the welcome and sharing of Ephesians 6:12, jump right into watching the Session 4 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo242d\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498127989\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo2o37\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 62) for Session 4 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. \\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 4, found on page 60 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 63, which is based on the topics of Session 4, if helpful.\\n- Encourage the women to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 4. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the women know it will be helpful to read Chapter 8 in Captivating to prepare for Session 5.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vo36ms\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 5: Beauty to Unveil\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vo3f0a\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Captivating chapter 8\\n\\n**About This Session:** The world\'s view of beauty is unattainable. Yet our constant pursuit of it, apart from God, has caused us countless tears and untold pain. Each of us, as a daughter of God, has a captivating beauty all our own to unveil. Because we bear God\'s image, we reflect his beauty—inside and out. A beautiful woman is a woman whose heart is alive.\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack the time for today\'s session. \\n\\n**Core Scripture:** 1 Samuel 16:7; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 5 Video:** After the welcome and sharing of 1 Samuel 16:7, jump right into watching the Session 5 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo48qv\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498128005\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo4j7t\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 82) for Session 5 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. \\n\\n**As You Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 5, found on page 80 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 83, which is based on the topics of Session 5, if helpful.\\n- Encourage the women to work through the questions in their Study Guide in the coming week. This is designed to take them deeper into the themes from Session 5. The primary goal of this is for personal growth and private reflection.\\n- Let the women know it will be helpful to read Chapter 12 in Captivating to prepare for Session 6.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vo535s\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 6: Your Irreplaceable Role\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vo5axz\", \"body\": \"**Chapter to have read for this week:** Captivating chapter 12\\n\\n**About This Session:** A woman doesn\'t come alive being merely useful. We want our lives to matter and to matter deeply. We want to be needed. Irreplaceable. And so does God. He has written something on your heart. Give yourself permission to dream. If you could do anything, what would it be? Now pursue that…with him!\\n\\n**Welcome:** If you feel there is time, take a few moments to see if anyone wants to share brief insights from their personal reflection during the previous week—but be careful this doesn\'t hijack the time for today\'s session. \\n\\n**Core Scripture:** Genesis 1:28; Take a few minutes and invite women to read from various translations aloud. Listen for fresh insights and share any thoughts about this verse with the group.\\n\\n**Watch Session 6 Video:** After the welcome and sharing of Genesis 1:28, jump right into watching the Session 6 video:\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo61pt\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/498128021\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vo6cxj\", \"body\": \"**Discussion:** Pick the group discussion questions from the Study Guide (found on page 100) for Session 6 ahead of time that you know you definitely want to cover, just in case you end up only having time to discuss a few of them. \\n\\n**A Strong Close:**\\n\\n- You can close by briefly reviewing the summary of Session 6, found on page 98 of the Study Guide.\\n- Pray—Close your time with prayer, simply talking with God. The leader or a volunteer can use the prayer found on page 101, which is based on the topics of Session 6, if helpful.\\n- Even though this is the last week of your group meeting together for this particular study, encourage the women to finish strong by working through the questions for Session 6 in their Study Guide this coming week.\\n- Encourage the women to stay in this message. You may recommend the [Captivating Guided Journal](https://churchsource.com/products/captivating-guided-journal-revised-edition-unveiling-the-mystery-of-a-womans-soul?variant=34091521114209) at this point, for continued personal growth, and as a helpful tool to stay in the themes of Captivating and everything God wants to continue to do in their lives.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m1z9kkwk\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 7: What\'s Next?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m1z9kvqt\", \"body\": \"Congratulations! you\'ve made it to the final session. We encourage you to watch Session 7 and we invite you to encourage others to lead a an experience like you have.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m1z9ln69\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/539660715\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m1z9lze1\", \"body\": \"**Steps to consider:**\\n\\n1. Read [Wild at Heart](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08BYZBC8C?ref=exp_ransomedheart_dp_vv_d) or [Captivating](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08BZ1BQ5T?ref=exp_ransomedheart_dp_vv_d) and share it with someone you know.\\n2. Dive deeper into this message with the [Wild at Heart Podcast](https://wildatheart.org/podcasts/wild-at-heart) and [Wild at Heart App](https://wildatheart.org/app/?sapurl=LytmODNjL2FwcD9lbWJlZD10cnVlJnJlY2VudFJvdXRlPWFwcC53ZWItYXBwLnJlZGlyZWN0b3ImcmVjZW50Um91dGVTbHVnPWFw).\\n3. Lead others in a group through the [Wild At Heart Experience](https://wildatheart.org/experiences/captivating).\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## CAPTIVATING EXPERIENCE \n\nThank you for your willingness to lead your group through Captivating. This film series, featuring the teaching of Stasi Eldredge, reveals every woman\'s longing to be loved, play an irreplaceable role in a great adventure, and bring life and beauty to the world. We\'re excited for you to take the women in your community through this life-changing journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader\'s guide will give you some tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\n\n## What Does It Take to Lead This Study?\n\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that\'s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several people together who have a hunger for God, want to learn more about what is available for them in the here and now, and are willing to be open and honest with God and themselves. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don\'t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart, a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\n\n## How This Study Works\n\nAs the group leader, you’ll want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of the Captivating Study Guide, and the book Captivating: Unveiling the Mystery of a Woman’s Soul if they are doing the recommended readings for each session. It works best if you can get books and guides to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the first chapter ahead of time, which will prepare them for your first video session together. The Study Guide is written in such a way that participants do not have to read the book to participate; however, their experience will be much richer if they do. In the Study Guide, there is a section for the group to do together and there is a section to help participants go deeper into the material on their own, during the following week. To do that, it is helpful that they read the corresponding chapters in the book as well.\n\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session approximately fifteen to twenty minutes in length. Each week, you\'ll meet together to watch the video and discuss the session. This series can also be used in classroom settings, such as Sunday school classes, though you may need to modify the discussion time depending on the size of the class. You could even use the video as sessions for a special retreat. Basically, each week you and your group will:\n\n1. Watch the video session together\n2. Talk about it with provided discussion questions\n3. Reflect on what you have learned, and go deeper, by completing the between-session activities and reading the corresponding chapter(s) in Captivating.\n\nThat\'s it!','## A FEW TIPS FOR LEADING A GROUP \n\nThe setting really matters. If you can choose to meet in a living room over a conference room in a church, do it. Pick an environment that\'s conducive to people relaxing and getting real. Remember, the enemy likes to distract us when it comes to prayer and seeking God, so do what you can to remove these obstacles from your group (silence cell phones, limit background noise, no texting). Set the chairs or couches in a circle to prevent having a \"classroom\" feel.\n\nConsider having some refreshments! Coffee and water will do; cookies and snacks are even better. People tend to be nervous when they join a new group, so if you can give them something to hold onto (like a warm mug of coffee), they will relax a lot more. It\'s human nature.\n\nGood equipment is important. Meet where you can watch the video sessions on a screen big enough for everyone to see and enjoy. Get or borrow the best gear you can. Also, be sure to test your media equipment ahead of time to make sure everything is in working condition. This way, if something isn\'t working, you can fix it or make other arrangements before the meeting begins. (You\'ll be amazed at how the enemy will try to mess things up for you!)\n\nBe honest. Remember that your honesty will set the tone for your time together. Be willing to answer questions personally, as this will set the pace for the length of your group members\' responses and will make others more comfortable in sharing.\n\nStick to the schedule. Strive to begin and end at the same time each week. The people in your group are busy, and if they can trust you to be a good steward of their time, they will be more willing to come back each week. Of course, you want to be open to the work God is doing in the group members as they are challenged to reconsider some of their preconceived ideas about the availability of the kingdom of God to bring them joy in their everyday lives, and at times you may want to linger in prayer or discussion. Remember the clock serves you; your group doesn\'t serve the clock. But work to respect the group\'s time, especially when it comes to limiting the discussion times.\n\nDon\'t be afraid of silence or emotion. Welcome awkward moments. The material presented during this study will likely bring to the surface areas of pain and suffering. Don\'t be afraid to ease into the material with the group to allow space for honoring one another\'s stories and personal questions.\n\nDon\'t dominate the conversation. Even though you are the leader, you are also a member of this small group. So don\'t steamroll over others in an attempt to lead-and don\'t let anyone else in the group do so either.\n\nPrepare for your meeting. Watch the video for the meeting ahead of time. Though it may feel a bit like cheating because you\'ll know what\'s coming, you\'ll be better prepared for what the session might stir in the hearts of your group members. Also, review the material in this guide and be sure to spend time in prayer. In fact, the most important thing you can do is simply pray ahead of time each week:\n\nLord Jesus, come and rule this time. Let Your Spirit fill this place. Bring Your kingdom here. Take us right to the things we really need to talk about and rescue us from every distraction. Show us the heart of the Father. Meet each person here. Give us Your grace and love for one another. In Your Name I pray.\n\nWe understand people are busy, but we encourage your group members to also prepare. Before the first meeting, secure enough copies of the study guide and the Captivating book for each member. Have these ready and on hand for the first meeting, or make sure the participants have purchased these resources for themselves. Send out a reminder email or a text a couple of days before the meeting to make sure folks don\'t forget about it.\n\nAdditional details will be available in the resources section after registration.','[{\"id\": \"lzk09prf\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## CAPTIVATING RETREAT SCHEDULE \\n\\nSession 1: The Heart of a Woman\\nSession 2: Fallen Eve\\nSession 3: The Wound and the Healer\\nSession 4: A Special Hatred\\nSession 5: Beauty to Unveil\\nSession 6: Your Irreplaceable Role\\n\\nA break down of each day, downloads and instructions will be available in the resources section after registration.\"}]','[]','event_types/b5113945-276c-4223-b59b-f273c0eecd73.jpg','4k-horiz-capexp.jpg',NULL,NULL,'[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-11 02:41:51','The Captivating Experience is a small-group journey for women to explore the message of Captivating and rediscover the beauty, strength, and life God placed within their hearts.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0voa20j\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/vmqcqcxzct20h0f4es36g/AO2cWG_5BgqtfYcuv5A6QuU?rlkey=tj9zft5sjkpya0vdwknlu52at&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'f7827b6f-005b-42f7-91df-0343387155ac'),
	(7,0,'Expected number of attendees','experience','course','Becoming A King Experience',NULL,9,NULL,NULL,'The Becoming a King Video Experience is a personal invitation to dive deeply into the mission of becoming the kind of man to whom God can gladly entrust the care of his Kingdom.',NULL,1,'men','becoming-a-king-experience','## The Path To Restoring The Heart Of A Man\r\n\r\nThe Becoming a King Video Experience is a personal invitation to dive deeply into the mission of becoming the kind of man to whom God can gladly entrust the care of his Kingdom.\r\n\r\nEvery boy knows he was made to be powerful. As an acorn carries the blueprint of the oak tree, so the heart of every boy holds the possibility of becoming a wholehearted king whose strength brings goodness to all under his care. Yet the headlines often confirm what we know too well from our own stories: the anguished consequences of masculine power gone awry.\r\n\r\nMasculinity is in need of restoration. But what is the way, and how can men find it?\r\n\r\nCurated and distilled over two decades, the message of Becoming a King offers a path to restoring the hearts of men in the image of our strong, present, wise, and loving God.\r\n\r\nJoin me as we venture together to recover your strength and restore your heart as a man.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0vphwos\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vpi77w\", \"body\": \"I’m moved by your courage to risk facilitating a Becoming a King group. Over the past 20 years of leading men, I have experienced again and again how often the deepest transformation in my masculine soul happens when I risk facilitating an experience for others. This film series features content curated and distilled from decades of seeking the heart of God through older, wiser guides. Even more, it is a personal invitation from the heart of God to the slow and steady process of becoming the kind of men, the kind of kings, to whom God can gladly entrust his Kingdom. We\'re excited for you to take the men in your community on this journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader’s guide will give you tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\\n\\n**WHAT DOES IT TAKE TO LEAD THIS STUDY?**\\n\\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that’s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several men together who have a deep thirst for apprenticeship to God and his Kingdom. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don’t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart and a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\\n\\n**HOW THIS STUDY WORKS**\\n\\nAs the group leader, you will want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of both the Becoming a King book and study guide. It works best if you can get the guides and books to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the material in the book ahead of time and be prepared to watch the first video session together. You can order the books directly by clicking [here.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cow2a)\\n\\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session being approximately 20 minutes in length. Be creative. The series is designed to be used in a wide variety of context. From a weekly small group of men, to a weekend retreat of any size. Make the necessary adjustments so that everyone has the opportunity to authentically engage. \\n\\n**A FEW DATA POINTS AS YOU SET OUT**\\n\\nOnline or in person, the same things apply. There are benefits and challenges to both. Either way, I encourage you to take each of these suggestions to heart.\\n\\n**The setting really matters.** Whether online or in person, create a distraction free environment, that allows people to get real. Remember, the enemy likes to distract us when it comes to seeking God, so do what you can to remove these obstacles from your group (silence cell phones, limit background noise, no texting, etc.). Set the chairs or couches in a circle to prevent having a “classroom” feel. Consider having some refreshments. Depending on your group’s culture, that can be anything from pints and cigars to coffee and donuts. Just be yourself.\\n\\n**Good equipment is important.** If you\'re online, be sure everyone has access to stream or download the video. If in person, meet where you can watch the video sessions on a screen big enough for everyone to see and enjoy. Get or borrow the best gear you can. Also, be sure to test your media equipment ahead of time to make sure everything is in working condition. That way, if something isn’t working, you can fix it or make other arrangements before the meeting begins.\\n\\n**Be honest.** Remember that your honesty will set the tone for your time together. Be willing to answer questions personally, as this will set the pace for the length of your group members’ responses and will make others more comfortable in sharing.\\n\\n**Confidentiality is essential.** Agree with the entire group that everything shared in your time together is held in strict confidence. The goal is to create a soul safe space, where men can be authentic. \\n\\n**Stick to the schedule.** Strive to begin and end your meetings at the same time each week. The people in your group have lives as full as yours, and if they can trust you to be a good steward of their time, they will be more willing to come back each week. Of course, you want to be open to the work God is doing, and at times you may want to linger in prayer or discussion. Remember, the clock serves you; your group doesn’t serve the clock. But work to respect the group’s time, especially when it comes to limiting the discussion times.\\n\\n**Don’t be afraid of silence or emotion.** Honor the two-minute pauses built into each session as they are laid out in the study guide. Welcome awkward moments. The message presented during this study will challenge the group members to reconsider some of their beliefs and compel the brave to put new things into practice in their lives. Don’t be afraid to ease into the material with the group.\\n\\n**Don’t dominate the conversation.** Though you are the leader, you are also a member of this small group. So don’t steamroll over others in an attempt to lead—and don’t let anyone else in the group do so either.\\n\\n**Prepare for your meeting.** Watch the video for the meeting ahead of time. You will feel better prepared for what the session might stir in the hearts of your group members. Also, be sure to review the material in this guide and spend some time in prayer. In fact, the most important thing you can do is simply pray ahead of time each week:\\n\\n> God, come and rule this time. Let your Spirit fill this place. Bring your Kingdom here. Take us to the things we really need to talk about, and rescue us from every distraction. Show us the heart of the Father. Meet each person here. Give us your grace and love for one another. In your name, I pray.\\n\\n**Send out a reminder email or text** a couple of days before the meeting to make sure folks don’t forget about it. And remember you can [get big discounts on the book and study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_coyfv) in bulk for your group. Everyone will want it in hand for session one.\\n \\n\\n**AS YOU GATHER**\\n\\nYou will find the following counsel especially helpful when you meet as a group for the first time. These comments are offered in the spirit of “here is what I would do if I were leading a group through this study.”\\n\\nFirst, as the group gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself and share your name, what drew you to participate, if you have a spouse and/or children, what you would love to see happen for your masculine soul through this experience. Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, as this will help get things started on a strong note. In the following weeks, you may want to start by allowing folks to catch up a little with some “how are you?” kind of banter. Too much of this burns up your meeting time, but you have to allow some room for it because it helps build relationships among the group members.\\n\\nNote that each group will have its own personality and dynamics. People will typically hold back the first week or two until they feel the group is “safe.” Then they will begin to share. Again, don’t let it throw you if your group seems a bit awkward at first. Of course, some people never want to talk, so you’ll need to coax them out as time goes on. But let it go the first week.\\n\\n**INSIGHT FOR DISCUSSION**\\n\\nIf the group members are at all open to talking about their lives as they relate to this material, you will likely not have enough time for every question suggested in the study guide. I encourage you to choose two or three questions or big ideas from the study guide as the centerpiece for each gathering. The men can dive into more of the study guide and suggested action steps in their time alone between gatherings.\\n\\nWhether online or in person, you set the tone for the group. Your honesty and vulnerability during discussion times will tell them what they can share. How long you talk will give them an example of how long they should respond. So give some thought to what stories or insights from your own work in the study guide you want to highlight.\\n\\n**A STRONG CLOSE**\\n\\nSome of the best learning will take place after the group time as God brings new insights to the participants during the week. Encourage your group to write down any questions they have as they work through the between-sessions exercises in the study guide. Make sure they know you are available for them as they explore the material. Finally, make sure you close your time by praying together—either by following the suggested prompts or by coming up with your own closing prayers. Ask two or three people to pray, inviting God to fill your group and lead each person during this study.\\n\\nThanks again for taking the time to lead your group. May God reward your efforts to help men recover the ancient path to becoming!\\n\\n**JOIN ME FOR A LIVE ONLINE GATHERING**\\n\\nOn a regular basis, I host an online session with Becoming a King facilitators and their groups for an exclusive face-to-face time to ask questions, dive deeper into the content, and pray together. You can find the registration link for your group under number four of the “Ways to Share” section [on this page.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/launch-team/)\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vpmdye\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Leader\'s Guide\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vpmj6u\", \"body\": \"The real work of transformation begins as we engage this journey, not only participating with God in the process of becoming but also offering what we live. To lead a Becoming a King group is an even deeper dive into this transformation. Let\'s get started.\\n\\nAs you risk offering your strength by way of leading this group, make sure you have the necessary materials:\\n\\n- [Becoming a King (book)](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp02j)\\n- [Becoming a King Study Guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp0g0)\\n\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com](https://becomegoodsoil.com/) to stay connected with new content and resources being made available to continue to strengthen you in this role.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vpnls6\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m0vpnmgq\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 1 - Becoming Powerful\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vpnx69\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** If we are to become who God meant when he meant us—as men—we must get honest about our God-given desire to be powerful. We must become men who neither deny nor misuse our power, but rather wield power for the good of others as we walk in wholehearted union with God. \\n\\n**Central question for this session:** How do we become the kind of men who can handle power?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease. Remind every participating that confidentiality is essential. Together, you are agreeing as a group that everything shared in your time is held in strict confidence. The goal is to create a soul safe space, where your participants can be authentic.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note: \\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vpon0d\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417286098\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vpp4no\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you. \\n\\n**READ**\\nThink of a moment in your childhood when you were entrusted with power.\\n\\nWhile riding bikes with my daughter yesterday, I had a visceral memory of the first time, as a young boy, I was turned loose to head off on my bike to the neighborhood beyond our street. All these years later, I can still remember the power I felt. Moments like this whisper to us a secret waiting to be recovered. \\n\\nI\'ve spent the last two decades excavating this desire in my heart and in the hearts of many men. With intense curiosity I’ve sought to uncover the source of this desire and why it so often leads a man sideways. As I scan the landscape of my own life and the lives of other men, I find \\n\\nfar too many stories of men being entrusted with power, only to have that power bring harm to themselves and others. \\n\\nIs there another way? Is there a path to becoming the kind of wholehearted man who can be entrusted with power and have it turn out for good? As I spent years leaning into the wisdom of contemporary sages as well as sages from millennia past, a path began to take shape. In time, that path revealed a process of transformation to become the kind of man to whom God can entrust his power. \\n\\nIt was John Eldredge who said, “The great problem of the earth and the great aim of the masculine journey boil down to this: When can you trust a man with power?” In Session 1, I invite you to risk recovering your God-given desire to be powerful. How has this desire played out in your masculine heart over the years? Where has it led you to places you never wanted to go? And what might the process look like to experience deep and lasting wholehearted restoration, becoming the kind of man who can wield power well? \\n\\nLet’s dig in. \\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp3cn) pages 16-17)\\n\\n1. Think back to your childhood. Recall a situation when you were entrusted with power. How did you feel? How did it go?\\n2. Describe a good king. Think of an example of a particular man (past or present) who, in your mind, is a compelling model of a wholehearted man. List specific qualities you admire in him. Ask yourself what qualities he is missing that would make him even more the kind of man who can be entrusted with the care of a kingdom. \\n3. How is your kingdom? Put words to the condition of the people and things that have been entrusted to your care. What does this raise within you? \\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n_Stand at the crossroads and look; ask for the ancient paths, ask where the good way is and walk in it, and you will find rest for your souls.\\n_Jeremiah 6:16 NIV\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\n\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into.Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead.\\n\\n**TAKE ACTION THIS WEEK**\\nRead chapter 1 of [Becoming a King](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp4bb).\\nComplete session 1 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp4kc)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\nWatch The Mask of Zorro. Consider the story of Alejandro and his relationship with Diego. Reflect on the presence and energy both men exhibit in the master/apprentice relationship. \\n\\n- What do you relate to in this story? \\n- What is God saying to you through Alejandro’s story of initiation? \\n- Who would you risk sharing this part of your story with? \\n\\nListen to the Becoming a King Wives Collection ([Part 1](https://becomegoodsoil.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Becoming-A-King-Wives-Conversation-Part-1.mp3) and [Part 2](https://becomegoodsoil.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Becoming-A-King-Wives-Conversation-Part-2.mp3)). It’s an exclusive conversation that will strengthen your soul. I invited my wife, Cherie, and the wives of three other men who have consented to the path and process of Becoming a King for more than a decade into the Become Good Soil podcast studio. With raw courage and winsome authenticity, they shared a behind-the-scenes view of what it has been like for them.\\n\\nListen to [Become Good Soil podcast episode 040.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/040-intensive-series-episode-1-of-8-podcast/)\\n\\nRead Become Good Soil blog post – [Fallen Kings](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2012/10/09/fallen-kings-fallen-kingdoms/), [Fallen Kingdoms.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2012/10/09/fallen-kings-fallen-kingdoms/)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vptoom\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 2 - Becoming a Son\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vptudr\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** Our identity as a beloved son is often where we’ve taken the greatest hits. Yet sonship is intended to be the foundation of our lives. As we learn to experience our secure place in our Father’s heart, we are able to bring our strength—rather than our questions—to the world. \\n\\n**Central questions for this session:** What if courage could replace fear and a sense of reliable abundance could replace the specter of scarcity? What if there was a way to become the kind of man who brings authentic strength to his world out of a deep reservoir of life within?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note: \\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vpui3j\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417286106\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vpustp\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you. \\n\\n**READ**\\nIt was said by George MacDonald, “Since we are the sons of God, we must become the sons of God.” Whatever else we encounter when we engage the life of Jesus, we encounter a person living fully as a son. Sonship is the truest state of his being. It is the epicenter of Jesus’ life, and it is intended to be the epicenter of ours. Only from an ongoing experience of sonship can we bring increasing strength—rather than our soul’s question—to the world.\\n                        \\nIf we live from an ever-expanding reservoir of sonship as our primary identity, we will become the kind of person who can prevail in any circumstance, no matter the cost. Even more, we will recover the treasure of deep and lasting joy. Let’s explore what it means to receive God as Father. It changes everything.\\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp8qn) pages 42-43)\\n\\n1. How have you learned “father”? Take an honest inventory. Think of the male figures in your life growing up—the good and the bad, including your father and/or stepfather, coaches, teachers, pastors, men held out as role models in the media, perhaps the fathers of your friends. Call to mind and make a list of the men who surrounded you. Without editing or filtering, what words would you use to describe the traits you saw in those men? \\n2. How has God raised the condition of fatherlessness in your heart? Notice what isn’t “working” in your life as a signpost of fatherlessness. What have you done with this part of your story? \\n3. Pause for a few moments and think back over your story from the last decade or so. What are several examples of ways God was working to father you, even if at the time you may not have had the capacity to receive or respond as a son?  \\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n_So that we would know for sure that we are his true children, God released the Spirit of Sonship into our hearts….And because we’re his, we can access everything our Father has. \\n_Galatians 4:6-7 TPT\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into.Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead. \\n\\n**TAKE ACTION THIS WEEK**\\n\\nRead chapter 2 of [Becoming a King](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cp9q4).\\nComplete session 2 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpa5e)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\nListen to [Become Good Soil podcast 013: Quick.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/013-quick-podcast/)\\n\\n- What does this podcast awaken in you? \\n- What do you hope is true? \\n- What makes you uncomfortable? \\n\\nRead [Become Good Soil blog post – How Have You Learned the Father?.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2013/03/14/how-have-you-learned-the-father/)\\n\\nFor more, go to [BecomeGoodSoil.com/Sonship](https://BecomeGoodSoil.com/Sonship)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vq0mri\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 3 - Becoming the Man You Were Born to Be\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vq0xyp\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** Much of who we have become is an attempt to hide because of our fear of failure and exposure. The ancient path of becoming a king invites us to a deepening awareness of the self-protective man so we can put to death the false self and become who we were made to be, recovering our true name.  \\n\\n**Central questions for this session:** What did God mean when he meant you? What if desire reveals design and design reveals destiny?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note:\\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vq1jmd\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417286117\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vq1ui1\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\n\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you.\\n\\n**READ**\\n\\n“There are many people who think they want to be matadors, only to find themselves in the ring with 2,000 pounds of bull bearing down on them, and then discover that what they really wanted was to wear tight pants and hear the crowd roar.” –Terry Pearce\\n\\nWho have I become? And who am I becoming?\\n\\nThese are the central questions to recover masculine initiation.\\n\\nAfter the fall of man, Adam confessed, “I was afraid because I was naked; so I hid.” Adam’s story is every man’s story. We have become who we are not. We are haunted by fear of failure and the taunting of what we lack within. In response to our terror, we form caricatures to help us deny our vulnerability and independently survive. Yet the self-protective man we have become is not the truest us. What if we have a destiny to reflect aspects of God’s heart that no one else exactly reflects, a destiny to offer a unique strength? Through recovering who we were born to be, we can shift from withering in the angst of our unvalidated soul to recovering a true and genuine strength to bring to the world. \\n\\nThe truest reality of the masculine soul is that we are inheritors of original goodness, magnificently crafted in the image of God. As Jesus promised, out of putting to death the false within a man, a greater life emerges. It is here we are welcomed to risk engaging in the extraordinary process of recovering an indestructible life, a life of ever-deepening union with God. A life worth living. \\n\\nLet’s dig in.\\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpfp0) pages 64-65)\\n\\n1. Describe your false self, or yourself as “the poser.” How and where do you hide?\\n2. What do you fear the people closest to you would say if they were asked to describe you?\\n3. Observe your motives and how you are currently engaging with your family, in your work, and beyond. Where are you living for identity and where are you living from it? \\n4. Describe your true self. Who is the man you are meant to be but are not yet? What is he like?  \\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n\\n_I was afraid, because I was naked; so I hid.\\n_Genesis 3:10 NIV\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\n\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into. Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead. \\n\\n**TAKE ACTION THIS WEEK**\\n\\nRead chapters 3 and 4 of [Becoming a King.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpgmp)\\nComplete session 3 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpgzf)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://becomegoodsoil.com)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\n\\nWatch the film The Secret Life of Walter Mitty. Start with the [extended trailer](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bp_cxxqOaPM) for a brief introduction. Consider the gap between Walter Mitty’s daydreams and his daily reality. Can you resonate with this? What would it be like to discover an adventure journal left specifically for you from your dad, with the words “Have Fun” etched on the inside cover? \\n\\nListen to [Become Good Soil podcast 041.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/041-intensive-series-episode-2-of-8-podcast/)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vq5fyo\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 4 - Becoming a Generalist\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vq5o1b\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** To become a generalist is to cultivate a broad agency over many real things in order to mature and strengthen the entire masculine soul. As we forsake playing it safe to choose to live on the frontier of our initiation, we become the kind of man who can handle himself in any situation, bringing actual skill and harnessed strength to meet the world’s needs.\\n\\n**Central Question for this session:** In some of his final words to his Kingdom apprentices, Jesus said, “Travel light. You are the equipment.” What if a man and a knife could save the world?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note: \\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vq68y5\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417286128\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vq6kgh\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you. \\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpl89) pages 88-89)\\n\\n1. This video session and chapter 5 of Becoming a King begin with a story relayed by Benjamin Franklin of a Native American chief’s response to American colonists who “generously” offered to educate several of their boys. What is your reaction to that story? What does it reveal about how the founders of our nation thought about “education”? In contrast, what did the Native Americans think was necessary to educate a young man? How does this story relate to your own?\\n2. Call to mind an experience when you were in the presence of a man who demonstrated a fierce mastery over a situation or an ability to walk in deep maturity in a particular relational context. Perhaps it was watching a mechanic work on a car, a teacher presenting a compelling idea, a heroic figure in a film, or a craftsman who created with his own hands. Think about what you admired about the man in this situation. Why did you admire it? What emotions does it bring up as you think of yourself in that same situation? If what he embodied was something you were actually meant to embody one day, how would you move toward engaging in the process required to demonstrate the capacity you see in that man?\\n3. Name one “next step” you could take to risk recovering your strength as a generalist. \\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n_...act like men…\\n_1 Corinthians 16:13 ESV\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into. Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead. \\n\\n**TAKE ACTION THIS WEEK**\\n\\nRead chapter 5 of [Becoming a King.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpmvv)\\nComplete session 4 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpnkv)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://becomegoodsoil.com)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\nWatch the film The Company Men. Consider the story of Bobby Walker and the path and process of masculine initiation he had to go through to become a more wholehearted king. What do you relate to in this film? What is God saying to you through it, and who would you risk sharing this part of your story with? [Note: This movie has some inappropriate scenes, so use discretion.]\\n\\nListen to [Become Good Soil podcast 004: Hello Trouble.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/004-hello-trouble-podcast/)\\n\\nRead these Become Good Soil blog posts:\\n\\n- [Castration: A Case for Carrying a Knife](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2014/02/11/castration-a-case-for-carrying-a-knife/)\\n- [Stranded with Flip Flops – A Case for the Generalist](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2014/02/24/stranded-with-flip-flops-a-case-for-a-generalist/)\\n\\nWatch [Hello, Trouble](https://becomegoodsoil.com/helloTrouble/). Use your soul’s experience of this video to dig deeper into session four of the study guide.\\n\\nPray about receiving a knife from God to mark this milestone or bestowing a knife on another man. Check out the [Become Good Soil knife collection](https://becomegoodsoil.com/knife/) and read more in this Become Good Soil blog post – [A Man and a Knife Can Save the World.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2021/05/18/a-man-and-a-knife-can-save-the-world/)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vqb9tm\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 5- The Way of Becoming\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vqbgju\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** As soul-full beings, we are made to thrive in constant connection with the life of God and his Kingdom. The restoration of the masculine soul requires restoring a habitat where we can recover our strength and live out what we were meant to be as a man. Within this habitat, we arrange our days around practices that fuel our becoming. \\n\\n**Central Questions for this session:** Around what are you arranging your days? How do you cultivate a habitat, habits, and a life-giving relational model that bears the fruit of joy, resolve, and becoming the kind of person who never puts things that matter less in front of things that matter most?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note: \\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqcfbk\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417286138\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqcoyi\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you. \\n\\n**READ**\\nHow are you arranging your days? This is where the rubber meets the road. The masculine soul is designed to thrive in a particular habitat shaped by habits that are soul-strengthening. And all of this is intended to thrive in a particular relational model. Dallas Willard once said, “You must arrange your days so that you are experiencing deep contentment, joy, and confidence in your everyday life with God.“ How do we become good soil, become deeply rooted, and cultivate a like-hearted relational model that allows us to thrive in cultures that often stand as enemies to our masculine soul? Let’s dig in.\\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpwlq) pages 114-116)\\n\\n1. Describe the current habitat in which you live your daily life.  \\n2. Contrast this to the kind of habitat in which your masculine soul would most thrive. \\n3. Looking over the last week, what habits are most predictable in your life? Consider which of these are strengthening your process of becoming wholehearted and which are not serving your commitment to growth and maturation. \\n4. Draw a picture that represents your current relational model. Use your time, energy, and emotional resources as a way of measuring in whom you choose to invest yourself. Resist any value statements or temptations to edit; simply let your investment dictate what you draw. In whom and in what do you choose to invest your time, energy, and emotional resources?  \\n5. Now imagine traveling five years down the road: you have become a man who invests time, money, and emotional capacity in a way that is healthy and strong for your soul and in terms of stewardship of those people entrusted to your care. Draw a picture to represent this more wholehearted and mature relational model for your life. What do you observe in how these two pictures differ? What are some small action steps you can take toward the healthier model? \\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n_There is a way that seems right to a man, but its end is the way to death.\\n_Proverbs 16:25 ESV\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into.Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead. \\n\\nTAKE ACTION THIS WEEK\\n\\nRead chapters 7, 8, and 9 of [Becoming a King.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpxxz)\\nComplete session 5 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cpydw)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://www.BecomeGoodSoil.com)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\nWatch the short film [Godspeed: The Pace of Being Known.](https://www.livegodspeed.org/watchgodspeed) What does this film evoke in your heart? What is your current pace? Does it leave room for you and those under your care to be known? \\n\\nListen to:\\n\\n- [Become Good Soil podcast 064: Cultivating a Habitat for the Soul.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/064-cultivating-a-habitat-for-the-soul-podcast/)\\n- [Become Good Soil podcast 044: Intensive Session 5 of 8.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/044-intensive-series-episode-5-of-8-podcast/)\\n- [Become Good Soil podcast 066: Arranging Our Days](https://becomegoodsoil.com/podcast/066-arranging-our-days-an-intimate-conversation-from-the-2019-become-good-soil-intensive-podcast/)\\n- Read [Become Good Soil blog post – First Light – A Truly Happy Thanksgiving.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/2013/11/26/a-happy-thanksgiving/\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vqh6ph\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Session 6 - Becoming a King\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vqhfku\", \"body\": \"**About this session:** Though every generation faces unprecedented challenges, every generation also shares unprecedented opportunities to recover the path of life. As we respond to Jesus’ radical invitation to travel deeper together along the ancient path of becoming, we too can become the kind of kings who grow steadily in trust and confidence in the authority of Jesus.  \\n\\n**Central Question for this session:** Very few men ever really learn to love God with their whole heart. How do you become the kind of wholehearted man activated by love to whom God can gladly entrust the care of his Kingdom?\\n\\n**Initial welcome:** As the group first gathers, start your time with introductions if people don’t know each other. Begin with yourself (share your name, a bit about your family, and what inspired you to offer this group). Going first will put the group more at ease.\\n\\nAfter the introductions, jump right in to watching the video teaching, getting things started on a strong note: \\n\\n**WATCH**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqi4c2\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/417287965\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vqidgv\", \"body\": \"**PAUSE**\\n\\nOne of the foundational beliefs of this process is that God is the initiator and we are simply invited to respond and participate. In each session, you’re invited to choose a two-minute pause after the video to let the message soak into your soul, let questions arise, and let God shine his light. \\n\\n> God, I invite you into this space as I sit in stillness with you. Here and now, I choose to recover my breath. I turn my attention and affection to you, God, and what you have prepared for me in this time. I choose to gather my scattered senses and focus my attention on the presence of God. I choose two minutes to breathe and center myself with you. \\n\\n**READ**\\nHenry Varley once said, “The world has yet to see what God will do with and for and through and in and by the man who is fully consecrated to him.” Though every generation faces unprecedented challenges, every generation also experiences unprecedented opportunities\\nto recover the path to life. Jesus promises that our Good Father is winsomely at work. As we respond to his radical invitation to travel together on this ancient path of becoming, we too can become the kind of kings who so trust and rely on an interactive life that we astonish the heart of God.    \\n\\n**DISCUSSION QUESTIONS** ([study guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cq3bq) pages 180-181)\\n\\n1. Jesus says he does nothing apart from the Father. Where and how do you observe this dependency operating in his life? \\n2. By comparison, how much of your day-to-day life is lived in strength through dependency? If you were to describe your actual relationship to God, what words would you use to describe the quality, frequency, and level of relating? How much would you use the words authentic, vulnerable, and intimate in association with your life in God?\\n3. Who would you love to be in a decade? Describe that man.\\n\\n**SCRIPTURE**\\n_Jesus was astonished when he heard this and said to those who were following him, “He has greater faith than anyone I’ve encountered in Israel!”\\n_Matthew 8:10 TPT\\n\\n**THERE IS MORE.**\\n\\nThe Greatest revolution in humanity began with twelve men. You are among that great line of the heroic few. Who are the men God would have you invite deeper into the work in which you have engaged in this message? \\n\\nOver twenty years of walking with men my great personal transformation has consistently occurred when I risk offering to others. Would you be willing to share this message with other men? Would you be willing to facilitate a group through Becoming a King. Pause, pray, and ask God. Who are the men and what is the next step? Write their names down.\\n\\nHere are some particular next steps I recommend.\\n\\n- Dive into the resources at [BecomeGoodSoil.com](https://becomegoodsoil.com/). Start at the beginning and work slowly through this content in all its forms over time.\\n- Participate in a Wild at Heart Retreat or facilitate one in your area (WildAtHeartBASIC.com).\\n- If you’re married, provide a way for your wife to attend or facilitate a Captivating retreat event (CaptivatingCORE.com).\\n- Above all else, give God your next decade. It’s worth it. You are worth it. Make your apprenticeship in becoming a king in God’s kingdom the central mission of your days and your decade. You are among the few.\\n\\nSince we are God’s kings, may we set our masculine hearts on becoming a king. I look forward very much to being with you at the campfires of the kingdom, celebrating our shared courage and the truest story of all—that in the end, love wins.\\n\\n**CLOSING PRAYER**\\nProtect time each week to pray. Don’t rush. Linger. Invite God to tend to your masculine hearts in what has surfaced in your time together. Ask him what else he wants you all to pray into. Invite his power and care into each of your lives as you take action and dig deeper into your story through this content in the week ahead.\\n\\n**TAKE ACTION THIS WEEK**\\n\\nComplete session 6 from the [Becoming a King Study Guide.](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=91k8_cq5k6)\\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com.](https://becomegoodsoil.com/)\\n\\n**FURTHER EXCAVATION (FOR THOSE WHO WANT TO GO EVEN DEEPER)**\\nWatch the film Gladiator. Consider Maximus. What do you love about him? What parts of his story do you resonate with? To whose authority are you consenting?\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## BECOMING A KING EXPERIENCE \n\nI’m moved by your courage to risk facilitating a Becoming a King group. Over the past 20 years of leading men, I have experienced again and again how often the deepest transformation in my masculine soul happens when I risk facilitating an experience for others. This film series features content curated and distilled from decades of seeking the heart of God through older, wiser guides. Even more, it is a personal invitation from the heart of God to the slow and steady process of becoming the kind of men, the kind of kings, to whom God can gladly entrust his Kingdom. We\'re excited for you to take the men in your community on this journey. The rewards of leading are different from the rewards of participating, and we hope you find your own walk with Jesus deepened by this experience. This leader’s guide will give you tips on how to prepare for your time together and facilitate a meaningful experience for your group members.\n\n## WHAT DOES IT TAKE TO LEAD THIS STUDY?\n\nGet together and watch God show up. Seriously, that’s the basics of how a small group works. Gather several men together who have a deep thirst for apprenticeship to God and his Kingdom. The Lord will honor this every time and show up in the group. You don’t have to be a pastor, priest, theologian, or counselor to lead a group through this study. Just invite people over, watch the video, and talk about it. All you need is a willing heart and a little courage, and God will do the rest. Really.\n\n## HOW THIS STUDY WORKS\n\nAs the group leader, you will want to make sure everyone in your group has a copy of both the Becoming a King book and study guide. It works best if you can get the guides and books to your group before the first meeting. That way, everyone can read the material in the book ahead of time and be prepared to watch the first video session together. You can order the books directly by clicking here.\n\nThis series is presented in six video sessions, with each session being approximately 20 minutes in length. Be creative. The series is designed to be used in a wide variety of context. From a weekly small group of men, to a weekend retreat of any size. Make the necessary adjustments so that everyone has the opportunity to authentically engage. \n\nA detailed guide will be available in the resources section after registration.','## BEFORE YOUR EVENT \n\nThe real work of transformation begins as we engage this journey, not only participating with God in the process of becoming but also offering what we live. To lead a Becoming a King group is an even deeper dive into this transformation. Let\'s get started.\n\nAs you risk offering your strength by way of leading this group, make sure you have the necessary materials:\n\n- [Becoming a King (book)](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=51k8_hk5h4)\n- [Becoming a King Study Guide](https://churchsource.com/pages/becoming-a-king?sscid=51k8_hk5nx)\n\nSubscribe to [BecomeGoodSoil.com](https://becomegoodsoil.com/) to stay connected with new content and resources being made available to continue to strengthen you in this role.','[{\"id\": \"b0a66ab4\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## SCHEDULE \\n\\nA detailed schedule will be available in the resources section after registration.\\n\\n1. Session 1: Becoming Powerful\\n2. Session 2: Becoming a son\\n3. Becoming the Man You Were Born to Be\\n4. Session 4: Becoming a Generalist\\n5. Session 5: The Way of Becoming\\n6. Session 6: Becoming a King\"}]','[]','event_types/2dacd65f-7782-4ba8-a25d-ffba260fa8c5.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-bakexp.jpg',NULL,NULL,'[]','2024-02-01 06:19:58','2026-03-11 02:42:03','The Becoming A King Experience helps men understand their life story, face the wounds that shaped them, and grow into wholehearted men who lead with courage and humility.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vphmv0\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/fh3cr0boi9u6kfb/AADiMNz5FsADCl9W6iOPhHr8a?e=1&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'0c83d059-91cf-40c2-a286-0b016afb8e20');

INSERT INTO `event_types` (`id`, `allow_materials_order`, `number_of_items_in_material_order_label`, `group_type`, `type`, `name`, `filter_name`, `order`, `free_gift_image`, `zapier_webhook_url`, `card_teaser_text`, `tags`, `is_active`, `sex`, `slug`, `description`, `card_description`, `event_guide_pages`, `video_link`, `welcome_nav_text_override`, `before_event_nav_text_override`, `schedule_nav_text_override`, `faq_nav_text_override`, `registration_welcome_video`, `registration_welcome_text`, `registration_before_your_event_text`, `event_schedule`, `event_faqs`, `image`, `new_image`, `hero_image`, `hero_video`, `photos`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `summary`, `summary_link`, `key_details`, `action_buttons`, `new_content`, `related_landing_page_id`)
VALUES
	(9,1,'Expected number of attendees','retreat','retreat','Survival School',NULL,7,NULL,'https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/21az2sp/','Survival School is a four-day retreat training men to thrive as disciples of Jesus. John Eldredge and his team lead men into deeper union with God through story, spiritual practices, and integrative prayer.',NULL,1,'men','survival-school','## What is Survival School? \n\nSurvival School is an advanced-level retreat led by John Eldredge and his team through video sessions in your local area. \n\n\n## Welcome/Why do I need Survival School?\n\nSurvival School is for men who have attended or hosted a Wild at Heart Retreat and are ready for their next step into a radical discipleship journey. If Wild at Heart Retreat is the doorway into masculine initiation, Survival School is the manual for thriving as a man in this hour on the earth. \nThis event unapologetically invites men to experience the heart of reality: “Jesus Christ is the integrating force of all things.” The ten sessions of curated teaching, stories, guided reflections, and prayer time bring the heart of a man into deeper union with God.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m3enigcb\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enikx6\", \"body\": \"## Survival School\\n\\nThank you for your willingness to lead men through Survival School. This event features the teaching of John Eldredge and invites men into deeper union with God through story, spiritual practices, and integrative prayer. We are excited to bring more men into a radical discipleship journey. We pray that by leading, you also experience deeper union with God and a deeper experience of Jesus. This leader\'s guide will give you tips on how to prepare and how to facilitate a meaningful event for the men attending.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enis87\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Before Your Survival School\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3eniy7v\", \"body\": \"## Before Your Survival School\\n\\nAnyone can facilitate a Survival School who has a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with us by following the guidelines we’ve laid out. First, to attend or host this event, a man must have previously attended a WAH Retreat or Boot Camp.\\n\\nAs a facilitator, you agree to offer the full four-day Survival School experience, adhering to the details, not adding to or subtracting from any of the content. You also agree to provide feedback so we can continue to improve Survival School for future events.\\n\\n\\nAs part of registration, you will:\\n1. Choose your date – Survival School requires four days (usually Thursday afternoon through Sunday at noon).\\n2. Choose your men – Survival School is designed for a group of four to eight men but will work for any size.\\n3. Choose your location – This is a full-immersion experience. It’s your responsibility to create a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility removed from everyday life. \\n4. Invite your guys – We’ll provide full marketing content in the resources section after you register, including posters, flyers, video trailers, and email invite templates.\\n5. Get yourself ready – We recommend you read the Survival School manual before the event and watch all the downloadable content from the resources section so you’re familiar with the content.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enj79g\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Survival School Schedule\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enjdw8\", \"body\": \"## IMPORTANT NOTES: \\n\\n- All sessions will be taught by the WAH team via video. You will not add to or take away from the content / schedule.\\n- Men need to fully unplug. Provide an emergency contact number (that goes to you) and tell your participants to make one last call or e-mail to give that number to those who may need it. Then have them turn off all devices. The outside world will try to distract people. This will be one of the best decisions you make.\\n- Built into the Survival School schedule are “covenants of silence” so the men have dedicated time to hear from God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the sessions. These times of silence are the centerpiece of Survival School, and you will need to help preserve and protect them.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enjm7r\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"m3enjno5\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Sessions Overview\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enjyjq\", \"body\": \"Session One – Initiation\\n\\nSession Two – Orientation\\n\\nSession Three – Hearing God\\n\\nSession Four – Integration: Union with Jesus\\n\\nSession Five – Risk 201\\n\\nSession Six – Integration: Parts Work\\n\\nSession Seven – Warfare 301\\n\\nSession Eight – Becoming Sagely\\n\\nSession Nine – Dailies\\n\\nSession Ten – Final Thoughts\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enk3xq\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Survival School: Day 1\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enka79\", \"body\": \"1:00 p.m. Facilitators: Watch Day 1 Facilitator Briefing Video\\n(Note: If you and your fellow facilitators are comfortable and confident, this can be optional and you can instead go into consecration as God leads)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enkhho\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1028962541\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enkqr1\", \"body\": \"1:30 - 3:00 p.m. Facilitators: Watch Consecration Briefing & Consecrate Survival School\\n(Note: If you and your fellow facilitators are comfortable and confident, this can be optional and you can instead go into consecration as God leads)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enkwif\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1028962446\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enl441\", \"body\": \"4:00 - 5:00 p.m. Attendees arrive\\n\\n6:00 - 7:00 p.m. Dinner\\n\\n7:00 - 7:55 p.m. Session 1 - Initiation\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enl6zq\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/949738086\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enlbtt\", \"body\": \"7:55 p.m. - 8:15 p.m. Time with God (Mandatory Silence)\\n\\n8:15 p.m. Optional Fire/Free Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enlh8b\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Survival School: Day 2\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enljq2\", \"body\": \"7:30 a.m. Facilitators: Watch the Day 2 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enlnw2\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1028962687\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enlwva\", \"body\": \"8:15 - 9:00 a.m. Breakfast\\n\\n9:00 - 9:50 a.m. Session 2 - Orientation\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enm298\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/949752591\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enm3s0\", \"body\": \"9:50 - 10:15 a.m. Break\\n\\n10:15 - 11:15 a.m. Session 3 - Hearing God\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enmaqa\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/949776133\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enmcjl\", \"body\": \"11:15 - 12:00 p.m. Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point (a time for facilitators to check in with the other each other and to pray as a group for the guys, the coming sessions and whatever else God has in store for you)\\n \\n12:00 - 12:45 p.m. Lunch\\n              \\t\\n12:45 - 4:30 p.m. Free Time – Ask God what your heart needs (sleep, adventure, solitude, etc.)\\n \\n4:30 - 5:45 p.m. Session 4 – Integration: Union with Jesus\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enmlcr\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/949774960\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enmmy4\", \"body\": \"5:45 - 6:15 p.m. Reflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n                    \\t\\n6:15 - 7:15 p.m. Dinner\\n \\n7:15 - 8:05 p.m. Session 5 – Risk 201\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enmxl3\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/949969501\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enn30t\", \"body\": \"8:05 - 8:30 p.m. Reflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n8:30 p.m. Optional Fire/Free Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enn7nh\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Survival School: Day 3\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enn9ye\", \"body\": \"7:30 a.m. Facilitators: Watch the Day 3 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team\\nFacilitators: Pray the Daily Prayer\\n(Note: If you and your fellow facilitators are comfortable and confident, this can be optional and you can instead go into consecration as God leads)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3ennfs3\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1028962898\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3ennnyk\", \"body\": \"8:15 - 9:00 a.m. Breakfast\\n \\n9:00 - 9:55 a.m. Session 6 – Integration: Parts Work\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3ennsu3\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/953330791\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3ennuhv\", \"body\": \"9:55 - 10:25 a.m. Reflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n \\n10:25 - 10:30 a.m. Break\\n                          \\t\\n10:30 - 11:50 p.m. Session 7 - Warfare 301\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3eno3ej\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/953614996\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3eno50v\", \"body\": \"11:50 - 12:15 p.m. Reflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n \\n12:15 - 1:15 p.m. Lunch\\n \\n1:15 - 5:30 p.m. Free Time\\n(Note: Please protect the free time and allow men to get outside, to breathe, to rest, and get what they need.)\\n \\n5:30 - 6:30 p.m. Dinner\\n\\n6:30 - 7:25 p.m. Session 8 – Becoming Sagely\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enod9b\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1002947431\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enohkb\", \"body\": \"7:30 - 8:00 p.m. Reflection Time with God (Mandatory Silence) / Facilitator Touch Point\\n\\n8:00 p.m. Optional Fire/Free Time\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enoj8w\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Survival School: Day 4\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enorc5\", \"body\": \"7:00 a.m. Facilitators: Watch the Day 4 Briefing Video from Wild at Heart Team\\nFacilitators: Pray the Daily Prayer\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enowd8\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1028963102\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enoz5a\", \"body\": \"8:00 - 8:45 a.m. Breakfast\\n \\n8:45 - 10:05 a.m. Session 9 – Dailies\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enp53x\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/954110958\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enp9e3\", \"body\": \"10:05 - 11:00 a.m. Final Time with God  \\n \\n11:00 - 12:00 p.m. Session 10 – Final Thoughts\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enpcc6\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/956755486\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m3enpix8\", \"body\": \"12:00 p.m. Optional Lunch\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"m3enpnfn\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Facilitator Feedback\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m3enpt5u\", \"body\": \"We need your feedback. It helps us to offer ongoing strength, support, and development to you and your men. We ask that you follow through with that feedback upon completion of Survival School by completing this short survey:\\n[https://forms.gle/VDSTtm8orxmUaSPAA](https://forms.gle/VDSTtm8orxmUaSPAA)\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'## Survival School\n\nThank you for your willingness to lead men through Survival School. This event features the teaching of John Eldredge and invites men into deeper union with God through story, spiritual practices, and integrative prayer. We are excited to bring more men into a radical discipleship journey. We pray that by leading, you also experience deeper union with God and a deeper experience of Jesus. This leader\'s guide will give you tips on how to prepare and how to facilitate a meaningful event for the men attending.','## BEFORE YOUR RETREAT\n\nAnyone can facilitate a Survival School who has a heart to help men and a willingness to partner with us by following the guidelines we’ve laid out. First, to attend or host this event, a man must have previously attended a Wild at Heart Retreat or Boot Camp.\n\nAs a facilitator, you agree to offer the full four-day Survival School experience, adhering to the details, not adding to or subtracting from any of the content. You also agree to provide feedback so we can continue to improve Survival School for future events.\n\n\nAs part of registration, you will:\n1. Choose your date – Survival School requires four days (usually Thursday afternoon through Sunday at noon).\n2. Choose your men – Survival School is designed for a group of four to eight men but will work for any size.\n3. Choose your location – This is a full-immersion experience. It’s your responsibility to create a distraction-free and unplugged environment where men can encounter God. We recommend renting a cabin or finding a facility removed from everyday life. \n4. Invite your guys – We’ll provide full marketing content in the resources section after you register, including posters, flyers, video trailers, and email invite templates.\n5. Get yourself ready – We recommend you read the Survival School manual before the event and watch all the downloadable content from the resources section so you’re familiar with the content.','[{\"id\": \"m3enf4q8\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## SURVIVAL SCHOOL SCHEDULE \\n\\nIMPORTANT NOTES: \\n\\n1. All sessions will be taught by the WAH team via video. You will not add to or take away from the content / schedule.\\n2. Men need to fully unplug. Provide an emergency contact number (that goes to you) and tell your participants to make one last call or e-mail to give that number to those who may need it. Then have them turn off all devices. The outside world will try to distract people. This will be one of the best decisions you make.\\n3. Built into the Survival School schedule are “covenants of silence” so the men have dedicated time to hear from God, journal, and go deeper into the issues raised in the sessions. These times of silence are the centerpiece of Survival School, and you will need to help preserve and protect them.\\n\\nOverview of Survival School Sessions: \\n1. Session One – Initiation\\n2. Session Two – Orientation\\n3. Session Three – Hearing God\\n4. Session Four – Integration: Union with Jesus\\n5. Session Five – Risk 201\\n6. Session Six – Integration: Parts Work\\n7. Session Seven – Warfare 301\\n8. Session Eight – Becoming Sagely\\n9. Session Nine – Dailies\\n10. Session Ten – Final Thoughts\"}]','[{\"id\": \"m3enfbtw\", \"answer\": \"Because this isn\'t a typical retreat. Trust us on this one. You\'ll see why later.\", \"question\": \"Why doesn\'t the schedule include typical retreat elements?\"}, {\"id\": \"m3enh6av\", \"answer\": \"If you would like to publicly list your Survival School on our website for anyone to find and attend then yes, we require you to follow the schedule exactly. The reason we require you to follow the schedule is because we’re promoting the BASIC listings on our website to thousands of people each month and guaranteeing they’re all lead the exact same way. Also, through more than a decade we’ve learned this schedule works.\\n\\nThat being said, we’re certainly behind you if God is leading you to host on a different schedule. We will happily bless any schedule you choose including weekly for 11 weeks. If you’d like to host a Survival School and deviate from the Survival School schedule laid out in this Facilitator’s guide, make sure you register your Survival School and then choose the option to remove it from the website listings. This way you’ll still receive your note taking guides and all of the Survival School benefits.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to follow the 4-day schedule?\"}, {\"id\": \"m3enhe4v\", \"answer\": \"Choose simple, ready-made meals. Don’t require prep of the attendees. If prep and cleanup take more than 10 minutes, we recommend having a dedicated person not involved in the event to do it. Meal time—not the sessions—is also the chance to make any “housekeeping announcements.”\", \"question\": \"What about meals?\"}, {\"id\": \"m3enhljj\", \"answer\": \"You can, but we encourage you to find a partner or a small team to help. It’s always better not to fly solo when possible.\", \"question\": \"Can you facilitate this alone?\"}, {\"id\": \"m3enhsj2\", \"answer\": \"We don’t recommend doing so. We provide our content and notebooks to you at no charge. Our assumption is the only additional costs would be meals and perhaps a facility charge. Some facilitators choose to absorb these costs. Others charge a minimal fee to each attendee.\", \"question\": \"Should I charge men to attend?\"}]','square-logo-srvvl-(1).jpg','4k-horiz-logo-srvvl.jpg',NULL,'https://vimeo.com/1031235754/d6b9d6bdb8','[]','2024-11-13 05:18:52','2026-03-11 02:41:07','Survival School is a deeper training experience for men who want to learn how to walk with God in the midst of spiritual battle and the realities of everyday life.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m3eumagk\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/fnpzsverm4u83iijmeyke/AHh9YxJKBShP5MS4-BQfpHI?rlkey=2x2y5ourdevlrgj7jjlbxxufz&st=tmmpvbtw&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m5v73xej\", \"button_url\": \"https://shop.wildatheart.org/\", \"button_label\": \"Order Materials\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'e5062723-f9aa-47a4-80d2-36663d0359cc'),
	(10,0,'Expected number of attendees','fire','gathering','Captivating Fires',NULL,1,'capfires-gift-image-(1)-(1).jpg','https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/2zu67oz/','A Captivating Fire is a monthly gathering where women experience God\'s presence through guided conversation and connection with one another. \n\nAll around a fire.','easy, no requisite',1,'women','captivating-fires','Captivating Fires: Come Get Your Heart Back\n\n## Connect Deeply in a Trusted Circle\n\nJoin Fireside Gatherings of Trust and Friendship.\n\nExperience the unique Captivating Fires, where a small group of women unite monthly to share stories and insights within a safe and confidential space.\n\n## Share and Listen in Confidence\n\nAround the fire, discover a sanctuary for women to openly share deeper parts of their stories, knowing their experiences are met with understanding and respect.\n\n## Foster Genuine Bonds and Support\n\nBe part of a community that values honesty, support, and the power of shared experiences in a confidential setting.\n\n## Ignite Personal Growth and Connection\n\nCaptivating Fires offer a chance to explore life\'s deeper questions and build authentic friendships and a deeper spiritual connection.',NULL,'[]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'reg text','reg before','[]','[]','capt-square-logo-capfires.jpg','4k-horiz-logo-capfires.jpg',NULL,NULL,'[]','2024-11-20 09:10:47','2026-03-11 02:40:22','At Captivating Fires, women gather in a welcoming space to share life, encourage one another, and explore what it means to live from the strength and beauty of their true heart.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"k1hgZc7f\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M18 3a1 1 0 00-1.447-.894L8.763 6H5a3 3 0 000 6h.28l1.771 5.316A1 1 0 008 18h1a1 1 0 001-1v-4.382l6.553 3.276A1 1 0 0018 15V3z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M18 3a1 1 0 00-1.447-.894L8.763 6H5a3 3 0 000 6h.28l1.771 5.316A1 1 0 008 18h1a1 1 0 001-1v-4.382l6.553 3.276A1 1 0 0018 15V3z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Fires aren\'t religious\", \"description\": \"Leave your religious and professional credentials behind.\"}, \"headline\": \"Fires aren\'t a Bible study\", \"description\": \"They are about God taking center stage as women foster heartfelt connections through genuine, guided conversations.\"}, {\"id\": \"P1dowUK4\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Your story matters\", \"description\": \"Fires are not a place for teaching or a podium for experts.\"}, \"headline\": \"Connect deeply in a trusted circle\", \"description\": \"A Captivating Fires is where a small group of women come together monthly to experience God through each other’s stories and the beauty of community.\"}, {\"id\": \"2LdWweMu\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M13.477 14.89A6 6 0 015.11 6.524l8.367 8.368zm1.414-1.414L6.524 5.11a6 6 0 018.367 8.367zM18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 20\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path fill-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\" d=\\\"M13.477 14.89A6 6 0 015.11 6.524l8.367 8.368zm1.414-1.414L6.524 5.11a6 6 0 018.367 8.367zM18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0z\\\" clip-rule=\\\"evenodd\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"No bullshit allowed\", \"description\": \"Fires are a place for authentic masculinity. No posing.\"}, \"headline\": \"Share and listen\", \"description\": \"Around the fire, discover a sanctuary for women to openly share their stories, knowing their experiences are met with understanding and respect.\"}, {\"id\": \"2rHQ4lHp\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z\\\"></path>\\n</svg>\", \"type\": \"event-type-detail-item\", \"fields\": {\"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\">\\r\\n  <path stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" d=\\\"M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z\\\"/>\\r\\n</svg>\", \"headline\": \"Confidentiality is essential\", \"description\": \"What is shared at a Fire stays at the Fire.\"}, \"headline\": \"Foster heartfelt connection\", \"description\": \"These gatherings are designed to foster a Christ-centered space where women are free to let down, feel encouraged, and be restored through guided conversation and shared experiences.\"}, {\"id\": \"m4hlhz9y\", \"icon\": \"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" width=\\\"24\\\" height=\\\"24\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"currentColor\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\" stroke-linejoin=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"lucide lucide-person-standing\\\"><circle cx=\\\"12\\\" cy=\\\"5\\\" r=\\\"1\\\"/><path d=\\\"m9 20 3-6 3 6\\\"/><path d=\\\"m6 8 6 2 6-2\\\"/><path d=\\\"M12 10v4\\\"/></svg>\", \"headline\": \"Ignite personal growth and community\", \"description\": \"The spirit of the Fires is to learn, grow, and practice becoming a daughter of God. Captivating Fires offers a chance to explore life\'s deeper questions and build authentic friendships.\"}]','[{\"id\": \"m5ln3o7n\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/3oydzgctk1rd18yi1p0zo/CAP-Fires_Firestarter-Manual-v1.0-011225.pdf?rlkey=a9wg2y6jf8gqzlhzf17luye30&st=6upkzk28&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Firestarter Manual\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m5mrcvr7\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/xy0sp4nqnpgqwer4whjuc/ACStVeVjVrW01axqTFfqAk8?rlkey=hpe1d671o88aedblwh20ocr42&e=1&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Invite Cards\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0zae6ni\", \"button_url\": \"https://shop.wildatheart.org/discount/RCFH23RNRE8J\", \"button_label\": \"Order Materials\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'ba734eb4-337b-4bf2-90ae-b6bd696d8911'),
	(11,1,'Expected number of attendees','retreat','retreat','1-Day Captivating Retreat',NULL,3,NULL,'https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/340972/2m31jy1/','Captivating Retreat is a retreat led by Stasi Eldredge and her team through video session in your local area.',NULL,1,'women','1-day-captivating-retreat','Rooted in the message of _Captivating_ by Stasi and John Eldredge, this video-led experience is hosted by women around the world who are saying yes to offering beauty, rest, and healing to the women in their communities.\n\nFor over two decades, women have gathered in the Colorado mountains for the Captivating Retreat, hosted by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team, to meet with God and recover what has been lost. Now this life-changing retreat is available through local hosts to women everywhere. Whether you host or attend, you\'re invited to walk with God through a deeper journey of restoration, identity, and joy.\n\nGod sees your longing for more life, more hope, and more healing, and he is inviting you to go on a treasure hunt for his heart—and your own. “Come away with me, my beloved,” he says (Song of Songs 2:10). Through the powerful video sessions, music, intentional times with God, and beauty, you won’t just gain more information—you’ll encounter Jesus. \n\nThis is for you: an invitation to risk, awaken, and recover your heart. Come and experience the beauty, strength, and presence of God in a setting crafted just for you.',NULL,'[{\"id\": \"m0umzjpy\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Welcome\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0umzn09\", \"body\": \"Dear one, welcome to the 1-Day Captivating Retreat. Thank you for saying yes.\\n\\nYou’ve stepped into something beautiful and brave. It matters. Generations will be healed and changed for the good because of it. Remember, this is God’s invitation to you. He is inviting you to walk with him and to do it out of his strength. He will give you everything you need to create space for the women to encounter his love—and in a single day, he can do far more than we could ever imagine. In these few hours, hearts will awaken and lives will be restored.\\n\\nYou’re not doing this alone. We’ll walk you through the details to help give you all you need to create a sacred experience for the women you invite, so that they can encounter God and move towards the more that he has for them.\\n\\nTo begin, watch this personal message from Stasi about what to expect:\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vofq5v\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127241222/aea212218f\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"m0vog4s9\", \"body\": \"**What’s at the heart of the Captivating Retreat?**\\n\\nWritten on the heart of every woman are three core desires:\\n\\n- to be romanced\\n- to play an irreplaceable role in a grand adventure\\n- to unveil a beauty all her own\\n\\nThese longings aren’t shallow or unrealistic dreams. They are echoes of who God created us to be and the life we were meant to live. This is the heartbeat of the Captivating message.\\n\\nWe as women long to come alive again, and Jesus is inviting us into more—into a sacred space to encounter God and reclaim the truth of who we are as his beloved daughters.\\n\\nWhether you’re hosting a few close friends or a larger group, we thank you for joining this global movement of women creating space for healing, restoration, and deeper connection with God. You are stepping into the beautiful mission of his Isaiah 61 ministry; this is what Jesus came to do: heal the brokenhearted and restore what has been lost. And now he is inviting you to join him.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What Comes with Your Registration\\n\\nAs a registered Captivating Retreat facilitator, you now have free access to\\n- all video sessions led by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team\\n- a detailed retreat schedule\\n- note-taking guides mailed to the address you provided at registration\\n- a video from Stasi for facilitators on what to expect\\n- an online community of facilitators where you can ask and answer questions, encourage one another, and offer support \\n\\nWhether you’re hosting a public or private retreat, you’ll have everything you need to facilitate. You’ll find all the resources and next steps throughout this guide.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml5kgwb9\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Preparing the Way\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5khhgu\", \"body\": \"**This is about your presence, not performance.**\\n\\nYou don’t need to be a teacher, counselor, or expert host—just have a willing heart. God has invited you into something sacred: creating space for women to encounter him. That’s no small thing.\\n\\nAs a facilitator, you’re committing to lead with integrity, which means honoring the way this retreat has been prayerfully shaped over decades:\\n\\n- hosting the full 1-day experience as designed\\n- creating a distraction-free, sacred space\\n- letting the sessions unfold without adding or removing content\\n\\nYou’re part of something beautiful: God’s invitation to restore hearts and change lives.\\n\\nLet’s begin preparing the way.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Choose Your Dates \\n\\nThis Captivating Retreat is a 1-day experience, most commonly held from 8:30 AM through 5:30 PM. Please plan for the full time. This message builds session by session and isn’t to be rushed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Choose Your Location\\n\\nThis is a full-immersion experience. Wherever you host, your goal is to provide an unplugged, peaceful, distraction-free setting. It doesn’t have to be fancy, just set apart.\\n\\nSome suggestions:\\n\\n- You can host in a cabin, VRBO, retreat center, or a quiet room at your church—whatever space allows for peace, privacy, and room for the women to go out and meet with God uninterrupted during the covenants of silence. Make sure the Wi-Fi is reliable, and download the sessions ahead of time just to be safe.\\n- If you choose to host in your home, do what you can to minimize noise, interruptions, pets, kids, and daily demands.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Invite Your Participants  \\n\\nThis retreat was created for both small and large groups. What matters most is a safe, sacred space where hearts can open and God can move.\\n\\nWe’ve provided a Captivating Retreat logo for you in the download section. Because this retreat is a local expression of a global movement with an established identity, we ask that the logo be used as-is, without edits. You’re welcome to use it across any promotional materials you need as long as you honor its original design. Thank you for helping us steward the heart and visual integrity of Captivating.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Prepare Your Heart\\n\\nThis retreat is for you too. Before the logistics take over, pause to tend your own heart and invite God to speak about what he has for you in this. Here are a few ways to prepare:\\n\\n- **Use the Pause App daily**, or whenever needed, to center your heart and realign with God’s presence. [(Download the **Pause app**.)](https://www.pauseapp.com/)\\n- **Read the book _Captivating_ again.**\\n- **Consider purchasing the _Captivating_ book and _Guided Journal_** for your attendees so they can dig into the full Captivating message. [(ChurchSource is offering **50% off** orders of 20 or more with the code WAH20.)](https://churchsource.com/collections/wild-at-heart-captivating)\\n- **Watch all the video sessions ahead of time** so you’re familiar with the content. Make sure you download the most updated versions from the resources section.\\n\\t-\\tTech note: We recommend having 200 GB of free space to download and run all video files smoothly.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThank you, beloved. You are offering something sacred. Something bold.\\n\\nGod is with you; you are not in this alone.\\n\\nWe are covering you in prayer and cheering you on as you step into this holy mission.\\n\\nLet the preparation begin.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"m0vohj4b\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Guiding the Experience\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"m0vohut7\", \"body\": \"Every session of the Captivating Retreat is delivered by video from Stasi and the Captivating team. With everything provided, your role is to host—keeping the space sacred, staying on schedule, and guiding the flow of the experience.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Protect an unplugged environment**\\n\\nInvite the women to fully unplug for the day (let them know ahead of time that this will be encouraged). Provide an emergency contact number so their families can reach you if necessary. You may offer a secure box for all of the phones—encouraged but not required. For those who choose to keep their phones, ask that any use be done privately, as the sight of a phone can pull others out of the moment. Unplugging, even for a few hours, is a rare and powerful gift.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Guard the covenants of silence**\\n\\nBuilt into the schedule is dedicated time alone with God—quiet, personal space we call “covenants of silence.” This gives women time to be alone with God, journal, and go deeper with what the sessions have stirred. These times are often the most impactful part of the retreat. As the facilitator, your role is to encourage and protect this sacred space.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Worship is simple but sacred**\\n\\nEach session begins with one or two worship songs—an essential part of the flow that helps center the women’s hearts. The final session includes an extended time of worship.\\n\\n**Worship area setup**\\n\\nIf your venue allows, consider creating a dedicated worship space for the covenants of silence, a sanctuary for women to meet with God beyond the sessions for personal worship, prayer, or reflection.\\n\\n**Setup ideas (keep it simple):**\\n\\n- soft lighting (lamps, fairy lights, or flameless candles)\\n- cozy seating (pillows, blankets, or chairs)\\n- gentle instrumental worship or a soaking worship playlist on loop\\n- simple supplies (paper, pens, tissues, and Scripture cards)\\n- prayer board or basket for women to leave written prayers\\n- optional sign on the door: “Worship Room – Sacred Space for Silence and Prayer”\\n\\n**Optional touches:**\\n\\n- printed Scripture displayed around the room\\n- cross or focal point to draw hearts toward Jesus\\n- designated intercessor available to pray quietly if someone desires\\n\\nEncourage women to use the space as they feel led—to kneel, weep, journal, dance, or rest. There’s no right way; this is simply an invitational space to come close to the One who loves them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Food (lunch and snacks)**\\n\\nThe key is to keep it simple. Meals and snacks shouldn’t pull the women—or you—away from the retreat experience. If prep or cleanup takes more than 10 minutes, invite someone who isn’t attending to help behind the scenes.\\n\\nLunch: Arrange catering, organize a potluck during registration, or ask women to bring their own lunches. While going out could be an option, staying together helps protect the atmosphere and keeps hearts present. Here are some simple ideas:\\n\\n- catering (some venues offer this)\\n- takeout or delivery\\n- prepped sandwich or salad bars\\n- grocery platters or grab-and-go items\\n- potluck-style (ask each attendee to bring something)\\n\\n**Snacks:** There is a 15-minute break between Sessions 1 and 2 in the morning and between 3 and 4 in the afternoon, during which women may need a snack. You can ask them to bring their own, but if you wish to provide a snack as part of the retreat experience, here are some low-key options:\\n\\n- coffee, tea, hot chocolate, water—kept quietly stocked throughout the day\\n- cheese sticks, nuts, fruit, cookies, or other easy grab-and-go items\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Consecrate the space**\\n\\nWhen everything is in place, either the day before or before attendees arrive, take 30 to 60 minutes to consecrate the space, bringing it into God’s Kingdom and under his authority. Watch this video for instruction from Stasi on how to approach this:\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml00zymt\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/366859423\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml010hwu\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"Retreat Schedule\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml5kl6mc\", \"body\": \"The day holds a rhythm of teaching, worship, covenants of silence, and rest. Let the schedule guide you as you stay attentive to how the Spirit is moving in the women’s hearts.\", \"type\": \"body_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml010pwq\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"ml010qjf\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Overview\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml010umm\", \"body\": \"- 8:30 – 9:00 a.m. = Registration\\n- 9:00 – 9:10 a.m. = Facilitator announcements\\n- 9:10 – 10:20 a.m. = Session 1 – Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart, with Stasi Eldredge\\n- 10:20 –10:30 a.m. = Bathroom break and snack\\n- 10:30 – 11:40 a.m. = Session 2 – Fallen Eve, with Lisa Beck\\n- 11:40 a.m. – 12:10 p.m. = Covenant of silence\\n- 12:10 – 1:10 p.m. = Lunch\\n- 1:10 – 2:20 p.m. = Session 3 – Healing the Wound, with Stasi Eldredge\\n- 2:20 – 2:50 p.m. = Covenant of silence\\n- 2:50 – 3:00 p.m. = Bathroom break and snack\\n- 3:00 – 4:05 p.m. = Session 4 – The New Name, with Cherie Snyder\\n- 4:05 – 4:30 p.m. = Covenant of silence\\n- 4:30 – 5:20 p.m. = Session 5 – Closing and time of extended worship\\n- 5:20 – 5:30 p.m. = Facilitator close/dismiss\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\nThe detailed daily schedule follows in the drop-down menu of the section below, titled DETAILED SCHEDULE. Remember:\\n\\n- Stick closely to the provided schedule.\\n- There is no need to add or remove content, all session teachings are provided.\\n- Encourage reflection and rest.\\n- Keep the tone sacred, not pressured.\\n\\nYou are leading something holy.\\n\\nKeep walking closely with God.\\n\\nLet’s step into this glorious and holy day together and see what God will do!\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml0124mr\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Detailed Schedule\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml012dez\", \"body\": \"**8:30 – 9:00 a.m.\\nCheck-in and settling in**\\n\\n- Give the women an arrival time of 8:30 a.m. If you have a larger group, you may consider opening the doors earlier to allow for registration and welcome. \\n- Keep the atmosphere peaceful and light to help the women feel safe and welcomed from the moment they walk in. \\n- If you’d like, offer simple refreshments (coffee, tea, snacks) as they settle in and wait for the day to start.\\n\\n**9:00 – 9:10 a.m.\\nWelcome announcements**\\n\\n- Welcome the women.\\n- Share where the bathrooms are located.\\n- Any other “housekeeping” announcements you need to make\\n- Note: In Session 1, Stasi explains the covenants of silence and encourages the women to stay off their phones, so you don’t need to address that. However, it is good to encourage the women to stay off their phones as much as possible; this is a sacred space, and even seeing someone on a phone can pull another out of the moment.\\n\\n**9:10 – 10:20 a.m.\\nSession 1: Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart**\\n\\n- Play the video session.\\n- Close with a few announcements: \\n\\t-\\tThere will now be a 10-minute bathroom break; let them know what time to be back in their seats.\\n\\t-\\tWhere the coffee and tea/snacks are (if some are provided)\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml013xdq\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127416482/76993badff\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01ibzb\", \"body\": \"**10:20 – 10:30 a.m.\\nBathroom break and snack**\\n\\n**10:30 – 11:40 a.m.\\nSession 2: Fallen Eve**\\n\\n- Invite the women back in from break. Let them know that this session will end with their first 30-minute covenant of silence. Lunch will begin after that time, so share any instructions then, depending on how lunch is being handled.\\n- Start the session, which begins with a worship song.\\n- At the end of the session and video, a still image of a whale appears. At this point, “I Am Set Free” begins playing to start the first mandatory covenant of silence.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01j049\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127762201/b4aaf3c431\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01jcol\", \"body\": \"**11:40 a.m. – 12:10 p.m.\\nCovenant of silence (mandatory silence)**\\n\\n[**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God.\\n\\n**12:10 – 1:10 p.m.\\nLunch** \\n\\n- Arrange catering, organize a potluck during registration, or ask women to bring their own lunch. \\n- While going out could be an option, staying together is encouraged to protect the atmosphere and keep hearts present.\\n\\n**1:10 – 2:20 p.m.\\nSession 3: Healing the Wound**\\nPlay the video session, which begins with a worship song.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01kkbe\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127241319/42c3b94d60\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01kqvi\", \"body\": \"**2:20 – 2:50 p.m.\\nCovenant of silence** (mandatory silence)\\n\\n[**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) helps hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God.\\n\\n**2:50 – 3:00 p.m.\\nBathroom break and snack** (flows in from the covenant of silence)\\n\\n**3:00 – 4:05 p.m.\\nSession 4: The New Name**\\n\\nPlay the video session, which begins with a worship song.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01lvoj\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127761848/8e0e946f49\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01m2dp\", \"body\": \"**4:05 – 4:30 p.m.\\nCovenant of silence** (mandatory silence)\\n\\n[**This playlist**](https://open.spotify.com/playlist/3Dmolc0c7fA2S2bADgXEcq?si=8f2624b04ef64edc&nd=1&dlsi=23211e65ed6949a0) can help hold the reflective space for anyone who wants to remain in the room with God.\\n\\n**4:30 – 5:20 p.m.\\nSession 5: Closing and time of extended worship**\\n\\nPlay the video session, which leads directly into a time of extended worship.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01myo7\", \"type\": \"video_set\", \"video\": \"https://vimeo.com/1127416394/bc240f1efd\", \"enabled\": true}, {\"id\": \"ml01noz3\", \"body\": \"**5:20 – 5:30 p.m.\\nFacilitator close and dismissal of attendees**\\n\\n---\\n\\nYou did it. Thank you!\\n\\nYou offered your yes, and God moved in beautiful, holy, and extraordinary ways.\\n  \\nWell done, beloved. May his favor rest on you, and may the ripples of this retreat extend far beyond what you can see this side of heaven.\\n\\nWe encourage you to stay in the [**Daily Prayer**](https://wildatheart.org/pray), especially over the next week. Consecrate your mind daily, so that it is only the voice of God that lets you know the glory of this retreat. \\n\\nBless you, dear one. May God now fill you to overflowing, restoring everything you just poured out for others to know him more deeply and have their hearts and stories healed and restored. \\n\\nWith joy and gratitude,\\n**The Captivating team**\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01obu4\", \"type\": \"page\", \"enabled\": true, \"page_title\": \"FAQ\", \"page_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01ofpx\", \"type\": \"accordion_set\", \"enabled\": true, \"accordion\": [{\"id\": \"ml01ogu7\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Can I facilitate this alone?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01okqi\", \"body\": \"You can, but if you\'re considering having more than just a few women, we encourage you to find a co-facilitator or team. It’s wonderful to be able to share the experience, carry the load, and cover each other in prayer. Should you choose a co-leader or team, we encourage you to prayerfully consider who and make sure you\'re aligned in heart and vision.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01ooys\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Do I need to follow the provided schedule?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01otlh\", \"body\": \"We ask that you follow the schedule exactly as provided for this 1-day retreat, including using the provided videos for the session teachings. This ensures that every woman attending a Captivating Retreat—wherever she is in the world—receives the same powerful experience, session by session. Plus, the retreat is specifically designed to fit into one day.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01owsr\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How soon should I start planning?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01p0xu\", \"body\": \"Ideally, begin six to eight weeks before your retreat to allow time for invitations, location, and preparation. But if God stirs sooner, trust him with the timing—he will make a way.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01p5fg\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What about meals?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01pdyt\", \"body\": \"The key is to keep it simple. Mealtime shouldn’t pull women—or you—away from the retreat experience. If prep or cleanup takes more than 10 minutes, we suggest assigning someone who is not attending the retreat to help.\\n\\nHere are a few easy options:\\n\\n- catering (some venues offer this)\\n- takeout or delivery\\n- prepped sandwich or salad bars\\n- grocery platters or grab-and-go items\\n- potluck-style (ask each attendee to bring something)\\n\\nThe goal is simplicity and ease, not perfection.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01pu1y\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"Should I charge women to attend?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01pxm7\", \"body\": \"The content and materials are provided at no cost, so the only expenses would be food or a rented venue. You may choose to cover those costs yourself or split them among attendees with a small fee. Either is fine—just be transparent up front so women know what to expect.\\n\\nWild at Heart Ministries is not able to provide scholarships for independently hosted retreats. If a woman expresses financial need and that’s not something your event can support, you might encourage her to explore support through her local church, such as women’s ministry or benevolence funds, as a possible avenue for help.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01q5qd\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How do I access the video sessions?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01qa8d\", \"body\": \"Go to the Dropbox folder with all the video sessions. (You don’t need a Dropbox account to access them.) We suggest you download the videos ahead of time, because Wi-Fi at retreat sites can be unreliable.\\n\\nYou\'ll need\\n\\n- a computer with adequate storage (We recommend 200 GB of free space to download and run all video files smoothly.)\\n- a TV or projector (connected via HDMI or compatible cable) that allows everyone to see and hear the sessions clearly\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01qr05\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"How do I create a safe space when facilitating a Captivating Retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01qzg8\", \"body\": \"Sacred space isn’t built through logistics alone—it’s created by the posture of our hearts. These are the things that matter most:\\n\\n- **Confidentiality is everything.** What’s shared at the retreat stays there—no exceptions unless someone gives express permission. This protects every heart.\\n- **Don’t offer advice, offer an ear.** Resist the urge to give counsel. This is a place for the women to hear from God, so leave room for him to speak and move.\\n- **Cover it all in prayer** before, during, and after the retreat. We also encourage you to invite intercessors to come alongside you, people you trust to pray for you and your group throughout the retreat.\\n- **Persevere.** You are doing Kingdom work, and hearts will be set free. There will be opposition, but don’t lose heart. Stay in prayer and allow God to lead; he will give you everything you need.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01rqgg\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What if someone needs emotional support during the retreat?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01rsu3\", \"body\": \"Sometimes the content stirs deep emotion. Be prepared with tissues and a kind presence. You’re not expected to counsel—simply listen and guide each woman back to Jesus, our Healer. \\n\\nRemember, your role isn’t to be responsible for another’s healing—Jesus will come for her. Still, if you’d like to learn more about walking with others, this [**Four Streams Clinic**](https://wildatheart.org/media/four-streams-clinic) from John Eldredge offers a thoughtful perspective and helpful tools.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}, {\"id\": \"ml01s9ft\", \"accordion_box_title\": \"What if something goes wrong—technical issues, illness, weather?\", \"accordion_box_content\": [{\"id\": \"ml01sgqs\", \"body\": \"Don’t panic. Pray, walk with God, and adapt as needed. Trust that God is still leading and is in this. Every Captivating Retreat unfolds uniquely, and he’ll meet you right where you are, just as you need him to.\", \"type\": \"text_set\", \"enabled\": true}]}]}]}]',NULL,'Invitation','About','Schedule','FAQs',NULL,'## INVITATION\n\n\nThe invitation of the Gospel is to live fully alive and in union with God. To come home to who you truly are—restored by his love, alive in his presence, walking in joy and courage, and offering the strength and beauty that flow from your radiant heart as a woman.\n\nThis goes far beyond duty or pressure. It’s the epic story of God\'s pursuit, awakening something deep and eternal inside you, because there is something fierce and life-giving there. Something essential to God’s heart and to his mission to come and rescue what has been lost.\n\nSo…what if this is God’s invitation to you?\n\nWhat if God is stirring something in your heart and asking you to explore this with him—to pray, listen, and follow his lead as you consider creating a space for women to encounter his love and remember who they truly are?\n\nYou don’t have to have all the answers or any special experience.\n\nBut if your heart is stirring, if something inside you whispers _maybe_, then we invite you to walk with God and explore what it might look like to host a Captivating Retreat.\n\n- It will be holy.\n- It will be tender.\n- It will be beautiful.\n- It will require something of you.\n\nAnd Jesus will meet you every step of the way.\n\n---\n\n**A Woman’s Deepest Longings**\n\nWritten on the heart of every woman are these longings:\n\n- to unveil a beauty all her own\n- to play an irreplaceable role in a grand adventure\n- to be romanced\n\nThese longings aren’t shallow or unrealistic dreams. They are echoes of who God created you to be. \n\nA woman must know she is seen. That she is delighted in. That she is chosen, cherished, and called into a story far bigger than herself.\n\nAnd as her heart awakens, she begins to see, honor, and want to call up the beauty in others. Our journey is not just about discovering who we are; it’s about learning to love and stand with one another with grace, strength, and compassion.\n\nThis is why we offer the Captivating Retreat—a journey into the welcoming heart of God to uncover the deep, restored places of our feminine souls.','## ABOUT THE RETREAT\n\n### What Is the Captivating Retreat?\n\nThe **Captivating Retreat** is a **video-led experience** hosted by women like you around the world—in homes, cabins, or retreat centers—in partnership with Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team.\n\nYou offer the invitation, and we’ll provide the resources designed to carry the weight for you:\n\n- video sessions led by Stasi and the Captivating team\n- the full retreat schedule (a step-by-step guide)\n- a video from Stasi for facilitators on what to expect\n- access to a private online facilitator community of women hosting worldwide\n\n\nWhen you register your retreat, you’ll gain full access to these resources. You’ll also choose whether your retreat is\n\n- private (by invitation only), or\n- public (listed on our site so others may register to join)\n\n---\n\n### A Note on Expectations \n\nIf you feel God stirring your heart to host a retreat, we’ll walk you through all the details once you register. For now, here’s a brief summary of what’s involved:\n\n**Commit to the full experience** \n\n- The 1-day retreat runs from 8:30 AM–5:30 PM.\n- Please plan for the full time. This message unfolds intentionally, each session building upon the last.\n\n**Lead by hosting**\n\n- The content is fully provided to you, for free, through video sessions. \n- You don’t need to teach, just provide a space, follow the guide, and allow God to move.\n\n**Create a distraction-free environment**\n\n- Whether you’re at a cabin, VRBO, or your living room, the space should invite peace so women can step away for this set-apart time and meet with God uninterrupted.\n\n**Invite women into this sacred experience**\n\n- Groups can be large or small. What matters most is a safe, sacred space where hearts can open and God can move.\n\n**Let God meet you too**\n\n- Let your heart be open to what God has for you in this. Remember, this is an invitation to do this with him. \n\n---\n\n### The Larger Story—and Your Beautiful Role\n\nOver the past two decades, Captivating Retreats led by Stasi and the Wild at Heart women’s team have guided more than **20,000 women** from around the world. These are not events. They are sacred encounters with God, and women leave forever changed, because something deep within is awakened and restored.\n\nEvery woman carries wounds as well as lies that say she’s too much, not enough, or somehow not quite right. But that is not the story God is telling. He is rewriting our stories with truth and inviting us to partner with him in that—not as an afterthought, but as a vital ally in his mission to heal and restore the hearts of others.\n\nAs Catherine of Siena wrote, “Become who you are meant to be, and you will set the world on fire.”\n\nDo you feel God asking you to take a chance on him? To bring this message to your community, to create space for women to encounter God, receive his love, and recover their true hearts?\n\nIf so…let’s begin.','[{\"id\": \"22186d0d\", \"type\": \"text\", \"enabled\": true, \"text_block\": \"## RETREAT SCHEDULE \\n\\n## What is a summary of the schedule?\\n\\nAfter registering, you’ll receive a detailed, step-by-step schedule to guide you through each session. But here’s a quick overview so you can get a sense of the flow:\\n\\n**1-Day Retreat**\\n\\nThis format offers a beautifully condensed version of the Captivating message:\\n \\n - Session 1 – Core Desires of a Woman’s Heart\\n - Session 2 – Fallen Eve\\n - Session 3 – Healing the Wound\\n - Session 4 – Your New Name\\n - Session 5 – Closing Session\\n\\nEach session builds upon the last, so we encourage you to follow the provided schedule, which allows God to gently shepherd each woman through her journey.\"}]','[{\"id\": \"lzjwybsy\", \"answer\": \"Not at all. You don’t need to be a speaker, teacher, or counselor. You just need to love Jesus, have a desire to encourage women, and say yes to creating a space for God to move. If he’s inviting you, trust that he will equip you.\", \"question\": \"Do I need to be “qualified” to lead?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjwysjq\", \"answer\": \"You can, but if you plan to invite more than a few women, we encourage you to find a co-facilitator or team. This is a big commitment, and it’s wonderful to be able to share the experience, carry the load, and cover each other in prayer. Should you choose a co-leader or team, we encourage you to prayerfully consider who and make sure you\'re aligned in heart and vision.\", \"question\": \"Can I facilitate this alone?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjwzmx6\", \"answer\": \"Both formats offer powerful teaching, worship, and space to meet with God. Both invite women to step away from their worlds so they can receive his love and walk with him into the \\\"more\\\" he has for them, in order to recapture their whole hearts.\\n\\n- The 4-day retreat is the full 4-day Captivating Retreat filmed in the mountains in Colorado. It is the retreat that Wild at Heart has been offering for over two decades.\\n- The 1-day retreat is a condensed, beautifully crafted introduction to Captivating—perfect for women who are new to the message or whose season of life doesn’t allow for a multi-day retreat.\\n\\nYou’ll be able to choose which retreat when you register. We’ll then give you access to the sessions, worship lists, schedules, and other detailed information for whichever you choose, all for free.\", \"question\": \"What’s the difference between the 1-day and 4-day retreat?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx1ejj\", \"answer\": \"The key is to keep it simple. Mealtime shouldn’t pull women—or you—away from the retreat experience. If prep or cleanup takes more than 10 minutes, ask someone not attending to help.\\n\\nHere are a few easy options:\\n\\n- catering (some venues offer this)\\n- takeout or delivery\\n- prepped sandwich or salad bars\\n- grocery platters or grab-and-go items\\n- potluck-style (ask each attendee to bring something)\\n\\nThe goal is simplicity and ease, not perfection.\", \"question\": \"What about meals?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx23fo\", \"answer\": \"We are so happy to provide the video content and downloadable materials at no cost to you, so the only expenses should be meals and your venue (if you’re renting a space). Some hosts choose to absorb these costs. Others split them among attendees with a small registration fee.\\n\\nEither way is fine. Just be transparent upfront so your attendees know what to expect.\", \"question\": \"Should I charge women to attend?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx34hy\", \"answer\": \"After you register, you’ll receive access to a Dropbox folder with all the video sessions. (You don’t need a Dropbox account.) We suggest you download videos ahead of time, because Wi-Fi at retreat sites can be unreliable.\\n\\nYou\'ll need\\n\\n- a computer with adequate storage (We recommend 200 GB of free space to download and run all video files smoothly.)\\n- a TV or projector (connected via HDMI or compatible cable) that allows everyone to see and hear the sessions clearly\", \"question\": \"How do I access the video sessions?\"}, {\"id\": \"lzjx3j3u\", \"answer\": \"Sacred space isn’t built through logistics alone—it’s created by the posture of our hearts. These are the things that matter most:\\n\\n- Confidentiality is everything. What’s shared at the retreat stays there—no exceptions unless someone gives express permission. This protects every heart.\\n- Don’t offer advice, offer an ear. Resist the urge to give counsel. This is a place for the women to hear from God, so leave room for him to speak and move.\\n- Cover it all in prayer before, during, and after the retreat. We also encourage you to invite intercessors to come alongside you, people you trust to pray for you and your group throughout the retreat.\\n- Persevere. You are doing Kingdom work, and hearts will be set free. There will be opposition. Don’t lose heart. Stay in prayer and allow God to lead. He will give you everything you need.\", \"question\": \"How do I create a safe space when facilitating a Captivating Retreat?\"}]','square-logo-1d-cap-rt-(1).jpg','square-logo-1d-cap-rt-(1).jpg',NULL,'https://vimeo.com/1012088113/dd6e0407ea','[]','2026-01-30 09:31:34','2026-04-09 10:36:51','Sint ullam ut dignissimos quos suscipit.',NULL,'[]','[{\"id\": \"m0vpfy8n\", \"button_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/v9a0ugwqz1m9hprfkwrqm/AD-rxlpAMWOB18eYshzPWrU?rlkey=utcgn163skz4uo0o1go6ob3he&e=1&dl=0\", \"button_label\": \"Downloads\", \"open_in_new_tab\": true}]',NULL,'f42e74d0-d4d4-44d9-a6d3-a8cd9b9208b0');

